INSERT INTO _s463 VALUES
(4255,'T',48,2,48,2,$n$*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.* (1 Enoch 48:2). *And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name Yahusha (JESUS): for he shall save his people from their sins* (Matthew 1:21). The name given at the manger had already been named before the Head of Days. Enoch saw the Son of Adam named in the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits before there was a Bethlehem to be born in; the angel's instruction to Yoseph (Joseph) is that name arriving on earth. The one who saves his people is the one who was named before his people existed.$n$,$n$And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.$n$,true),
(4257,'T',48,6,48,6,$n$*And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.* (1 Enoch 48:6). *They shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, Elohim (God) with us* (Matthew 1:23). Chosen and hidden before the creation of the world — then revealed in flesh. The Formed one, drawn from the Father before anything was made, is the one Matthew calls *Elohim (God) with us.* He was not new at the manger; he was hidden, and the hiding ended.$n$,$n$And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.$n$,true),
(4390,'T',46,1,46,1,$n$*And there I saw One who had a head of days, And His head was white like wool, And with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man, And his face was full of graciousness, like one of the holy angels.* (1 Enoch 46:1). *The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air have nests; but the Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20). This is where the title comes from. Enoch saw the Head of Days, white-haired, and beside him one with the face of a man and the graciousness of a holy angel, and asked who he was. When Yahusha (Jesus) calls himself the Son of Adam, he is naming himself as the one who stood beside the Head of Days — and that one now has no bed on the earth he came to.$n$,$n$And there I saw One who had a head of days, And His head was white like wool, And with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man, And his face was full of graciousness, like one of the holy angels.$n$,true),
(4392,'T',46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *The Son of Adam hath not where to lay his head* (Matthew 8:20). The angel answered Enoch's question by title and by role: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, who reveals what is hidden, whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits has chosen, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. That is the figure Yahusha (Jesus) names himself as. The pre-eminent one before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits is the homeless one on the road to Capernaum, and both are the same Son of Adam.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$,true),
(4409,'T',48,2,48,2,$n$*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.* (1 Enoch 48:2). *The Son of Adam hath power on earth to forgive sins* (Matthew 9:6). The scribes called it blasphemy because only Yahuah (God) forgives. Enoch had already seen this Son of Adam named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, before the Head of Days — named, not made. The power exercised over a palsied man in Capernaum is the standing of the one who was named before creation, now exercised in flesh. The scribes were right about who forgives; they were wrong about who stood in front of them.$n$,$n$And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.$n$,true),
(4455,'T',99,5,99,5,$n$*And in those days the destitute shall go forth and carry off their children, And they shall abandon them, so that their children shall perish through them: Yea, they shall abandon their children (that are still) sucklings, and not return to them, And shall have no pity on their beloved ones.* (1 Enoch 99:5). *I am come to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her mother* (Matthew 10:35). Enoch saw the household come apart in the day of destruction — parents carrying off and abandoning their own children, no pity for their beloved. The King says the same division will run through the household when his voice is heard, because some in the house will hear and some will not. The line does not stop at the front door.$n$,$n$And in those days the destitute shall go forth and carry off their children, And they shall abandon them, so that their children shall perish through them: Yea, they shall abandon their children (that are still) sucklings, and not return to them, And shall have no pity on their beloved ones.$n$,true),
(4456,'T',100,1,100,1,$n$*And in those days in one place the fathers together with their sons shall be smitten And brothers one with another shall fall in death Till the streams flow with their blood. For a man shall not withhold his hand from slaying his sons and his sons’ sons, And the sinner shall not withhold his hand from his honoured brother: From dawn till sunset they shall slay one another.* (1 Enoch 100:1–2). *And a man's foes shall be they of his own household* (Matthew 10:36). The King is quoting Micah: *a man's enemies are the men of his own house* (Micah 7:6). Enoch saw it in blood — fathers and sons smitten in one place, brother falling on brother from dawn till sunset. The seed war of Genesis 3:15 runs inside families, not only between nations; two brunettes can bear a son of Belial, and Eli's own sons were sons of Belial. Hearing the Shepherd's voice divides a house because not everyone in the house is a sheep.$n$,$n$And in those days in one place the fathers together with their sons shall be smitten And brothers one with another shall fall in death Till the streams flow with their blood.$n$,true),
(4481,'T',46,1,46,1,$n$*And there I saw One who had a head of days, And His head was white like wool, And with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man, And his face was full of graciousness, like one of the holy angels.* (1 Enoch 46:1). *No man knoweth the Son, but the Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son* (Matthew 11:27). Enoch saw the two together before the incarnation: One with a head of days, and with him another whose face was like a man's and full of grace. The Father and the Son, side by side, in a vision written centuries before Matthew. What the King says in prayer — that the Father and the Son know each other as no one else does — Enoch saw as a picture: the two of them, together, and no third.$n$,$n$And there I saw One who had a head of days, And His head was white like wool, And with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man, And his face was full of graciousness, like one of the holy angels.$n$,true),
(4482,'T',46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *Neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son will reveal him* (Matthew 11:27). The angel told Enoch what the Son of Adam does: he *revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden,* because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits chose him. The Father is the hidden treasure; the Son is the one who reveals him, and he reveals him to whom he will. Enoch is told this by title; the King says it in the first person.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$,true),
(4483,'T',48,6,48,6,$n$*And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.* (1 Enoch 48:6). *No man knoweth the Son, but the Father* (Matthew 11:27). Chosen and hidden before him, before the creation of the world — the Son was known to the Father before anyone else existed to know him. That is why no one knows the Son but the Father: the knowing began before the world did. The disciples would come to know him later; the Father's knowing has no beginning.$n$,$n$And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.$n$,true),
(4484,'T',48,7,48,7,$n$*And the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous; For he hath preserved the lot of the righteous, Because they have hated and despised this world of unrighteousness, And have hated all its works and ways in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: For in his name they are saved, And according to his good pleasure hath it been in regard to their life.* (1 Enoch 48:7). *Thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes* (Matthew 11:25). Enoch says who the revealing is for: the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits reveals him *to the holy and righteous,* the ones who have hated this world of unrighteousness and all its ways. Not the credentialed, not the wise in their own eyes — the ones whose lot he preserved. The babes of Matthew 11:25 are the holy and righteous of 1 Enoch 48:7. The revealing does not make them his; it finds them already his.$n$,$n$And the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous; For he hath preserved the lot of the righteous, Because they have hated and despised this world of unrighteousness, And have hated all its works and ways in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: For in his name they are saved, And according to his good pleasure hath it been in regard to their life.$n$,true),
(4502,'T',49,1,49,1,$n$*For wisdom is poured out like water, And glory faileth not before him for evermore. For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, And unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, And have no continuance; Because the Elect One standeth before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his glory is for ever and ever, And his might unto all generations.* (1 Enoch 49:1–2). *Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him* (Matthew 12:18). Matthew is quoting Isaiah 42:1 over the Galilean ministry. Enoch saw the same anointing from the other side of the veil: wisdom poured out on the Elect One like water, glory that does not fail, might in all the secrets of righteousness. The Spirit the Father put upon his servant at the river is the wisdom Enoch saw poured out on the one who stands before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,$n$For wisdom is poured out like water, And glory faileth not before him for evermore.$n$,true),
(4503,'T',49,3,49,3,$n$*And in him dwells the spirit of wisdom, And the spirit which gives insight, And the spirit of understanding and of might, And the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in righteousness.* (1 Enoch 49:3). *I will put my spirit upon him* (Matthew 12:18). Isaiah named what that Spirit is: *the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 11:2). Enoch names the same spirits dwelling in the Elect One — wisdom, insight, understanding and might — and adds one Isaiah did not: *the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in righteousness.* The anointed one carries the righteous dead with him. Three witnesses, one Spirit, one anointed.$n$,$n$And in him dwells the spirit of wisdom, And the spirit which gives insight, And the spirit of understanding and of might, And the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in righteousness.$n$,true),
(4508,'T',10,4,10,4,$n$*And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein. And place upon him rough and jagged rocks, and cover him with darkness, and let him abide there for ever, and cover his face that he may not see light.* (1 Enoch 10:4–5). *How can one enter into a strong man's house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man?* (Matthew 12:29). Binding is how Yahuah (God) deals with the strong man. Raphael was sent to bind Azazel hand and foot, cast him into darkness, cover him with rocks, and leave him there until the judgment. When Yahusha (Jesus) cast out devils and said the strong man had to be bound first, he was describing something that had been done before and would be done again — the binding of the serpent for the length of the reign (Revelation 20:2). The exorcisms were the spoiling; the binding is older than Galilee.$n$,$n$And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein.$n$,true),
(4509,'T',54,5,54,5,$n$*And he said unto me: ‘These are being prepared for the hosts of Azâzêl, so that they may take them and cast them into the abyss of complete condemnation, and they shall cover their jaws with rough stones as Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits commanded.* (1 Enoch 54:5). *Except he first bind the strong man* (Matthew 12:29). Enoch asked what the chains were for and was told: for the hosts of Azazel, to cast them into the abyss of complete condemnation with their jaws covered in stones. The chains were already forged when the King spoke of binding. The spoiling of the strong man's house in Galilee is the beginning of what those chains were made for.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘These are being prepared for the hosts of Azâzêl, so that they may take them and cast them into the abyss of complete condemnation, and they shall cover their jaws with rough stones as Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits commanded.$n$,true),
(4518,'T',51,1,51,1,$n$*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* (1 Enoch 51:1). *So shall the Son of Adam be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth* (Matthew 12:40). The heart of the earth gives back. Enoch saw the earth return what was entrusted to it, Sheol give back what it received, hell give back what it owes. The sign of Jonah is a man going into the deep and being given back; the Son of Adam went into the heart of the earth knowing the earth would have to return him, because the earth returns what it holds.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$,true),
(4535,'T',6,1,6,1,$n$*And it came to pass when the children of men had multiplied that in those days were born unto them beautiful and comely daughters. And the angels, the children of the heaven, saw and lusted after them, and said to one another: ‘Come, let us choose us wives from among the children of men and beget us children.’* (1 Enoch 6:1–2). *But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat* (Matthew 13:25). Here is the sowing. In the days of Jared the children of heaven looked on the daughters of men and took wives, and a seed entered the field that was not of Adam. The enemy sowed while men slept; Enoch tells you who the enemy was and what he sowed. The parable is not a figure of speech. It is the history of Genesis 6 told as a field.$n$,$n$And it came to pass when the children of men had multiplied that in those days were born unto them beautiful and comely daughters.$n$,true),
(4537,'T',15,8,15,8,$n$*And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling. Evil spirits have proceeded from their bodies; because they are born from men and from the holy Watchers is their beginning and primal origin; they shall be evil spirits on earth, and evil spirits shall they be called.* (1 Enoch 15:8–9). *The tares are the children of the wicked one* (Matthew 13:38). The children of the wicked one have a father and a beginning. Enoch names it: the giants born of spirits and flesh became evil spirits on the earth when their bodies died, and evil spirits they are called. The tares are not bad wheat; they are another seed with another origin, and the spirits of that seed are still at work in the field. The parable names them; 1 Enoch names where they came from.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$,true),
(4542,'T',104,2,104,2,$n$*Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.* (1 Enoch 104:2). *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father* (Matthew 13:43). Enoch says it to the righteous directly: you were put to shame, and now you shall shine as the lights of heaven, you shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you. Daniel says the same (Daniel 12:3). The shining is not a reward for effort; it is what happens to the righteous when the shame is lifted at the harvest.$n$,$n$Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.$n$,true),
(4544,'T',48,6,48,6,$n$*And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.* (1 Enoch 48:6). *I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world* (Matthew 13:35). The one speaking in parables was himself the secret kept from the foundation of the world — chosen and hidden before the creation, and for evermore. When he opens his mouth in parables he is the hidden one revealing hidden things. The secret and the one who tells it are the same.$n$,$n$And for this reason hath he been chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world and for evermore.$n$,true),
(4554,'T',100,5,100,5,$n$*And over all the righteous and holy He will appoint guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye, Until He makes an end of all wickedness and all sin, And though the righteous sleep a long sleep, they have nought to fear.* (1 Enoch 100:5). *The angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just* (Matthew 13:49). The angels who sever at the end are the angels who guard until the end. Enoch saw holy angels set over the righteous as guardians, keeping them as the apple of an eye until all wickedness is done away, so that the righteous sleep without fear. The same hands that guard the just through the age are the hands that separate the wicked from them at the harvest.$n$,$n$And over all the righteous and holy He will appoint guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye, Until He makes an end of all wickedness and all sin, And though the righteous sleep a long sleep, they have nought to fear.$n$,true),
(4599,'T',48,2,48,2,$n$*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.* (1 Enoch 48:2). *Thou art the Messiah (Christ), the Son of the living Elohim (God)* (Matthew 16:16). Kefa (Peter) names him on earth. Enoch saw him named in heaven — the Son of Adam named in the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, before the Head of Days. The confession at Caesarea Philippi did not give him the name; it recognized a name that was given before the world was made.$n$,$n$And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.$n$,true),
(4600,'T',48,3,48,3,$n$*Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 48:3). *Flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven* (Matthew 16:17). What the Father revealed to Kefa (Peter) was old: *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made, his name was named.* The revealing did not create a truth; it uncovered one older than the stars. That is why Yahusha (Jesus) credits the Father and not Kefa — the Father is the one who named him in the first place.$n$,$n$Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,true),
(4613,'T',51,1,51,1,$n$*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* (1 Enoch 51:1). *The gates of hell shall not prevail against it* (Matthew 16:18). The gates of Sheol cannot hold because Sheol has to give back. Enoch saw the earth return what was entrusted to it, Sheol give back what it received, and hell give back what it owes. The assembly built on the rock is built on a resurrection; the gates that could not hold him cannot hold his own.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$,true),
(4678,'T',10,8,10,8,$n$*And the whole earth has been corrupted through the works that were taught by Azâzêl: to him ascribe all sin.’* (1 Enoch 10:8). *Woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come* (Matthew 18:7). Why must they come? Because the whole earth was corrupted through what Azazel taught, and the corruption is still running. Enoch says *to him ascribe all sin.* Offences are inevitable in a corrupted world — and that inevitability excuses no one, which is why the King's woe lands on the man by whom the offence comes. The earth is defiled under its inhabitants, as Isaiah said (Isaiah 24:5–6), and every man who adds to the defiling answers for his part.$n$,$n$And the whole earth has been corrupted through the works that were taught by Azâzêl: to him ascribe all sin.’$n$,true),
(4679,'T',19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *But woe to that man by whom the offence cometh!* (Matthew 18:7). Uriel showed Enoch the angels who joined themselves to women, and said their spirits, taking many forms, *lead them astray* — into sacrificing to demons as gods. Leading astray is the offence. Every system that teaches the little ones to walk contrary to the Father's commandments is doing what those spirits do, in whatever form the age gives it. The little ones led astray are victims; the woe is for the ones doing the leading.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$,true),
(4681,'T',27,2,27,2,$n$*Then Uriel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered and said: ‘This accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever: Here shall all the accursed be gathered together who utter with their lips against Yahuah (Lord) unseemly words and of His glory speak hard things. Here shall they be gathered together, and here shall be their place of judgement.* (1 Enoch 27:2). *It is better for thee to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire* (Matthew 18:9). The hell fire the King names is Gehenna — the valley on the south side of Jerusalem. Enoch was shown that valley before the city had a name for it: *this accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever,* where those who speak hard things against Yahuah (Lord) are gathered for judgment. The place of judgment is a real place, and it is the place where the judgment is carried out; that is why a man cuts off what makes him stumble.$n$,$n$Then Uriel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered and said: ‘This accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever: Here shall all the accursed be gathered together who utter with their lips against Yahuah (Lord) unseemly words and of His glory speak hard things. Here shall they be gathered together, and here shall be their place of judgement.$n$,true),
(4684,'T',90,6,90,6,$n$*But behold lambs were borne by those white sheep, and they began to open their eyes and to see, and to cry to the sheep.* (1 Enoch 90:6). *It is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish* (Matthew 18:14). Enoch saw lambs born to the white sheep begin to open their eyes and see, and cry to the sheep. The Father's will for the little ones is that they open their eyes. The ones who open them are the ones who could — the lambs who were sheep's lambs. The Father does not lose what is his; what is his hears when he calls.$n$,$n$But behold lambs were borne by those white sheep, and they began to open their eyes and to see, and to cry to the sheep.$n$,true),
(4714,'T',98,10,98,10,$n$*And now, know ye that ye are prepared for the day of destruction: wherefore do not hope to live, ye sinners, but ye shall depart and die; for ye know no ransom; for ye are prepared for the day of the great judgement, for the day of tribulation and great shame for your spirits.* (1 Enoch 98:10). *Who then can be saved?* (Matthew 19:25). The disciples asked it because the rich had always looked blessed. Enoch had already answered: *ye know no ransom.* Riches are no ransom on the day of the great judgment; the sinner who trusted them departs and dies. If the thing everyone counted as blessing cannot save, then no one can be saved by what he has — which is the point the King makes in the next verse: with men impossible, with Elohim (God) possible.$n$,$n$And now, know ye that ye are prepared for the day of destruction: wherefore do not hope to live, ye sinners, but ye shall depart and die; for ye know no ransom; for ye are prepared for the day of the great judgement, for the day of tribulation and great shame for your spirits.$n$,true),
(4727,'T',48,1,48,1,$n$*And in that place I saw the fountain of righteousness Which was inexhaustible: And around it were many fountains of wisdom: And all the thirsty drank of them, And were filled with wisdom, And their dwellings were with the righteous and holy and elect.* (1 Enoch 48:1). *For many be called, but few chosen* (Matthew 20:16). Enoch saw the fountain: inexhaustible righteousness, many fountains of wisdom around it, and *all the thirsty drank.* The call goes out wide because the thirsty are scattered and no one knows them by sight. But the verse ends with where the drinkers lived — *with the righteous and holy and elect.* Many drink; the ones whose dwelling was already with the elect are the few. The call reveals who was chosen; it does not make the choice.$n$,$n$And in that place I saw the fountain of righteousness Which was inexhaustible: And around it were many fountains of wisdom: And all the thirsty drank of them, And were filled with wisdom, And their dwellings were with the righteous and holy and elect.$n$,true),
(4734,'T',46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *The Son of Adam came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The one who gives his life is the one Enoch was told about by title: the Son of Adam who has righteousness, chosen by Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, whose lot has the pre-eminence for ever. The title is not a humble word for *human.* It is the name of the pre-eminent one, and the pre-eminent one came to serve.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$,true),
(4735,'T',48,2,48,2,$n$*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.* (1 Enoch 48:2). *To give his life a ransom for many* (Matthew 20:28). The ransom was not an accident of history. The Son of Adam who gave it was named before the Head of Days, before the sun and the stars; John calls him *the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world* (Revelation 13:8). He walked into the ransom knowing it, because it was settled before there was a world to ransom.$n$,$n$And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.$n$,true),
(4780,'T',46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *What think ye of Messiah (Christ)? whose son is he? They say unto him, The Son of David* (Matthew 22:42). Right as far as it goes. The Messiah is David's son by the promise to David. But Enoch was shown a Son of Adam whose lot has the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits *for ever* — before David, before Adam's line reached David at all. The Pharisees had the half the Tanakh gave them. The other half was in a book the scribes did not read from.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$,true),
(4781,'T',48,2,48,2,$n$*And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.* (1 Enoch 48:2). *How then doth David in spirit call him Adonai (Lord)?* (Matthew 22:43). David calls his own descendant *my Lord* because the descendant is older than the ancestor. Enoch saw the Son of Adam named before the Head of Days — before David's line existed, before any line existed. The Pharisees could not answer the question because they did not have this verse. David, in the Spirit, did.$n$,$n$And at that hour that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And his name before the Head of Days.$n$,true),
(4791,'T',99,2,99,2,$n$*Woe to them who pervert the words of uprightness, And transgress the eternal law, And transform themselves into what they were not [into sinners]: They shall be trodden under foot upon the earth.* (1 Enoch 99:2). *Ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves* (Matthew 23:15). Enoch's woe is the same woe: on those who pervert the words of uprightness, transgress the eternal law, and *transform themselves into what they were not.* The proselyte is transformed into something — and what he is transformed into is a sinner wearing Torah's name, because the ones who made him teach contrary to the Torah they claim. *He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar* (1 John 2:4). The test is old.$n$,$n$Woe to them who pervert the words of uprightness, And transgress the eternal law, And transform themselves into what they were not [into sinners]: They shall be trodden under foot upon the earth.$n$,true),
(4806,'T',10,2,10,2,$n$*’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.* (1 Enoch 10:2). *But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:37). Enoch tells you what the days of Noah were. A messenger was sent to Noah in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name: hide yourself, the end is approaching, a deluge is coming on the whole earth. The earth was corrupted by the Watchers' works, the judgment was announced to one man, and the flood came on the rest. The coming of the Son of Adam is that pattern again: a corrupted earth, a warning carried by the few, and a day the many do not see coming.$n$,$n$’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.$n$,true),
(4811,'T',57,1,57,1,$n$*And it came to pass after this that I saw another host of wagons, and men riding thereon, and coming on the winds from the east, and from the west to the south.* (1 Enoch 57:1). *For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be* (Matthew 24:27). Nothing secret about it. Enoch saw hosts on wagons coming on the winds from the east and from the west — a coming that fills the sky from one side to the other. The King gives the same picture: lightning, east to west, seen by everyone. Whatever the pulpit sells as a quiet disappearance, the coming of the Son of Adam is a sky-wide event.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that I saw another host of wagons, and men riding thereon, and coming on the winds from the east, and from the west to the south.$n$,true),
(4812,'T',57,2,57,2,$n$*And the noise of their wagons was heard, and when this turmoil took place the holy ones from heaven remarked it, and the pillars of the earth were moved from their place, and the sound thereof was heard from the one end of heaven to the other, in one day.* (1 Enoch 57:2). *And they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other* (Matthew 24:31). *From one end of heaven to the other* is Enoch's phrase before it is Matthew's: when the wagons came, the sound was heard *from the one end of heaven to the other, in one day.* The gathering of the elect is loud and whole-sky — the twelve tribes brought back from wherever they were driven (Deuteronomy 30:4; Ezekiel 37:21), with a sound that moves the pillars of the earth.$n$,$n$And the noise of their wagons was heard, and when this turmoil took place the holy ones from heaven remarked it, and the pillars of the earth were moved from their place, and the sound thereof was heard from the one end of heaven to the other, in one day.$n$,true),
(4813,'T',61,5,61,5,$n$*And these measures shall reveal all the secrets of the depths of the earth, And those who have been destroyed by the desert, And those who have been devoured by the beasts, And those who have been devoured by the fish of the sea, That they may return and stay themselves On the day of the Elect One; For none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And none can be destroyed.* (1 Enoch 61:5). *They shall gather together his elect from the four winds* (Matthew 24:31). The gathering reaches the ones no one could find. Enoch saw the measures reveal the secrets of the depths of the earth — those destroyed in the desert, devoured by beasts, devoured by the fish of the sea — *that they may return,* on the day of the Elect One, *for none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The seed scattered into the sea and the wilderness is not lost to him. The four winds give back what they took.$n$,$n$And these measures shall reveal all the secrets of the depths of the earth, And those who have been destroyed by the desert, And those who have been devoured by the beasts, And those who have been devoured by the fish of the sea, That they may return and stay themselves On the day of the Elect One; For none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And none can be destroyed.$n$,true),
(4851,'T',46,4,46,4,$n$*And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.* (1 Enoch 46:4). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven* (Matthew 26:64). He said it to the men who were about to sentence him. Enoch saw what that Son of Adam does to men in seats of power: he raises the kings and the mighty from their seats and breaks the teeth of the sinners. The council that judged him will be raised from its seats by him. The verdict on the night was the Sanhedrin's; the verdict that stands is his.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$,true),
(4852,'T',48,3,48,3,$n$*Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 48:3). *Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam* (Matthew 26:64). Bound before the council, he names himself with the name Enoch heard named before the sun and the stars were made. The high priest called it blasphemy. But the Sanhedrin did not name the Son; the Father did, before the creation of the world — and the Father's naming is the one that stands when the council's has been forgotten.$n$,$n$Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,true),
(4898,'T',51,1,51,1,$n$*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* (1 Enoch 51:1). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). He says it as the firstfruits of the resurrection, three days after the earth was handed what it could not keep. Enoch saw the day the earth gives back what was entrusted to it and Sheol gives back what it received. The one who walked out of the tomb is the proof that Sheol gives back; the power he announces is the power of the one the earth could not hold.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.$n$,true),
(4899,'T',51,2,51,2,$n$*And he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them: For the day has drawn nigh that they should be saved.* (1 Enoch 51:2). *All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth* (Matthew 28:18). Power to do what? Enoch says: *he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them.* The gathering is wide and the choosing comes after it — the wheat gathered out of all nations and then sifted, chaff from kernel, goats from sheep (Ezekiel 20:37–38; Matthew 25:32). The one who does the sifting is the one to whom all power was given. The tares were never wheat; the sifting is of the wheat, and he does it himself.$n$,$n$And he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them: For the day has drawn nigh that they should be saved.$n$,true),
(7878,'T',46,3,46,3,$n$*And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* (1 Enoch 46:3). *I am: and ye shall see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power* (Mark 14:62). Enoch was told the Son of Adam's lot has *the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The right hand of power is that pre-eminence. Asked by the council who he was, the King answered with the title the angel gave Enoch — and claimed the seat that goes with it.$n$,$n$And he answered and said unto me: This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness, With whom dwelleth righteousness, And who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden, Because Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath chosen him, And whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.$n$,true),
(7917,'T',10,4,10,4,$n$*And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein.* (1 Enoch 10:4). *When a stronger than he shall come upon him, and overcome him, he taketh from him all his armour wherein he trusted, and divideth his spoils* (Luke 11:22). The strong man has been overcome before. Raphael was sent to bind Azazel hand and foot and cast him into darkness. The stronger one who divides the spoils in Luke is doing in Galilee what Yahuah (God) commanded in the days of Jared, and will do again when the serpent is bound for the length of the reign (Revelation 20:2).$n$,$n$And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein.$n$,true),
(7943,'T',10,3,10,3,$n$*And now instruct him that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.’* (1 Enoch 10:3). *Until the day that Noe entered into the ark, and the flood came, and destroyed them all* (Luke 17:27). Two outcomes, no third. Enoch records the instruction: Noah is to escape, and his seed is to be preserved for all the generations of the world — while everything else is destroyed. The days of the Son of Adam end the same way: the seed preserved, the rest swept away. The ark is not a metaphor for safety; it is the line between the two.$n$,$n$And now instruct him that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.’$n$,true),
(7944,'T',10,2,10,2,$n$*’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.* (1 Enoch 10:2). *And as it was in the days of Noe, so shall it be also in the days of the Son of Adam* (Luke 17:26). Enoch tells what the days of Noah were: a warning carried to one man in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name — hide yourself, the end is approaching — over an earth corrupted by the Watchers. The flood came on a corrupted earth after a warning most did not hear. The days of the Son of Adam come on an earth corrupted the same way, after a warning carried the same way.$n$,$n$’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.$n$,true),
(7993,'T',48,3,48,3,$n$*Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 48:3). *Before Abraham was, I am* (John 8:58). Enoch places the name earlier still: *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made, his name was named.* The Yahudim (Jews) picked up stones because they understood him — he was claiming to be older than Avraham (Abraham). He was older than the stars. The Formed one speaks his own name in the first person; Enoch heard it named in the third.$n$,$n$Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,true),
(15033,'T',18,12,18,12,$n$*And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.* (1 Enoch 18:12). *I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit* (Revelation 9:1). Enoch was shown the pit before John was: beyond the abyss, a place with no firmament above and no founded earth beneath, no water, no birds — a waste and horrible place. That is the bottomless pit. The fallen star is handed the key to a place Enoch had already walked to the edge of.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$,true),
(25558,'T',48,3,48,3,$n$*Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* (1 Enoch 48:3). *Their names shall be blotted out of the book of life* (1 Enoch 108:3). Names can be blotted out because they were written first — and Enoch tells when: the Son's own name was named *before the sun and the signs were created, before the stars of the heaven were made.* The roll was written before the world. Chapter 108 takes names off it; nothing in Enoch, or in the canon, ever adds one.$n$,$n$Yea, before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,true),
(25627,'T',6,6,6,6,$n$*And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.* (1 Enoch 6:6). *In his days the angels of Yahuah (God) descended on the earth, those who are named the Watchers* (Jubilees 4:15). Jubilees dates the descent to Jared's days; 1 Enoch dates it the same way and adds the place and the number — two hundred, on the summit of Hermon, bound by an oath. Two books, one generation, one mountain.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$,true),
(25629,'T',13,8,13,8,$n$*And behold a dream came to me, and visions fell down upon me, and I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven, and reprimand them.* (1 Enoch 13:8). *There he writes down the condemnation and judgment of the world* (Jubilees 4:23). The commission Jubilees describes, 1 Enoch shows from the inside: the dream, the visions of chastisement, and the voice telling Enoch to carry it to the sons of heaven and reprimand them. Jubilees says he became the scribe of judgment; 1 Enoch is the judgment he wrote.$n$,$n$And behold a dream came to me, and visions fell down upon me, and I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven, and reprimand them.$n$,true),
(25648,'T',7,3,7,3,$n$*Who consumed all the acquisitions of men. And when men could no longer sustain them, the giants turned against them and devoured mankind.* (1 Enoch 7:3–4). *They began to devour each other* (Jubilees 5:2). Jubilees says all flesh began to devour each other; 1 Enoch says who started it. The giants consumed everything men had, and when men could no longer feed them, the giants turned on mankind and ate them. The devouring of Jubilees 5:2 has a face.$n$,$n$Who consumed all the acquisitions of men.$n$,true),
(25653,'T',10,3,10,3,$n$*And now instruct him that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.’* (1 Enoch 10:3). *But Noah found grace before the eyes of Yahuah (God)* (Jubilees 5:5). What the grace did, 1 Enoch records as an order given to an angel: instruct him so that he escapes and his seed is preserved for every generation of the world. Grace found Noah; the instruction is what grace looked like.$n$,$n$And now instruct him that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.’$n$,true),
(25656,'T',10,9,10,9,$n$*And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.* (1 Enoch 10:9). *He sent His sword into their midst that each should slay his neighbour* (Jubilees 5:9). The sword has a name in 1 Enoch: Gabriel, sent against the children of the Watchers to *send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle.* Jubilees reports the slaughter; 1 Enoch reports the command that caused it.$n$,$n$And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.$n$,true),
(25900,'T',10,6,10,6,$n$*And on the day of the great judgement he shall be cast into the fire.* (1 Enoch 10:6). *Till the day of judgment, on which Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) shall judge them with a sword and with fire* (Jubilees 9:15). The day the sons of Noah bound themselves to by oath is the day the bound Watchers are waiting for. 1 Enoch names it the same way — *the day of the great judgement,* and the fire. One day, two books, the same reckoning.$n$,$n$And on the day of the great judgement he shall be cast into the fire.$n$,true),
(25928,'T',15,8,15,8,$n$*And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.* (1 Enoch 15:8). *The unclean demons began to lead astray the children of the sons of Noah* (Jubilees 10:1). Jubilees calls them unclean demons; 1 Enoch tells you what they are. The giants born of spirits and flesh became evil spirits on the earth when their bodies died, and the earth is their dwelling. The demons troubling Noah's grandsons are the dead giants of the Watchers.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$,true),
(25953,'T',19,1,19,1,$n$*And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.* (1 Enoch 19:1). *All the signs of the stars, and the signs of the moon and of the sun are all in the hand of Yahuah (God). Why do I search (them) out?* (Jubilees 12:17). Abram turns from the stars and, in the next verses, prays to be delivered from the evil spirits that rule men's hearts. Uriel showed Enoch those spirits: the Watchers' spirits in many forms, *lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods.* Star-reading was one of the arts they taught. Abram walked away from the art and asked to be kept from its teachers.$n$,$n$And Uriel said to me: ‘Here shall stand the angels who have connected themselves with women, and their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray into sacrificing to demons as gods, (here shall they stand,) till the day of the great judgement in which they shall be judged till they are made an end of.$n$,true),
(26002,'T',99,7,99,7,$n$*And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.* (1 Enoch 99:7). *Over all has He placed spirits in authority to lead them astray from Him* (Jubilees 15:31). The spirits set over the nations are the spirits behind the idols. 1 Enoch names the worship — stones, images of gold and silver and wood and clay, impure spirits and demons — and the result: *no manner of help from them.* The nations were handed to spirits; Yashar'el (Israel) was kept for Yahuah (God) himself. The idols are not empty; they have tenants.$n$,$n$And they who worship stones, and grave images of gold and silver and wood and stone and clay, and those who worship impure spirits and demons, and all kinds of idols not according to knowledge, shall get no manner of help from them.$n$,true),
(26034,'T',10,13,10,13,$n$*In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.* (1 Enoch 10:13). *It was commanded and engraven concerning all his seed, on the heavenly tables, to remove them and root them out* (Jubilees 16:9). The judgment of Sodom was written before it fell. 1 Enoch shows the same pattern for the Watchers: their end was fixed — led off to the abyss of fire, to the torment and the prison, for ever. The sentence is written before the day; the day only executes it.$n$,$n$In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.$n$,true),
(29171,'T',10,2,10,2,$n$*’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.* (1 Enoch 10:2). *The end of all flesh is come before me, on account of their evil deeds, and behold I will destroy the earth* (Jasher 5:25). Jasher gives the word to Noah; 1 Enoch gives the messenger. An angel was sent in Yahuah's (the Lord's) name to tell Noah to hide himself, that the end was approaching and a deluge would destroy everything on the earth. Two books carry the same warning to the same man.$n$,$n$’Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!” and reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed, and a deluge is about to come upon the whole earth, and will destroy all that is on it.$n$,true),
(60445,'T',10,4,10,4,$n$*And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein.* (1 Enoch 10:4). *Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment* (2 Peter 2:4). Kefa (Peter) is summarizing something written out in full elsewhere. 1 Enoch gives the order to Raphael: bind Azazel hand and foot, cast him into the darkness, cover him with rough rocks until the judgment. The chains of darkness are these chains; the reserving unto judgment is this reserving. Jude 6 and 1 Peter 3:19 are reading the same book.$n$,$n$And again Yahuah (Lord) said to Raphael: ‘Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dûdâêl, and cast him therein.$n$,true),
(141653,'T',15,3,15,3,$n$*Wherefore have ye left the high, holy, and eternal heaven, and lain with women, and defiled yourselves with the daughters of men and taken to yourselves wives, and done like the children of earth, and begotten giants (as your) sons?* (1 Enoch 15:3). *His angels he charged with folly* (Job 4:18). What folly? 1 Enoch names it, in the charge spoken to the Watchers' faces: you left the high, holy, eternal heaven, lay with women, defiled yourselves with the daughters of men, and begot giants. Eliphaz knew that angels had been charged with something. Enoch records the charge.$n$,$n$Wherefore have ye left the high, holy, and eternal heaven, and lain with women, and defiled yourselves with the daughters of men and taken to yourselves wives, and done like the children of earth, and begotten giants (as your) sons?$n$,true),
(21342,'S',8,4,10,12,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* The Watchers' binding in the abyss until the judgment is Isaiah's host shut in the pit until they are visited.$n$,$n$And when their sons have slain one another, and they have seen the destruction of their beloved ones, bind them fast for seventy generations in the valleys of the earth, till the day of their judgement and of their consummation, till the judgement that is for ever and ever is consummated.$n$,false),
(16297,'S',13,10,13,7,$n$Jubilees 5:10 — *And their fathers were witnesses (of their destruction), and after this they were bound in the depths of the earth for ever, until the day of the great condemnation when judgment is executed on all those who have corrupted their ways and their works before Yahuah (God).* Why the petition Enoch read at the waters of Dan till he fell asleep (13:7) fails — the Watcher-fathers are bound, not forgiven.$n$,$n$And I went off and sat down at the waters of Dan, in the land of Dan, to the south of the west of Hermon: I read their petition till I fell asleep.$n$,false),
(16326,'S',14,16,14,19,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The fiery stream that issued from before the Ancient of days is the stream Enoch saw: from underneath the throne came streams of flaming fire, so that he could not look on it (14:19).$n$,$n$And from underneath the throne came streams of flaming fire so that I could not look thereon.$n$,false),
(16327,'S',14,16,14,18,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The throne like the fiery flame with wheels as burning fire is the lofty throne Enoch saw — its appearance as crystal, its wheels as the shining sun, and the cherubim about it (14:18).$n$,$n$And I looked and saw therein a lofty throne: its appearance was as crystal, and the wheels thereof as the shining sun, and there was the vision of cherubim.$n$,false),
(16352,'S',16,2,15,4,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude reads the Watchers' crossing of the heaven-flesh boundary in Enoch 15:4 as angels abandoning their first estate, reserved for judgment.$n$,$n$And though ye were holy, spiritual, living the eternal life, you have defiled yourselves with the blood of women, and have begotten (children) with the blood of flesh, and, as the children of men, have lusted after flesh and blood as those also do who die and perish.$n$,false),
(16353,'S',16,2,15,4,$n$Genesis 6:4 — *There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of Elohim (God) came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown.* The defilement Enoch names in 15:4 is the very union that produced the giants of Genesis 6.$n$,$n$And though ye were holy, spiritual, living the eternal life, you have defiled yourselves with the blood of women, and have begotten (children) with the blood of flesh, and, as the children of men, have lusted after flesh and blood as those also do who die and perish.$n$,false),
(16354,'S',16,2,15,4,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* The Watchers' "union" with women in Enoch 15:4 is Moses' sons-of-Elohim taking wives of the daughters of men.$n$,$n$And though ye were holy, spiritual, living the eternal life, you have defiled yourselves with the blood of women, and have begotten (children) with the blood of flesh, and, as the children of men, have lusted after flesh and blood as those also do who die and perish.$n$,false),
(16675,'S',17,8,18,1,$n$Psalms 104:2 — *Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:* The wisdom by which He ordered all creation and founded the world (1 Enoch 18:1) is the psalm's God who stretches out the heavens.$n$,$n$I saw the treasuries of all the winds: I saw how He had furnished with them the whole creation and the firm foundations of the earth.$n$,false),
(16743,'S',22,12,22,5,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* The martyrs' cry for vengeance is Enoch's suit of the dead going forth to heaven (Enoch 22:5), still awaiting the appointed reckoning.$n$,$n$I saw the spirits of the children of men who were dead, and their voice went forth to heaven and made suit.$n$,false),
(16744,'S',22,12,22,7,$n$Hebrews 12:24 — *And to Yahusha (Jesus) the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.* Hebrews knows Abel's blood still speaks. Enoch heard it: the spirit that went forth from Abel, making his suit against his brother's seed (22:7). The blood of sprinkling answers that suit with a better word.$n$,$n$And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’$n$,false),
(17149,'S',26,4,30,3,$n$Ezekiel 47:12 — *And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.* Ezekiel sees trees lining both sides of the sanctuary-stream — Enoch saw fragrant cinnamon on the sides of the valleys of the holy mountain (30:3).$n$,$n$And on the sides of those valleys I saw fragrant cinnamon. And beyond these I proceeded to the east.$n$,false),
(17200,'S',30,1,30,3,$n$Exodus 30:23 — *Take thou also unto thee principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred shekels, and of sweet cinnamon half so much, even two hundred and fifty shekels, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty shekels,* Enoch found cinnamon on the sides of the valleys (30:3) — one of the principal spices Yahuah (LORD) set apart for the holy anointing oil.$n$,$n$And on the sides of those valleys I saw fragrant cinnamon. And beyond these I proceeded to the east.$n$,false),
(17201,'S',30,2,31,2,$n$Song of Solomon 4:14 — *Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:* The bride's garden has aloes among its chief spices; Enoch found a whole mountain of aloe-trees at the east of the ends of the earth, their trees full of stacte (31:2).$n$,$n$And beyond these mountains I saw another mountain to the east of the ends of the earth, whereon were aloe-trees, and all the trees were full of stacte, being like almond-trees.$n$,false),
(17208,'S',31,1,29,2,$n$Song of Solomon 3:6 — *Who is this that cometh out of the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all powders of the merchant?* The myrrh and frankincense that herald the Bridegroom are what Enoch's aromatic trees exhale (29:2).$n$,$n$And there I saw aromatic trees exhaling the fragrance of frankincense and myrrh, and the trees also were similar to the almond tree.$n$,false),
(17209,'S',31,1,31,1,$n$Exodus 30:34 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* The galbanum that flows as nectar from the groves Enoch saw (31:1) is one of the sweet spices Yahuah (LORD) named for the holy incense.$n$,$n$And I saw other mountains, and amongst them were groves of trees, and there flowed forth from them nectar, which is named sarara and galbanum.$n$,false),
(17247,'S',34,1,34,2,$n$Job 37:9 — *Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.* Job names the cold north-wind Enoch is shown loosed from the northern portals first.$n$,$n$And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.$n$,false),
(17259,'S',34,2,34,2,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,* The frost and snow that come through Enoch's north portals (34:2) are drawn from these treasuries no man has entered.$n$,$n$And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.$n$,false),
(17261,'S',34,2,34,2,$n$Psalms 135:7 — *He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth the wind out of his treasuries.* The north portals of 1 Enoch 34:2 are these very treasuries from which Yahuah (LORD) brings out the wind.$n$,$n$And here I saw three portals of heaven open in the heaven: through each of them proceed north winds: when they blow there is cold, hail, frost, snow, dew, and rain.$n$,false),
(17272,'S',36,3,76,1,$n$Revelation 7:1 — *And after these things I saw four angels standing on the four corners of the earth, holding the four winds of the earth, that the wind should not blow on the earth, nor on the sea, nor on any tree.* John sees four angels holding the four winds at the four corners of the earth; Enoch was shown the twelve portals at the ends of the earth, open to all the quarters, from which the winds go forth (76:1).$n$,$n$And at the ends of the earth I saw twelve portals open to all the quarters (of the heaven), from which the winds go forth and blow over the earth.$n$,false),
(17922,'S',37,4,1,2,$n$1 Corinthians 2:7 — *But we speak the wisdom of Elohim (God) in a mystery, even the hidden wisdom, which Elohim (God) ordained before the world unto our glory.* Paul's hidden wisdom ordained before the world matches Enoch's vision of wisdom held back for the generation 'which is for to come' (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$,$n$And he took up his parable and said—Enoch a righteous man, whose eyes were opened by Elohim (God), saw the vision of the Holy One in the heavens, which the angels showed me, and from them I heard everything, and from them I understood as I saw, but not for this generation, but for a remote one which is for to come.$n$,false),
(17924,'S',37,4,1,2,$n$Deuteronomy 29:29 — *The secret things belong unto Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God): but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.* The Torah's sealed-versus-revealed line is the very frame of Enoch's wisdom withheld from former generations and granted to the elect (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$,$n$And he took up his parable and said—Enoch a righteous man, whose eyes were opened by Elohim (God), saw the vision of the Holy One in the heavens, which the angels showed me, and from them I heard everything, and from them I understood as I saw, but not for this generation, but for a remote one which is for to come.$n$,false),
(17925,'S',37,4,1,2,$n$Matthew 13:35 — *That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world.* Yahusha's parable-speech unveils what was kept secret, exactly as Enoch's vision of wisdom is reserved 'not for this generation' (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$,$n$And he took up his parable and said—Enoch a righteous man, whose eyes were opened by Elohim (God), saw the vision of the Holy One in the heavens, which the angels showed me, and from them I heard everything, and from them I understood as I saw, but not for this generation, but for a remote one which is for to come.$n$,false),
(17940,'S',38,1,38,1,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* Wisdom's persecuted elect shining at their visitation is Enoch's congregation of the righteous appearing while the sinners are judged and driven from the face of the earth (38:1).$n$,$n$The First Parable. When the congregation of the righteous shall appear, And sinners shall be judged for their sins, And shall be driven from the face of the earth:$n$,false),
(17934,'S',38,2,50,2,$n$Isaiah 26:2 — *Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.* Isaiah's righteous nation that keeps the truth is the congregation of the righteous and elect who are victorious in the name of Yahuah of Spirits (50:2).$n$,$n$On the day of affliction on which evil shall have been treasured up against the sinners. And the righteous shall be victorious in the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits: And He will cause the others to witness (this) That they may repent And forgo the works of their hands.$n$,false),
(17927,'S',38,3,38,3,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The books opened and the dead judged by their works is the hour Enoch names: the secrets of the righteous revealed and the sinners judged (38:3).$n$,$n$When the secrets of the righteous shall be revealed and the sinners judged, And the godless driven from the presence of the righteous and elect,$n$,false),
(17928,'S',38,3,38,3,$n$Revelation 20:11 — *And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.* The throne from whose face earth and heaven flee is the presence Enoch sees the godless driven from — away from the righteous and the elect (38:3).$n$,$n$When the secrets of the righteous shall be revealed and the sinners judged, And the godless driven from the presence of the righteous and elect,$n$,false),
(17935,'S',38,3,38,2,$n$Isaiah 53:11 — *He shall see of the travail of his soul, and shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.* Isaiah's righteous servant who justifies many is the Righteous One who appears before the eyes of the righteous in Enoch's first parable (38:2).$n$,$n$And when the Righteous One shall appear before the eyes of the righteous, Whose elect works hang upon Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And light shall appear to the righteous and the elect who dwell on the earth, Where then will be the dwelling of the sinners, And where the resting-place of those who have denied Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits? It had been good for them if they had not been born.$n$,false),
(17981,'S',38,3,38,3,$n$Matthew 10:26 — *Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and hid, that shall not be known.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) promise that every hidden thing shall be uncovered is Enoch's hour when the secrets of the righteous are revealed and the sinners judged (38:3).$n$,$n$When the secrets of the righteous shall be revealed and the sinners judged, And the godless driven from the presence of the righteous and elect,$n$,false),
(17930,'S',38,6,54,6,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) furnace of fire for the children of the wicked one is the burning furnace the four archangels cast the hosts of Azazel into on the great day (54:6).$n$,$n$And Michael, and Gabriel, and Raphael, and Phanuel shall take hold of them on that great day, and cast them on that day into the burning furnace, that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits may take vengeance on them for their unrighteousness in becoming subject to Satan and leading astray those who dwell on the earth.’$n$,false),
(17931,'S',38,6,62,10,$n$Revelation 6:17 — *For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?* The great day before which no power can stand is Enoch's day when the kings and the mighty go out from his presence with their faces filled with shame (62:10).$n$,$n$Nevertheless that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits will so press them That they shall hastily go forth from His presence, And their faces shall be filled with shame, And the darkness grow deeper on their faces.$n$,false),
(17932,'S',38,6,48,8,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* John's kings and mighty men hiding in terror are Enoch's kings of the earth downcast in countenance on the day of their anguish, unable to save themselves (48:8).$n$,$n$In these days downcast in countenance shall the kings of the earth have become, And the strong who possess the land because of the works of their hands, For on the day of their anguish and affliction they shall not (be able to) save themselves.$n$,false),
(17959,'S',39,3,39,8,$n$John 14:2 — *In my Father's house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.* Yahusha (Jesus) names the dwelling-places Enoch's spirit longed for — *there I wished to dwell, and my spirit longed for that dwelling-place* (39:8) — and says he goes ahead to prepare them.$n$,$n$There I wished to dwell, And my spirit longed for that dwelling-place: And there heretofore hath been my portion, For so has it been established concerning me before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(17956,'S',39,5,45,3,$n$Isaiah 42:1 — *Behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, in whom my soul delighteth; I have put my spirit upon him: he shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles.* Isaiah's *mine elect* is Enoch's *Mine Elect One* (45:3) — the chosen servant in whom the Father delights, set on the throne of glory.$n$,$n$On that day Mine Elect One shall sit on the throne of glory And shall try their works, And their places of rest shall be innumerable. And their souls shall grow strong within them when they see Mine elect ones, And those who have called upon My glorious name:$n$,false),
(17957,'S',39,6,39,6,$n$Revelation 21:3 — *And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of Elohim (God) is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God).* John hears the tabernacle of Elohim (God) with men; Enoch saw the Elect One of righteousness with the righteous and the elect without number before him for ever and ever (39:6).$n$,$n$And in that place mine eyes saw the Elect One of righteousness and of faith, And righteousness shall prevail in his days, And the righteous and elect shall be without number before Him for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(17946,'S',39,11,40,2,$n$Revelation 4:8 — *And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Yahuah Elohim (Lord God) Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.* John's four living creatures praising ceaselessly about the throne are Enoch's four presences who surround the throne of glory and praise in 1 Enoch 40:2.$n$,$n$And on the four sides of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits I saw four presences, different from those that sleep not, and I learnt their names: for the angel that went with me made known to me their names, and showed me all the hidden things.$n$,false),
(17986,'S',41,8,41,8,$n$Hebrews 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* Enoch is told no angel hinders and no power can — he himself appoints the judge and judges all (41:9). The intercession that reaches that throne is the Son's, who ever lives to make it for those who come to the Father by him.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(17987,'S',41,8,41,8,$n$1 Timothy 2:5 — *For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus);* No angel hinders, no power hinders; he judges them all before him (41:9). The one mediator between that judge and men is not an angel but the Formed Son come in flesh.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(18041,'S',41,8,41,8,$n$Genesis 1:18 — *And to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness: and Elohim (God) saw that it was good* The luminaries themselves are the agents of the division Enoch names in 41:8 — light to the righteous and darkness to the sinners, in the name of him who divided the spirits of men.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(18042,'S',41,8,41,8,$n$Genesis 1:4 — *And Elohim (God) saw the light, that it was good: and Elohim (God) divided the light from the darkness* The first division of creation is the pattern Enoch extends in 41:8 to the dividing of the spirits of men — the same one who separated light from darkness.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(17985,'S',41,9,41,9,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* He who judges them all before him in Enoch (41:9) is the One whose opened books judge the dead by their works.$n$,$n$For no angel hinders and no power is able to hinder; for He appoints a judge for them all and He judges them all before Him.$n$,false),
(18935,'S',45,5,48,9,$n$Malachi 4:1 — *For, behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that cometh shall burn them up, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts), that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.* The wicked as stubble in the burning day is Enoch 48:9's sinners who burn as straw in the fire before the face of the holy, and leave no trace.$n$,$n$And I will give them over into the hands of Mine elect: As straw in the fire so shall they burn before the face of the holy: As lead in the water shall they sink before the face of the righteous, And no trace of them shall any more be found.$n$,false),
(18936,'S',45,5,48,9,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* The righteous flaming over the stubble is the bright reverse of Enoch 48:9, where the sinners themselves become the straw that burns.$n$,$n$And I will give them over into the hands of Mine elect: As straw in the fire so shall they burn before the face of the holy: As lead in the water shall they sink before the face of the righteous, And no trace of them shall any more be found.$n$,false),
(18933,'S',45,6,98,3,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) furnace of fire for the wicked is the furnace of fire into which Enoch's sinners' spirits are cast, in shame and slaughter (98:3).$n$,$n$Therefore they shall be wanting in doctrine and wisdom, And they shall perish thereby together with their possessions; And with all their glory and their splendour, And in shame and in slaughter and in great destitution, Their spirits shall be cast into the furnace of fire.$n$,false),
(18934,'S',45,6,45,6,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* The righteous shining in the kingdom of their Father are the righteous ones the Father has satisfied with peace and caused to dwell before him, while judgment waits for the sinners (45:6).$n$,$n$For I have provided and satisfied with peace My righteous ones And have caused them to dwell before Me: But for the sinners there is judgement impending with Me, So that I shall destroy them from the face of the earth.$n$,false),
(19849,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* The everlasting indestructible kingdom given to the Son of Adam is the stone-kingdom that outlasts the metal mountains Enoch sees go powerless.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19850,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* Daniel beholds one LIKE the Son of Adam (the kaph: he resembles mortal-man having taken on flesh) coming to the Ancient of days, while 1 Enoch names that same Elect One before whom the metal kingdoms melt.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19851,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Daniel 2:45 — *Forasmuch as thou sawest that the stone was cut out of the mountain without hands, and that it brake in pieces the iron, the brass, the clay, the silver, and the gold; the great Elohim (God) hath made known to the king what shall come to pass hereafter: and the dream is certain, and the interpretation thereof sure.* The stone breaking iron, brass, clay, silver, and gold is the same dissolution of empire's metals that Enoch shows before the Elect One.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19852,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Daniel 2:34 — *Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces.* The stone cut without hands that smites the metal image is Daniel's form of the Elect One before whose feet Enoch's metal mountains become powerless.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19853,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.* The Elect One unmakes the powers not by force but by His word, exactly as Isaiah's Branch slays the wicked with the breath of His lips.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19854,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Zechariah 4:7 — *Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.* Enoch's metal mountains melting to powerlessness is Zechariah's great mountain leveled to a plain before the chosen one.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19855,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Zechariah 4:6 — *Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of Yahuah (LORD) unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts).* The metals going powerless before the Elect One's feet enacts Zechariah's word: the kingdom comes not by might or power but by the Spirit.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19856,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Psalm 97:5 — *The hills melted like wax at the presence of Yahuah (LORD), at the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of the whole earth.* The hills melting like wax at Yahuah's presence is the same theophany Enoch sees worked through the Elect One before whom the metals go powerless.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19857,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Micah 1:4 — *And the mountains shall be molten under him, and the valleys shall be cleft, as wax before the fire, and as the waters that are poured down a steep place.* Micah's mountains melting like wax and running like poured waters is Enoch's exact image of the metal mountains dissolving before the Elect One.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19858,'S',52,3,52,6,$n$Daniel 2:44 — *And in the days of these kings shall the Elohim (God) of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever.* The Elect One before whose feet the metals melt is the everlasting stone-kingdom that consumes the kingdoms of metal.$n$,$n$And these mountains which thine eyes have seen, The mountain of iron, and the mountain of copper, and the mountain of silver, And the mountain of gold, and the mountain of soft metal, and the mountain of lead, All these shall be in the presence of the Elect One As wax before the fire, And like the water which streams down from above [upon those mountains], And they shall become powerless before his feet.$n$,false),
(19870,'S',53,2,53,1,$n$Isaiah 66:24 — *And they shall go forth, and look upon the carcases of the men that have transgressed against me: for their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched; and they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh.* Isaiah names the never-quenched judgment on the transgressors; Enoch saw the deep valley with open mouths that receives the homage of all the earth and never becomes full (53:1).$n$,$n$There mine eyes saw a deep valley with open mouths, and all who dwell on the earth and sea and islands shall bring to him gifts and presents and tokens of homage, but that deep valley shall not become full.$n$,false),
(19981,'S',62,11,46,6,$n$Isaiah 52:15 — *So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for that which had not been told them shall they see; and that which they had not heard shall they consider.* The strong abased and silenced in Enoch 46:6 are the kings who shut their mouths before the vindicated Servant.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(19985,'S',62,11,46,6,$n$Philippians 2:10 — *That at the name of Yahusha (Jesus) every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth.* Paul names the One before whom the proud of Enoch 46:6 are abased: Yahusha, the Son of Adam exalted by the Father.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(19986,'S',62,11,46,6,$n$Isaiah 45:23 — *I have sworn by myself, the word is gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and shall not return, That unto me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear.* The pride of the mighty abased in Enoch 46:6 ends where every knee bows before the throne of glory.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(21318,'S',62,13,62,13,$n$2 Peter 2:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) knoweth how to deliver the godly out of temptations, and to reserve the unjust unto the day of judgment to be punished.* The same Lord who drowns the ungodly delivers his own, just as Enoch's righteous and elect are saved on that day and never again see the face of the sinners (62:13).$n$,$n$And the righteous and elect shall be saved on that day, And they shall never thenceforward see the face of the sinners and unrighteous.$n$,false),
(18003,'S',62,14,62,14,$n$Revelation 21:3 — *And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of Elohim (God) is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God).* Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits abiding over his elect, who eat and lie down and rise up with the Son of Adam for ever (62:14), is the tabernacle of Elohim (God) finally set among his people.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits will abide over them, And with that Son of Adam shall they eat And lie down and rise up for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(18004,'S',62,14,62,14,$n$Sirach 24:8 — *So the Creator of all things gave me a commandment, and he that made me caused my tabernacle to rest, and said, Let your dwelling be in Jacob, and your inheritance in Yashar'el (Israel).* Wisdom, denied a dwelling among men, is given her resting-place in Jacob — the elect over whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits abides and with whom the Son of Adam eats for ever (62:14).$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits will abide over them, And with that Son of Adam shall they eat And lie down and rise up for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(21278,'S',63,5,62,2,$n$Matthew 25:31 — *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:* Yahusha (Jesus) names himself the Son of Adam seated on the throne of glory to judge — the seat Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits set him on, where the word of his mouth slays all the sinners (62:2).$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$,false),
(21270,'S',63,6,69,27,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:6 — *Therefore have we erred from the way of truth, and the light of righteousness has not shined to us, and the sun of righteousness rose not upon us.* Those who led the world astray (69:27) confess at last that they themselves erred from the way of truth.$n$,$n$And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.$n$,false),
(21281,'S',63,6,69,27,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* The Son of Adam driving the sinners from the earth (69:27) exercises the everlasting dominion given Him before the Ancient of days.$n$,$n$And he sat on the throne of his glory, And the sum of judgement was given unto the Son of Adam, And he caused the sinners to pass away and be destroyed from off the face of the earth, And those who have led the world astray.$n$,false),
(21273,'S',63,7,63,7,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:8 — *What has pride profited us? or what good has riches with our vaunting brought us?* The hollow boast of pride and riches is exactly the confession of Enoch's kings: *our hope was in the sceptre of our kingdom, and in our glory* (63:7).$n$,$n$For we have not believed before Him Nor glorified the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, [nor glorified our Lord] But our hope was in the sceptre of our kingdom, And in our glory.$n$,false),
(21275,'S',63,7,62,4,$n$Revelation 6:17 — *For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?* The day of wrath that none can stand against is Enoch's day when pain comes upon the kings and the mighty as on a woman in travail (62:4).$n$,$n$Then shall pain come upon them as on a woman in travail, [And she has pain in bringing forth] When her child enters the mouth of the womb, And she has pain in bringing forth.$n$,false),
(21269,'S',63,9,63,9,$n$Psalms 2:12 — *Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish from the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him.* Passing away from before his face on account of their works (63:9) is the perishing-from-the-way the kings courted by refusing to kiss the Son while there was time.$n$,$n$And we pass away from before His face on account of our works, And all our sins are reckoned up in righteousness.’$n$,false),
(21311,'S',65,6,65,6,$n$2 Peter 2:3 — *And through covetousness shall they with feigned words make merchandise of you: whose judgment now of a long time lingereth not, and their damnation slumbereth not.* The command that has gone forth from the presence of Yahuah (Lord) — their ruin accomplished because of the secrets they learned (65:6) — is the sentence Peter says lingers not and does not slumber.$n$,$n$And a command has gone forth from the presence of Yahuah (Lord) concerning those who dwell on the earth that their ruin is accomplished because they have learnt all the secrets of the angels, and all the violence of the Satans, and all their powers—the most secret ones—and all the power of those who practise sorcery, and the power of witchcraft, and the power of those who make molten images for the whole earth:$n$,false),
(21307,'S',65,9,64,2,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* The descended angels of Enoch 64:2 are the angels Jude says left their habitation and are reserved in chains for judgement.$n$,$n$I heard the voice of the angel saying: ‘These are the angels who descended to the earth, and revealed what was hidden to the children of men and seduced the children of men into committing sin.’$n$,false),
(21308,'S',65,9,64,2,$n$Genesis 6:12 — *And Elohim (God) looked upon the earth, and, behold, it was corrupt; for all flesh had corrupted his way upon the earth.* The angels who 'corrupted the earth' in Enoch 64:2 are why Moses says all flesh had corrupted its way.$n$,$n$I heard the voice of the angel saying: ‘These are the angels who descended to the earth, and revealed what was hidden to the children of men and seduced the children of men into committing sin.’$n$,false),
(21305,'S',65,10,15,12,$n$Jubilees 5:1 — *And it came to pass when the children of men began to multiply on the face of the earth and daughters were born to them, that the angels of Elohim (God) saw them on a certain year of this jubilee, that they were beautiful to look upon; and they took themselves wives of all whom they chose, and they bare to them sons and they were giants.* The spirits of the giants in Enoch 15:12 are the offspring of the angels Jubilees says took wives and bore giants.$n$,$n$And these spirits shall rise up against the children of men and against the women, because they have proceeded from them.$n$,false),
(21306,'S',65,11,65,11,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment.* Those who showed what was hidden have no place of repentance for ever — *they are the damned* (65:11). Peter's angels that sinned, cast down and reserved unto judgment, are these.$n$,$n$And these—they have no place of repentance for ever, because they have shown them what was hidden, and they are the damned: but as for thee, my son, Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits knows that thou art pure, and guiltless of this reproach concerning the secrets.$n$,false),
(21301,'S',65,12,10,20,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake; for the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth; neither will I again smite any more every thing living, as I have done.* The cleansed earth of Enoch 10:20 is the ground Yahuah vows not again to curse once the Flood has passed.$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$,false),
(21302,'S',65,12,10,20,$n$Jubilees 5:11 — *And He destroyed all from their places, and there was not left one of them whom He judged not according to all their wickedness. And He made for all His works a new and righteous nature, so that they should not sin in their whole nature for ever, but should be all righteous each in his kind alway.* The earth cleansed and made righteous in Enoch 10:20 is Jubilees' new and righteous nature after the Flood.$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$,false),
(21325,'S',67,7,10,20,$n$Revelation 21:1 — *And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.* John sees the cleansed creation Enoch foresaw — the corrupted first earth passed away once all sin and iniquity are purged at 10:20.$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$,false),
(21326,'S',67,7,10,20,$n$2 Peter 3:13 — *Nevertheless we, according to his promise, look for new heavens and a new earth, wherein dwelleth righteousness.* Peter's hope of an earth *wherein dwelleth righteousness* is Enoch's earth cleansed from all oppression, all unrighteousness, all sin and all godlessness (10:20).$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$,false),
(21327,'S',67,7,10,20,$n$Isaiah 65:17 — *For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth: and the former shall not be remembered, nor come into mind.* Isaiah's new creation is Enoch's earth cleansed from all unrighteousness and uncleanness (10:20) — the defiled former order wiped away and remembered no more.$n$,$n$And cleanse thou the earth from all oppression, and from all unrighteousness, and from all sin, and from all godlessness: and all the uncleanness that is wrought upon the earth destroy from off the earth.$n$,false),
(21340,'S',67,1,10,13,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* The reserving of the fallen angels for the judgment of the great day is Enoch's *in those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire* (10:13) — the prison kept for them till then.$n$,$n$In those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison in which they shall be confined for ever.$n$,false),
(21394,'S',71,8,60,12,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The same ordering hand that weighs the winds in 60:12 appoints the lights of the moon — the Creator's measured order, looking ahead to Enoch's Luminaries.$n$,$n$And the chambers of the winds, and how the winds are divided, and how they are weighed, and (how) the portals of the winds are reckoned, each according to the power of the wind, and the power of the lights of the moon, and according to the power that is fitting: and the divisions of the stars according to their names, and how all the divisions are divided.$n$,false),
(21395,'S',71,8,60,12,$n$Jeremiah 10:13 — *When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens, and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.* The winds brought out of Yahuah's treasures are the storehouses of the winds Enoch sees divided and weighed in 60:12.$n$,$n$And the chambers of the winds, and how the winds are divided, and how they are weighed, and (how) the portals of the winds are reckoned, each according to the power of the wind, and the power of the lights of the moon, and according to the power that is fitting: and the divisions of the stars according to their names, and how all the divisions are divided.$n$,false),
(21396,'S',71,8,60,12,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail.* The storehouses of the heavens Enoch is shown in 60:12 are the same treasure-chambers Yahuah challenges Job to enter — the Creator's hidden ordering of the elements.$n$,$n$And the chambers of the winds, and how the winds are divided, and how they are weighed, and (how) the portals of the winds are reckoned, each according to the power of the wind, and the power of the lights of the moon, and according to the power that is fitting: and the divisions of the stars according to their names, and how all the divisions are divided.$n$,false),
(22496,'S',73,3,78,8,$n$Psalm 89:37 — *It shall be established for ever as the moon, and as a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.* The moon Enoch watches wax to fifteen parts and wane part by part (78:7–8) is the heaven's faithful witness — her steady count pledges the steadiness of the covenant.$n$,$n$And in her waning (the moon) decreases on the first day to fourteen parts of her light, on the second to thirteen parts of light, on the third to twelve, on the fourth to eleven, on the fifth to ten, on the sixth to nine, on the seventh to eight, on the eighth to seven, on the ninth to six, on the tenth to five, on the eleventh to four, on the twelfth to three, on the thirteenth to two, on the fourteenth to the half of a seventh, and all her remaining light disappears wholly on the fifteenth.$n$,false),
(22495,'S',73,4,78,8,$n$Ecclesiasticus 43:6 — *He made the moon also to serve in her season for a declaration of times, and a sign of the world.* The waning Enoch numbers part by part (78:8) is the moon serving in her season as the declared sign of the times.$n$,$n$And in her waning (the moon) decreases on the first day to fourteen parts of her light, on the second to thirteen parts of light, on the third to twelve, on the fourth to eleven, on the fifth to ten, on the sixth to nine, on the seventh to eight, on the eighth to seven, on the ninth to six, on the tenth to five, on the eleventh to four, on the twelfth to three, on the thirteenth to two, on the fourteenth to the half of a seventh, and all her remaining light disappears wholly on the fifteenth.$n$,false),
(22497,'S',73,4,78,7,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* As fifteen parts of light are transferred to the moon till her light is accomplished according to the sign of the year (78:7), she keeps the seasons she was appointed to mark.$n$,$n$And fifteen parts of light are transferred to her till the fifteenth day (when) her light is accomplished, according to the sign of the year, and she becomes fifteen parts, and the moon grows by (the addition of) fourteenth parts.$n$,false),
(22509,'S',74,1,74,2,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork.* The positions and months of the luminaries Uriel showed Enoch and he wrote down (74:2) are the firmament preaching the Maker's handiwork.$n$,$n$And all these Uriel, the holy angel who is the leader of them all, showed to me, and their positions, and I wrote down their positions as he showed them to me, and I wrote down their months as they were, and the appearance of their lights till fifteen days were accomplished.$n$,false),
(22511,'S',74,1,74,2,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The luminaries Uriel shows Enoch are the very lights set for the appointed times (moedim) on the fourth day.$n$,$n$And all these Uriel, the holy angel who is the leader of them all, showed to me, and their positions, and I wrote down their positions as he showed them to me, and I wrote down their months as they were, and the appearance of their lights till fifteen days were accomplished.$n$,false),
(22510,'S',74,3,74,3,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The moon accomplishing all her light in the east and all her darkness in the west, by sevenths (74:3), is the Creator's own appointment of the seasons, not a man-made scheme.$n$,$n$In single seventh parts she accomplishes all her light in the east, and in single seventh parts accomplishes all her darkness in the west.$n$,false),
(22507,'S',74,11,74,11,$n$Jubilees 6:36 — *For there will be those who will assuredly make observations of the moon–now (it) disturbs the seasons and comes in from year to year ten days too soon.* Jubilees names the same shortfall Enoch records — the moon falling behind the sun and the stars, six days every year, thirty in five (74:11). Enoch counts her against the sun; Jubilees counts her ten days short of the 364; both say the moon cannot keep the year.$n$,$n$And the overplus of the sun and of the stars amounts to six days: in 5 years 6 days every year come to 30 days: and the moon falls behind the sun and stars to the number of 30 days.$n$,false),
(22501,'S',74,13,74,12,$n$Deuteronomy 4:19 — *And lest thou lift up thine eyes unto heaven, and when thou seest the sun, and the moon, and the stars, even all the host of heaven, shouldest be driven to worship them, and serve them, which Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath divided unto all nations under the whole heaven.* The luminaries that mark the reckoning are servants of the appointed times, never to be worshipped — the host of heaven is the Creator's order, not a god to serve.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22502,'S',74,13,74,12,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* To change the order of the lights is the enemy's work — the horn who thinks to change the very times and laws Enoch 74:12 says must not be changed.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22504,'S',74,13,74,12,$n$Jubilees 6:35 — *...for the book (lies) written before me, and on the heavenly tables the division of days is ordained, lest they forget the feasts of the covenant and walk according to the feasts of the nations after their error and after their ignorance.* The heavenly tables ordain the division of days so the covenant feasts are kept — the same righteousness Enoch 74:12 demands of the year.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22505,'S',74,13,74,12,$n$Leviticus 23:4 — *These are the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), even holy convocations, which ye shall proclaim in their seasons.* The stations that must not transgress their reckoning are the moedim — the feasts proclaimed in their seasons, fixed by the lights Enoch is shown.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22520,'S',75,4,75,1,$n$1 Chronicles 27:1 — *Now the children of Yashar'el (Israel) after their number, to wit, the chief fathers and captains of thousands and hundreds, and their officers that served the king in any matter of the courses, which came in and went out month by month throughout all the months of the year, of every course were twenty and four thousand.* The leaders of the heads of thousands set over the whole creation and the stars, who serve on the four days outside the count of the year (75:1), are mirrored on earth by Israel's courses of captains of thousands — the heavenly ranks ordering time as the priestly ranks order service.$n$,$n$And the leaders of the heads of the thousands, who are placed over the whole creation and over all the stars, have also to do with the four intercalary days, being inseparable from their office, according to the reckoning of the year, and these render service on the four days which are not reckoned in the reckoning of the year.$n$,false),
(22521,'S',75,6,75,1,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The leaders set over the stars and the four days that divide the year (75:1) keep the very appointment the Psalmist celebrates — the moon for the seasons, the sun for its setting.$n$,$n$And the leaders of the heads of the thousands, who are placed over the whole creation and over all the stars, have also to do with the four intercalary days, being inseparable from their office, according to the reckoning of the year, and these render service on the four days which are not reckoned in the reckoning of the year.$n$,false),
(22525,'S',76,9,76,5,$n$Job 37:9 — *Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.* Job sorts the winds by quarter just as Enoch's portals do — the east wind of the first portal bringing desolation, drought, heat, and destruction (76:5), the north portals cold and frost.$n$,$n$And the first wind from those portals, called the east wind, comes forth through the first portal which is in the east, inclining towards the south: from it come forth desolation, drought, heat, and destruction.$n$,false),
(22539,'S',77,7,32,3,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* Enoch's tree of wisdom in the Garden of Righteousness (32:3) is the Torah's tree set in the midst of the garden.$n$,$n$And I came to the Garden of Righteousness, and saw beyond those trees many large trees growing there and of goodly fragrance, large, very beautiful and glorious, and the tree of wisdom whereof they eat and know great wisdom.$n$,false),
(22536,'S',77,8,32,4,$n$Ezekiel 47:12 — *And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.* Ezekiel's tree by the river from the sanctuary matches Enoch's beautiful, far-fragrant tree of the garden.$n$,$n$That tree is in height like the fir, and its leaves are like (those of) the Carob tree: and its fruit is like the clusters of the vine, very beautiful: and the fragrance of the tree penetrates afar.$n$,false),
(22537,'S',77,8,32,4,$n$Revelation 22:2 — *In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.* The fruitful tree of the paradise of righteousness stands restored in the New Jerusalem.$n$,$n$That tree is in height like the fir, and its leaves are like (those of) the Carob tree: and its fruit is like the clusters of the vine, very beautiful: and the fragrance of the tree penetrates afar.$n$,false),
(22551,'S',78,3,78,1,$n$Psalm 148:5 — *Let them praise the name of Yahuah (LORD): for he commanded, and they were created.* Enoch names the sun by name — Orjârês and Tômâs (78:1); Psalm 148 grounds the naming in the Creator's command that made them.$n$,$n$And the names of the sun are the following: the first Orjârês, and the second Tômâs.$n$,false),
(22548,'S',78,4,74,12,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts.* The sun and the stars completing the years with perfect justice in 364 days (74:12) is the very reckoning Jubilees commands Israel keep so the feasts are not disturbed.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22543,'S',78,9,69,20,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork.* The luminaries that complete their courses in righteousness (Enoch 69:20) are the firmament preaching its Maker's order without a word.$n$,$n$And through that oath the sun and moon complete their course, And deviate not from their ordinance from eternity to eternity.$n$,false),
(22542,'S',78,11,69,20,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* Where Enoch's sun and moon deviate not from their ordinance from eternity to eternity (69:20), the enemy thinks to change the times — the perversion of the reckoning the luminary book warns against.$n$,$n$And through that oath the sun and moon complete their course, And deviate not from their ordinance from eternity to eternity.$n$,false),
(22544,'S',78,12,78,12,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The first day is called the new moon, for on that day the light rises upon her (78:12) — the moon appointed for the seasons, the Creator's order of the appointed times.$n$,$n$And on the first day she is called the new moon, for on that day the light rises upon her.$n$,false),
(22545,'S',78,12,78,12,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years.* The new moon named on its first day (78:12) is one of the signs and seasons the fourth-day mandate set the lights for.$n$,$n$And on the first day she is called the new moon, for on that day the light rises upon her.$n$,false),
(22565,'S',79,3,79,1,$n$Jeremiah 31:35 — *Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), which giveth the sun for a light by day, and the ordinances of the moon and of the stars for a light by night, which divideth the sea when the waves thereof roar; Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts) is his name:* The ordinances of moon and stars Enoch shows are Yahuah's own fixed ordinances, sworn by His name.$n$,$n$And now, my son, I have shown thee everything, and the law of all the stars of the heaven is completed.$n$,false),
(22567,'S',79,3,79,1,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The lights are appointed for the seasons (moedim) — Enoch 79 simply unfolds the law Genesis sets at creation.$n$,$n$And now, my son, I have shown thee everything, and the law of all the stars of the heaven is completed.$n$,false),
(22562,'S',79,4,74,12,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork.* The hosts completing their revolutions in righteousness is the firmament's wordless declaration of its Maker.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22563,'S',79,4,74,12,$n$Psalm 148:3 — *Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.* The sun and the stars that complete the years with perfect justice (74:12) are the chorus the Psalm calls to praise.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22564,'S',79,4,74,12,$n$Psalm 148:6 — *He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass.* The decree that holds the host in their courses is the same reason Enoch's luminaries do not change their order.$n$,$n$And the sun and the stars bring in all the years exactly, so that they do not advance or delay their position by a single day unto eternity; but complete the years with perfect justice in 364 days.$n$,false),
(22557,'S',79,5,79,5,$n$Jubilees 6:36 — *For there will be those who will assuredly make observations of the moon–now (it) disturbs the seasons and comes in from year to year ten days too soon.* Enoch records the moon falling behind the sun and the order of the stars (79:5) — the disturbance Jubilees warns of when men reckon by the moon alone.$n$,$n$She falls behind the sun and the order of the stars exactly five days in the course of one period, and when this place which thou seest has been traversed.$n$,false),
(22558,'S',79,5,74,10,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts.* The 364 days Enoch counts when the years are full (74:10) is the same reckoning Jubilees commands Israel to keep so the feasts are not disturbed.$n$,$n$And if five years are added together the sun has an overplus of thirty days, and all the days which accrue to it for one of those five years, when they are full, amount to 364 days.$n$,false),
(22575,'S',80,1,80,7,$n$Romans 1:25 — *Who changed the truth of Elohim (God) into a lie, and worshipped and served the creature more than the Creator, who is blessed for ever. Amen.* Paul names the root of the error Enoch foretells — the order of the stars concealed from the sinners, who err and take them to be gods (80:7): the created luminary served in place of the Creator who appointed it.$n$,$n$And the whole order of the stars shall be concealed from the sinners, And the thoughts of those on the earth shall err concerning them, [And they shall be altered from all their ways], Yea, they shall err and take them to be gods.$n$,false),
(22576,'S',80,1,80,7,$n$Jeremiah 8:2 — *And they shall spread them before the sun, and the moon, and all the host of heaven, whom they have loved, and whom they have served, and after whom they have walked, and whom they have sought, and whom they have worshipped: they shall not be gathered, nor be buried; they shall be for dung upon the face of the earth.* Jeremiah's idolaters loved and served the same sun, moon, and host that Enoch says men come to take for gods (80:7).$n$,$n$And the whole order of the stars shall be concealed from the sinners, And the thoughts of those on the earth shall err concerning them, [And they shall be altered from all their ways], Yea, they shall err and take them to be gods.$n$,false),
(22577,'S',80,1,80,6,$n$Deuteronomy 4:19 — *And lest thou lift up thine eyes unto heaven, and when thou seest the sun, and the moon, and the stars, even all the host of heaven, shouldest be driven to worship them, and serve them, which Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath divided unto all nations under the whole heaven.* When the chiefs of the stars transgress their order and alter their orbits (80:6), men err and worship the host of heaven — the very driving-away Moses forbade.$n$,$n$And many chiefs of the stars shall transgress the order (prescribed). And these shall alter their orbits and tasks, And not appear at the seasons prescribed to them.$n$,false),
(22588,'S',81,3,81,6,$n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way, and when thou liest down, and when thou risest up.* Enoch's charge to teach his children and record it for them and testify to all his children (81:6) is the Shema's command to teach the next generation diligently.$n$,$n$One year we will leave thee with thy son, till thou givest thy (last) commands, that thou mayst teach thy children and record (it) for them, and testify to all thy children; and in the second year they shall take thee from their midst.$n$,false),
(22586,'S',81,5,82,1,$n$Proverbs 3:3 — *Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:* Enoch writes the wisdom down lest it be lost (82:1); the canon writes the same on the tablet of the heart.$n$,$n$And now, my son Methuselah, all these things I am recounting to thee and writing down for thee, and I have revealed to thee everything, and given thee books concerning all these: so preserve, my son Methuselah, the books from thy father’s hand, and (see) that thou deliver them to the generations of the world.$n$,false),
(22587,'S',81,5,82,1,$n$Deuteronomy 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart:* The words of truth Enoch writes for Methuselah to preserve (82:1) are the commanded words kept in the heart so they are not lost.$n$,$n$And now, my son Methuselah, all these things I am recounting to thee and writing down for thee, and I have revealed to thee everything, and given thee books concerning all these: so preserve, my son Methuselah, the books from thy father’s hand, and (see) that thou deliver them to the generations of the world.$n$,false),
(22582,'S',81,7,80,6,$n$Jubilees 6:37 — *For this reason the years will come upon them when they will disturb (the order), and make an abominable (day) the day of testimony, and an unclean day a feast day, and they will confound all the days, the holy with the unclean, and the unclean day with the holy; for they will go wrong as to the months and sabbaths and feasts and jubilees. For this reason I command and testify to you that you may testify to them; for after your death your children will disturb (them), so that they will not make the year three hundred and sixty-four days only, and for this reason they will go wrong as to the new moons and seasons and sabbaths and festivals, and they will eat all kinds of blood with all kinds of flesh.* Jubilees names what Enoch foresaw — the chiefs of the stars transgressing their order and not appearing at the seasons prescribed (80:6) — and adds the result among men: going wrong as to new moons, seasons, sabbaths and festivals, and eating blood with all kinds of flesh.$n$,$n$And many chiefs of the stars shall transgress the order (prescribed). And these shall alter their orbits and tasks, And not appear at the seasons prescribed to them.$n$,false),
(22583,'S',81,7,82,5,$n$Jubilees 6:34 — *And all the children of Yashar'el (Israel) will forget, and will not find the path of the years, and will forget the new moons, and seasons, and sabbaths, and they will go wrong as to all the order of the years.* Jubilees describes the identical drift Enoch foretells — men at fault, not reckoning the days accurately in the whole reckoning of the year (82:5) — forgetting the new moons, seasons and sabbaths of the 364-day order.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$,false),
(22584,'S',81,7,80,6,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* To alter the orbits and seasons prescribed (80:6) is the work of the horn who thinks to change times and laws.$n$,$n$And many chiefs of the stars shall transgress the order (prescribed). And these shall alter their orbits and tasks, And not appear at the seasons prescribed to them.$n$,false),
(22585,'S',81,7,80,2,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The times and seasons were written into creation by the lights; in the days of the sinners all things on the earth alter and do not appear in their time (80:2) — the order violated, not rewritten by men.$n$,$n$And in the days of the sinners the years shall be shortened, And their seed shall be tardy on their lands and fields, And all things on the earth shall alter, And shall not appear in their time: And the rain shall be kept back And the heaven shall withhold (it).$n$,false),
(22578,'S',81,9,81,9,$n$Psalm 1:1 — *Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.* Enoch's righteous who die on account of the deeds of men and are taken away because of the doings of the godless (81:9) are the blessed man of the two ways — the one who would not walk in the counsel of the ungodly, and paid for it.$n$,$n$And those who practise righteousness shall die on account of the deeds of men, And be taken away on account of the doings of the godless.’$n$,false),
(22581,'S',81,10,82,4,$n$Leviticus 23:2 — *Speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), and say unto them, Concerning the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my feasts.* Blessed are those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners in the reckoning of all their days (82:4) — to keep the count is to keep the feasts that are Yahuah's (the LORD's) own appointed times, fixed by the lights.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$,false),
(22602,'S',82,3,82,5,$n$Jubilees 6:38 — *...they will go wrong as to the months and sabbaths and feasts and jubilees. For this reason I command and testify to you that you may testify to them; for after your death your children will disturb (them), so that they will not make the year three hundred and sixty-four days only, and for this reason they will go wrong as to the new moons and seasons and sabbaths and festivals, and they will eat all kinds of blood with all kinds of flesh.* Jubilees and Enoch describe the same coming apostasy from the reckoning: men at fault, not reckoning the days in the whole reckoning of the year (82:5) — Jubilees adds the going wrong as to new moons, sabbaths and feasts, down to eating blood with flesh.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$,false),
(22603,'S',82,3,80,7,$n$Deuteronomy 4:19 — *And lest thou lift up thine eyes unto heaven, and when thou seest the sun, and the moon, and the stars, even all the host of heaven, shouldest be driven to worship them, and serve them, which Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath divided unto all nations under the whole heaven.* When the order of the lights is concealed from the sinners they err and take them to be gods (80:7) — the host-of-heaven idolatry Torah forbade.$n$,$n$And the whole order of the stars shall be concealed from the sinners, And the thoughts of those on the earth shall err concerning them, [And they shall be altered from all their ways], Yea, they shall err and take them to be gods.$n$,false),
(22604,'S',82,3,82,5,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The new moons and seasons men fail to reckon accurately (82:5) are appointed by the luminaries themselves.$n$,$n$Owing to them men shall be at fault and not reckon them in the whole reckoning of the year: yea, men shall be at fault, and not recognize them accurately.$n$,false),
(22605,'S',82,3,82,6,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The year completed in three hundred and sixty-four days, truly recorded for ever (82:6), is the Genesis decree of lights for days and years worked out in full.$n$,$n$For they belong to the reckoning of the year and are truly recorded (thereon) for ever, one in the first portal and one in the third, and one in the fourth and one in the sixth, and the year is completed in three hundred and sixty-four days.$n$,false),
(22606,'S',82,3,80,7,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* Enoch's sinners from whom the order of the stars is concealed, who err about the times (80:7), are Daniel's horn that thinks to change times and laws.$n$,$n$And the whole order of the stars shall be concealed from the sinners, And the thoughts of those on the earth shall err concerning them, [And they shall be altered from all their ways], Yea, they shall err and take them to be gods.$n$,false),
(22599,'S',82,5,82,4,$n$Leviticus 23:4 — *These are the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), even holy convocations, which ye shall proclaim in their seasons.* Blessed are those who sin not as the sinners in the reckoning of all their days (82:4) — to keep the count right is to keep the appointed feasts in their seasons, as the lights ordain them.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$,false),
(22600,'S',82,5,82,4,$n$Psalm 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night.* The blessed walk in the way of righteousness and keep the reckoning of their days (82:4) because their delight is in his law.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$,false),
(22601,'S',82,5,82,4,$n$Psalm 1:1 — *Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.* Enoch's *blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners* (82:4) is the blessing of the man who does not walk in the way of sinners.$n$,$n$Blessed are all the righteous, blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners, in the reckoning of all their days in which the sun traverses the heaven, entering into and departing from the portals for thirty days with the heads of thousands of the order of the stars, together with the four which are intercalated which divide the four portions of the year, which lead them and enter with them four days.$n$,false),
(22596,'S',82,6,82,6,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts...* The reckoning Enoch records as true for ever — the year completed in three hundred and sixty-four days (82:6) — is the same count Jubilees commands Israel to keep.$n$,$n$For they belong to the reckoning of the year and are truly recorded (thereon) for ever, one in the first portal and one in the third, and one in the fourth and one in the sixth, and the year is completed in three hundred and sixty-four days.$n$,false),
(22597,'S',82,7,82,7,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The seasons do not shift because the reckoning of the luminaries is exact and recorded (82:7); the moon and sun keep the courses they were appointed.$n$,$n$And the account thereof is accurate and the recorded reckoning thereof exact; for the luminaries, and months and festivals, and years and days, has Uriel shown and revealed to me, to whom Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the world hath subjected the host of heaven.$n$,false),
(22598,'S',82,7,82,7,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The luminaries do not alter their courses because their Maker fixed them for signs and seasons from creation — the exact account Uriel showed Enoch (82:7).$n$,$n$And the account thereof is accurate and the recorded reckoning thereof exact; for the luminaries, and months and festivals, and years and days, has Uriel shown and revealed to me, to whom Yahuah (Lord) of the whole creation of the world hath subjected the host of heaven.$n$,false),
(22593,'S',82,8,82,11,$n$Jubilees 6:17 — *For this reason it is ordained and written on the heavenly tables, that they should celebrate the feast of weeks in this month once a year, to renew the covenant every year...* The feasts governed by Enoch's leaders of the four parts of the year and the twelve orders of the months (82:11) are the heavenly-tablet appointments by which the covenant is renewed.$n$,$n$Their four leaders who divide the four parts of the year enter first; and after them the twelve leaders of the orders who divide the months; and for the three hundred and sixty (days) there are heads over thousands who divide the days; and for the four intercalary days there are the leaders which sunder the four parts of the year.$n$,false),
(22595,'S',82,8,82,11,$n$Leviticus 23:2 — *Speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), and say unto them, Concerning the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my feasts.* The leaders who divide the four parts of the year and the months (82:11) mark the appointed feasts of Yahuah (LORD), proclaimed by the lights.$n$,$n$Their four leaders who divide the four parts of the year enter first; and after them the twelve leaders of the orders who divide the months; and for the three hundred and sixty (days) there are heads over thousands who divide the days; and for the four intercalary days there are the leaders which sunder the four parts of the year.$n$,false),
(22594,'S',82,11,82,11,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The leaders who divide the parts of the year, the months and the days (82:11) keep the very signs and seasons set at creation.$n$,$n$Their four leaders who divide the four parts of the year enter first; and after them the twelve leaders of the orders who divide the months; and for the three hundred and sixty (days) there are heads over thousands who divide the days; and for the four intercalary days there are the leaders which sunder the four parts of the year.$n$,false),
(23818,'S',83,5,83,4,$n$Genesis 7:11 — *In the six hundredth year of Noah's life, in the second month, the seventeenth day of the month, the same day were all the fountains of the great deep broken up, and the windows of heaven were opened.* The broken-up deep is the great abyss that swallows the earth in Enoch's vision (83:4).$n$,$n$And when it fell to the earth I saw how the earth was swallowed up in a great abyss, and mountains were suspended on mountains, and hills sank down on hills, and high trees were rent from their stems, and hurled down and sunk in the abyss.$n$,false),
(23820,'S',83,5,83,4,$n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* The violence that fills the earth is the corruption Enoch sees punished when the earth is swallowed in the abyss at 83:4.$n$,$n$And when it fell to the earth I saw how the earth was swallowed up in a great abyss, and mountains were suspended on mountains, and hills sank down on hills, and high trees were rent from their stems, and hurled down and sunk in the abyss.$n$,false),
(23803,'S',83,6,83,7,$n$2 Peter 3:11 — *Seeing then that all these things shall be dissolved, what manner of persons ought ye to be in all holy conversation and godliness.* Peter turns the earth Enoch saw sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction (83:7) toward holy living, not toward law-as-curse.$n$,$n$And I recounted to him the whole vision which I had seen, and he said unto me: ‘A terrible thing hast thou seen, my son, and of grave moment is thy dream-vision as to the secrets of all the sin of the earth: it must sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction.$n$,false),
(23806,'S',83,6,83,7,$n$Matthew 24:37 — *But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be.* Yahusha (Jesus) makes the flood Mahalalel reads in Enoch's dream — the earth sinking into the abyss for the sin of the earth (83:7) — the type of the coming of the Son of Adam.$n$,$n$And I recounted to him the whole vision which I had seen, and he said unto me: ‘A terrible thing hast thou seen, my son, and of grave moment is thy dream-vision as to the secrets of all the sin of the earth: it must sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction.$n$,false),
(23805,'S',83,7,83,7,$n$Matthew 24:39 — *And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be.* The flood that takes all away is the great destruction Mahalalel names over Enoch's dream — the earth sinking into the abyss (83:7) — made the figure of the last day.$n$,$n$And I recounted to him the whole vision which I had seen, and he said unto me: ‘A terrible thing hast thou seen, my son, and of grave moment is thy dream-vision as to the secrets of all the sin of the earth: it must sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction.$n$,false),
(23817,'S',83,7,83,7,$n$Genesis 7:23 — *And every living substance was destroyed which was upon the face of the ground, both man, and cattle, and the creeping things, and the fowl of the heaven; and they were destroyed from the earth: and Noah only remained alive, and they that were with him in the ark.* The earth destroyed with a great destruction for the sin of the earth (83:7) is the deluge that left only Noah's house alive.$n$,$n$And I recounted to him the whole vision which I had seen, and he said unto me: ‘A terrible thing hast thou seen, my son, and of grave moment is thy dream-vision as to the secrets of all the sin of the earth: it must sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction.$n$,false),
(23819,'S',83,7,83,7,$n$Genesis 6:13 — *And Elohim (God) said unto Noah, The end of all flesh is come before me; for the earth is filled with violence through them; and, behold, I will destroy them with the earth.* The sin of the earth that sinks it into the abyss (83:7) is this very decree against all flesh.$n$,$n$And I recounted to him the whole vision which I had seen, and he said unto me: ‘A terrible thing hast thou seen, my son, and of grave moment is thy dream-vision as to the secrets of all the sin of the earth: it must sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction.$n$,false),
(23804,'S',83,9,83,8,$n$Genesis 8:1 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the cattle that was with him in the ark: and Elohim (God) made a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged.* The remembering of Noah is the answer to Enoch's prayer that the whole earth not be destroyed (83:8) — a seed preserved through the waters.$n$,$n$And now, my son, arise and make petition to Yahuah (Lord) of glory, since thou art a believer, that a remnant may remain on the earth, and that He may not destroy the whole earth.$n$,false),
(23807,'S',83,9,83,8,$n$Amos 7:6 — *Yahuah (LORD) repented for this: This also shall not be, saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD).* Yahuah relents at the prophet's plea, the very answer Enoch's intercession seeks when he prays the earth be spared (83:8).$n$,$n$And now, my son, arise and make petition to Yahuah (Lord) of glory, since thou art a believer, that a remnant may remain on the earth, and that He may not destroy the whole earth.$n$,false),
(23808,'S',83,9,83,8,$n$Amos 7:5 — *Then said I, O Yahuah (Lord) GOD, cease, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he is small.* The prophet's intercession for the small remnant echoes Enoch praying that the whole earth not be destroyed (83:8).$n$,$n$And now, my son, arise and make petition to Yahuah (Lord) of glory, since thou art a believer, that a remnant may remain on the earth, and that He may not destroy the whole earth.$n$,false),
(23814,'S',83,10,83,4,$n$Revelation 6:14 — *And the heaven departed as a scroll when it is rolled together; and every mountain and island were moved out of their places.* The sixth seal's mountains and islands moved out of their places is Enoch's dream — mountains suspended on mountains, hills sinking on hills, as the earth is swallowed in the abyss (83:4).$n$,$n$And when it fell to the earth I saw how the earth was swallowed up in a great abyss, and mountains were suspended on mountains, and hills sank down on hills, and high trees were rent from their stems, and hurled down and sunk in the abyss.$n$,false),
(23815,'S',83,10,83,4,$n$Isaiah 34:4 — *And all the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a scroll: and all their host shall fall down, as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling fig from the fig tree.* Isaiah's unmaking on the Day of Yahuah (the LORD) — the host falling as leaves from the vine — is the unmaking Enoch dreamed: the earth swallowed in the abyss and the mountains hurled down (83:4).$n$,$n$And when it fell to the earth I saw how the earth was swallowed up in a great abyss, and mountains were suspended on mountains, and hills sank down on hills, and high trees were rent from their stems, and hurled down and sunk in the abyss.$n$,false),
(23900,'S',89,16,89,16,$n$Exodus 3:8 — *And I am come down to deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians, and to bring them up out of that land unto a good land and a large, unto a land flowing with milk and honey...* The Lord of the sheep descending at the voice of the sheep from a lofty abode and pasturing them (89:16) is Yahuah (LORD) come down to deliver Israel.$n$,$n$And a sheep which had been saved from the wolves fled and escaped to the wild asses; and I saw the sheep how they lamented and cried, and besought their Lord with all their might, till that Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep descended at the voice of the sheep from a lofty abode, and came to them and pastured them.$n$,false),
(23904,'S',89,16,89,16,$n$Exodus 19:4 — *Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles' wings, and brought you unto myself.* The Lord of the sheep coming down to the sheep that cried to him (89:16) is Yahuah (LORD) bearing Israel on eagles' wings to himself.$n$,$n$And a sheep which had been saved from the wolves fled and escaped to the wild asses; and I saw the sheep how they lamented and cried, and besought their Lord with all their might, till that Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep descended at the voice of the sheep from a lofty abode, and came to them and pastured them.$n$,false),
(23901,'S',89,18,89,23,$n$Exodus 14:21 — *And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and Yahuah (LORD) caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided.* The wolves pursuing the sheep till they reached a sea of water (89:23) is Pharaoh's pursuit broken at the divided sea.$n$,$n$But the wolves began to pursue those sheep till they reached a sea of water.$n$,false),
(23902,'S',89,19,89,26,$n$Exodus 14:28 — *And the waters returned, and covered the chariots, and the horsemen, and all the host of Pharaoh that came into the sea after them; there remained not so much as one of them.* The sea gathering itself together and rising till it covered the wolves (89:26) is the host of Pharaoh drowned in the returning sea.$n$,$n$And when they saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, they turned to flee before His face, but that sea gathered itself together, and became as it had been created, and the water swelled and rose till it covered those wolves.$n$,false),
(23903,'S',89,19,89,27,$n$Exodus 14:30 — *Thus Yahuah (LORD) saved Yashar'el (Israel) that day out of the hand of the Egyptians; and Yashar'el (Israel) saw the Egyptians dead upon the sea shore.* All the wolves who pursued the sheep perished and were drowned (89:27) — Yahuah (LORD) himself saved Israel out of Egypt's hand.$n$,$n$And I saw till all the wolves who pursued those sheep perished and were drowned.$n$,false),
(23905,'S',89,23,89,30,$n$Exodus 19:18 — *And mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke, because Yahuah (LORD) descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.* The Lord of the sheep standing before them, great and terrible and majestic, so that all the sheep were afraid before his face (89:30), is Sinai, where Yahuah (LORD) descended in fire.$n$,$n$And after that I saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep who stood before them, and His appearance was great and terrible and majestic, and all those sheep saw Him and were afraid before His face.$n$,false),
(23907,'S',89,23,89,28,$n$Exodus 24:8 — *And Moses took the blood, and sprinkled it on the people, and said, Behold the blood of the covenant, which Yahuah (LORD) hath made with you concerning all these words.* The sheep whose eyes began to open in the wilderness, pastured by the Lord of the sheep himself (89:28), are the people brought to the covenant he would seal with blood.$n$,$n$But the sheep escaped from that water and went forth into a wilderness, where there was no water and no grass; and they began to open their eyes and to see; and I saw Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep pasturing them and giving them water and grass, and that sheep going and leading them.$n$,false),
(23911,'S',89,34,89,55,$n$Ezekiel 34:5 — *And they were scattered, because there is no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.* The wild beasts tearing the sheep in pieces (89:55) is Ezekiel's flock made meat to the beasts of the field.$n$,$n$And He gave them over into the hands of the lions and tigers, and wolves and hyenas, and into the hand of the foxes, and to all the wild beasts, and those wild beasts began to tear in pieces those sheep.$n$,false),
(23909,'S',89,35,89,56,$n$2 Kings 17:6 — *In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria, and carried Yashar'el (Israel) away into Assyria, and placed them in Halah and in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.* The house and tower forsaken and the sheep given into the hand of the lions (89:56) is the northern house carried away into Assyria.$n$,$n$And I saw that He forsook that their house and their tower and gave them all into the hand of the lions, to tear and devour them, into the hand of all the wild beasts.$n$,false),
(23910,'S',89,35,89,58,$n$2 Kings 17:23 — *Until Yahuah (LORD) removed Yashar'el (Israel) out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Yashar'el (Israel) carried away out of their own land to Assyria unto this day.* The Lord of the sheep unmoved while the sheep are devoured and robbed (89:58) is Yahuah (LORD) removing Israel out of his sight for breaking the covenant.$n$,$n$But He remained unmoved, though He saw it, and rejoiced that they were devoured and swallowed and robbed, and left them to be devoured in the hand of all the beasts.$n$,false),
(23912,'S',89,35,89,57,$n$Psalm 80:1 — *Give ear, O Shepherd of Yashar'el (Israel), thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest between the cherubims, shine forth.* Enoch crying to the Lord of the sheep that they were devoured by all the wild beasts (89:57) is the cry to the Shepherd of Israel to shine forth on Joseph's scattered flock.$n$,$n$And I began to cry aloud with all my power, and to appeal to Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, and to represent to Him in regard to the sheep that they were devoured by all the wild beasts.$n$,false),
(23917,'S',89,41,90,20,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The throne erected and the sealed books opened before the Lord of the sheep (90:20) is Daniel's judgment set and the books opened.$n$,$n$And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.$n$,false),
(23918,'S',89,41,90,20,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The sealed books opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne (90:20) is the white-throne judgment with the books opened.$n$,$n$And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.$n$,false),
(23913,'S',89,45,90,25,$n$Ezekiel 34:2 — *Son of Adam, prophesy against the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel)... Woe be to the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel) that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?* The seventy shepherds judged and found guilty and cast into the fiery abyss (90:25) are Ezekiel's self-feeding shepherds of Israel.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$,false),
(23914,'S',89,45,90,25,$n$Ezekiel 34:10 — *Behold, I am against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock... for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.* The judgment of the shepherds and their casting into the abyss (90:25) is Yahuah requiring His flock at the false shepherds' hand.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$,false),
(23915,'S',89,45,90,25,$n$Jeremiah 23:1 — *Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds judged for not feeding the sheep (90:25) are Jeremiah's pastors who destroy and scatter the flock.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$,false),
(23916,'S',89,45,90,25,$n$Zechariah 11:17 — *Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword shall be upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.* The shepherds cast into the fiery abyss (90:25) are Zechariah's worthless idol shepherd who abandons the flock of slaughter.$n$,$n$And those seventy shepherds were judged and found guilty, and they were cast into that fiery abyss.$n$,false),
(23933,'S',90,16,89,74,$n$Jeremiah 23:1 — *Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds to whom the sheep were delivered for destruction, who trampled and devoured them (89:74), are the pastors woed for destroying and scattering the flock.$n$,$n$And as touching all this the eyes of those sheep were blinded so that they saw not, and (the eyes of) their shepherds likewise; and they delivered them in large numbers to their shepherds for destruction, and they trampled the sheep with their feet and devoured them.$n$,false),
(23934,'S',90,16,89,74,$n$Jeremiah 23:2 — *Therefore thus saith Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Yashar'el (Israel) against the pastors that feed my people; Ye have scattered my flock, and driven them away, and have not visited them: behold, I will visit upon you the evil of your doings, saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds who trampled the sheep with their feet and devoured them (89:74) are visited for scattering and not visiting the flock.$n$,$n$And as touching all this the eyes of those sheep were blinded so that they saw not, and (the eyes of) their shepherds likewise; and they delivered them in large numbers to their shepherds for destruction, and they trampled the sheep with their feet and devoured them.$n$,false),
(23935,'S',90,16,89,74,$n$Zechariah 11:17 — *Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword shall be upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.* The blinded shepherds who destroyed the sheep delivered to them (89:74) answer the woe on the idol shepherd who leaves the flock.$n$,$n$And as touching all this the eyes of those sheep were blinded so that they saw not, and (the eyes of) their shepherds likewise; and they delivered them in large numbers to their shepherds for destruction, and they trampled the sheep with their feet and devoured them.$n$,false),
(23919,'S',89,46,90,29,$n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar'el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all:* The new house gathering all the sheep (90:29) is the two houses made one nation under one king, the regathering.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$,false),
(23920,'S',89,46,90,29,$n$Isaiah 11:12 — *And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth.* The Lord bringing all the sheep into the new house (90:29) is the assembling of the outcasts of Israel and dispersed of Judah.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$,false),
(23921,'S',89,46,90,29,$n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.* The new house greater and loftier than the first (90:29) is the New Jerusalem coming down from heaven.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$,false),
(23939,'S',90,17,90,29,$n$Ezekiel 37:26 — *Moreover I will make a covenant of peace with them; it shall be an everlasting covenant with them: and I will place them, and multiply them, and will set my sanctuary in the midst of them for evermore.* All the sheep brought into the new house is the everlasting sanctuary set in the midst of the regathered nation.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$,false),
(23940,'S',90,17,90,29,$n$Micah 4:1 — *But in the last days it shall come to pass, that the mountain of the house of Yahuah (LORD) shall be established in the top of the mountains, and it shall be exalted above the hills; and people shall flow unto it.* The new house built greater and loftier is the mountain of the house exalted in the last days.$n$,$n$And I saw till Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep brought a new house greater and loftier than that first, and set it up in the place of the first which had been folded up: all its pillars were new, and its ornaments were new and larger than those of the first, the old one which He had taken away, and all the sheep were within it.$n$,false),
(23937,'S',90,17,90,36,$n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.* The new house, large and broad and very full (90:36), is the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from heaven.$n$,$n$And I saw that that house was large and broad and very full.$n$,false),
(23925,'S',90,1,90,9,$n$1 Maccabees 2:66 — *As for Judas Maccabeus, he has been mighty and strong, even from his youth up: let him be your captain, and fight the battle of the people.* The great horn that sprouted on one of the sheep, whose eyes were opened (90:9), matches the mighty captain raised to fight the people's battle.$n$,$n$And I saw till horns grew upon those lambs, and the ravens cast down their horns; and I saw till there sprouted a great horn of one of those sheep, and their eyes were opened.$n$,false),
(23924,'S',90,3,90,10,$n$1 Maccabees 2:1 — *In those days arose Mattathias the son of John, the son of Simeon, a priest of the sons of Joarib, from Jerusalem, and dwelt in Modin.* The great horn that cried to the sheep so that the rams ran to it (90:10) is read first against the Maccabean priest-line raised up to rally a scattered Israel.$n$,$n$And it looked at them [and their eyes opened], and it cried to the sheep, and the rams saw it and all ran to it.$n$,false),
(23926,'S',90,4,90,38,$n$Jeremiah 23:5 — *Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth.* The Lord of the sheep rejoicing over the great one with the black horns and over all the oxen (90:38) points beyond the Maccabees to the righteous Branch raised to David.$n$,$n$And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.$n$,false),
(23927,'S',90,7,90,9,$n$Ezekiel 34:23 — *And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.* The great horn raised on one of the sheep (90:9), with help sent to it from heaven (90:14), is the Lord's setting up of the one Davidic shepherd over the flock.$n$,$n$And I saw till horns grew upon those lambs, and the ravens cast down their horns; and I saw till there sprouted a great horn of one of those sheep, and their eyes were opened.$n$,false),
(23929,'S',90,11,90,38,$n$John 10:11 — *I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.* The Lord of the sheep rejoicing over the great one and over all the oxen (90:38) is the good shepherd who laid down his life for his own, now rejoicing over them.$n$,$n$And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.$n$,false),
(23930,'S',90,12,90,20,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The throne erected in the pleasant land, the Lord of the sheep seated on it, and the sealed books opened before him (90:20) is the Ancient of days seated for judgment.$n$,$n$And I saw till a throne was erected in the pleasant land, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep sat Himself thereon, and the other took the sealed books and opened those books before Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep.$n$,false),
(23931,'S',90,12,90,24,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The judgment held first over the stars, judged and found guilty and cast into the abyss of fire (90:24), is Daniel's set judgment with the books opened — the books of 90:20 opened and the sentence read.$n$,$n$And the judgement was held first over the stars, and they were judged and found guilty, and went to the place of condemnation, and they were cast into an abyss, full of fire and flaming, and full of pillars of fire.$n$,false),
(23932,'S',90,12,90,26,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The blinded sheep judged and found guilty and cast into the fiery abyss (90:26) is the white-throne judgment where the dead are judged by what is written in the books.$n$,$n$And I saw at that time how a like abyss was opened in the midst of the earth, full of fire, and they brought those blinded sheep, and they were all judged and found guilty and cast into this fiery abyss, and they burned; now this abyss was to the right of that house.$n$,false),
(23936,'S',90,15,90,24,$n$Revelation 20:10 — *And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.* The stars judged and found guilty and cast into an abyss full of fire and pillars of fire (90:24) are the deceiving powers consigned to the lake of fire.$n$,$n$And the judgement was held first over the stars, and they were judged and found guilty, and went to the place of condemnation, and they were cast into an abyss, full of fire and flaming, and full of pillars of fire.$n$,false),
(23943,'S',90,18,90,33,$n$Ezekiel 37:21 — *And say unto them, Thus saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD); Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land:* All that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in that house (90:33) is the regathering of scattered Israel from the heathen into their land.$n$,$n$And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.$n$,false),
(23938,'S',90,19,90,33,$n$Revelation 21:3 — *And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of Elohim (God) is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God).* The sheep returned to His house is the tabernacle of God dwelling with His people.$n$,$n$And all that had been destroyed and dispersed, and all the beasts of the field, and all the birds of the heaven, assembled in that house, and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced with great joy because they were all good and had returned to His house.$n$,false),
(25342,'S',94,4,97,8,$n$Luke 12:20 — *But Elohim (God) said unto him, Thou fool, this night thy soul shall be required of thee: then whose shall those things be, which thou hast provided?* Yahusha's (Jesus's) rich fool meets the same reckoning Enoch announces on those who say *we have become rich with riches and have possessions* (97:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25344,'S',94,5,100,6,$n$Psalm 49:7 — *None of them can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to Elohim (God) a ransom for him:* Riches cannot ransom a man — exactly what Enoch says the children of the earth will come to recognize: *their riches shall not be able to save them in the overthrow of their sins* (100:6).$n$,$n$And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.$n$,false),
(25365,'S',95,1,99,1,$n$Luke 6:24 — *But woe unto you that are rich! for ye have received your consolation.* — Yahusha (Jesus) takes up the same prophetic woe-form Enoch uses, pronouncing loss on those whose consolation is already spent.$n$,$n$Woe to you who work godlessness, And glory in lying and extol them: Ye shall perish, and no happy life shall be yours.$n$,false),
(25366,'S',95,1,99,1,$n$Isaiah 5:21 — *Woe unto them that are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!* — the self-wise who glory in their own lying are the godless of Enoch 99:1 who shall find no good.$n$,$n$Woe to you who work godlessness, And glory in lying and extol them: Ye shall perish, and no happy life shall be yours.$n$,false),
(25367,'S',95,2,99,2,$n$Isaiah 5:20 — *Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!* Isaiah's woe against inverting the moral order is Enoch's woe on those who pervert the words of uprightness and transgress the eternal law (99:2).$n$,$n$Woe to them who pervert the words of uprightness, And transgress the eternal law, And transform themselves into what they were not [into sinners]: They shall be trodden under foot upon the earth.$n$,false),
(25368,'S',96,1,96,5,$n$Amos 5:11 — *Forasmuch therefore as your treading is upon the poor, and ye take from him burdens of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink wine of them.* The prophet's word for the very treading-and-feasting Enoch condemns in 96:5, and the houses the oppressors shall not keep.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25370,'S',96,1,96,5,$n$Isaiah 3:14 — *Yahuah (LORD) will enter into judgment with the ancients of his people, and the princes thereof: for ye have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor is in your houses.* Those who devour the might of others and eat the best food (96:5) are the very princes who have eaten up the vineyard.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25373,'S',96,2,96,8,$n$Luke 6:24 — *But woe unto you that are rich! for ye have received your consolation.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) woe on the rich is the sentence Enoch pronounces on the mighty who oppress the righteous with their might: *the day of your destruction is coming* (96:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25375,'S',96,2,96,8,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James opens his woe on the rich where Enoch does — the mighty who oppress the righteous, whose day of destruction is coming (96:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25376,'S',96,2,96,8,$n$James 5:3 — *Your gold and silver is cankered; and the rust of them shall be a witness against you, and shall eat your flesh as it were fire. Ye have heaped treasure together for the last days.* The cankering of hoarded wealth is how James shows the day of destruction Enoch warns the mighty of (96:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25374,'S',96,3,96,5,$n$Luke 6:25 — *Woe unto you that are full! for ye shall hunger. Woe unto you that laugh now! for ye shall mourn and weep.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) woe on the full is Enoch's woe on those who devour the finest of the wheat and drink wine in large bowls while treading the lowly under foot (96:5).$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25377,'S',96,3,96,5,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:8 — *What has pride profited us? or what good has riches with our vaunting brought us?* Wisdom voices the doomed rich confessing the emptiness of their feasting — the finest of the wheat and the wine in large bowls Enoch's woe names (96:5).$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25378,'S',96,7,97,9,$n$Luke 12:18 — *And he said, This will I do: I will pull down my barns, and build greater; and there will I bestow all my fruits and my goods.* The rich fool's brimming barns are the very granaries Enoch's hoarders boast of in 97:9.$n$,$n$And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,$n$,false),
(25382,'S',96,7,97,9,$n$Amos 8:6 — *That we may buy the poor for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes; yea, and sell the refuse of the wheat?* The wheat hoarded in Enoch's full granaries (97:9) is the same refuse Amos says was sold by defrauding the needy.$n$,$n$And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,$n$,false),
(25383,'S',96,8,96,8,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The mighty who oppress the righteous with their might (96:8) are James's rich men whose withheld wages cry to Yahuah (Lord) of hosts.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25385,'S',96,8,96,8,$n$Ecclesiasticus 34:22 — *He that takes away his neighbour's living slayeth him; and he that defraudeth the labourer of his hire is a bloodshedder.* Ben Sira makes defrauding the labourer a deed of blood — the oppression of the righteous by might that Enoch's woe names (96:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye mighty, Who with might oppress the righteous; For the day of your destruction is coming. In those days many and good days shall come to the righteous—in the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25475,'S',102,1,102,1,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *...and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* When he brings a grievous fire and there is nowhere to flee (102:1), Daniel's deliverance belongs to every one found written in the book — the deciding line is the name already written, election before any confession.$n$,$n$In those days when He hath brought a grievous fire upon you, Whither will ye flee, and where will ye find deliverance? And when He launches forth His word against you Will you not be affrighted and fear?$n$,false),
(25477,'S',102,1,102,6,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:2 — *In the sight of the unwise they seemed to die: and their departure is taken for misery,* Wisdom's unwise who take the righteous death for misery are Enoch's sinners speaking over the righteous dead — *as we die, so die the righteous, and what benefit do they reap for their deeds?* (102:6). The world reads that death as defeat and cannot see the path that runs through it.$n$,$n$And yet when ye die the sinners speak over you: ‘As we die, so die the righteous, And what benefit do they reap for their deeds?$n$,false),
(25473,'S',102,2,22,9,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The division made in Sheol between the spirits of the righteous and the rest (22:9) is Daniel's two-fold awakening — life for the one, shame for the other.$n$,$n$And he answered me and said unto me: ‘These three have been made that the spirits of the dead might be separated. And such a division has been made for the spirits of the righteous, in which there is the bright spring of water.$n$,false),
(25476,'S',102,3,102,4,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:4 — *For though they be punished in the sight of men, yet is their hope full of immortality.* The hope full of immortality is Enoch's word to the righteous dead: fear not, and be hopeful, ye that have died in righteousness (102:4) — punished in the world's eyes, kept whole before him.$n$,$n$Fear ye not, ye souls of the righteous, And be hopeful ye that have died in righteousness.$n$,false),
(25478,'S',102,3,102,4,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 — *But the souls of the righteous are in the hand of Yahuah (God), and there shall no torment touch them.* Wisdom's souls of the righteous in the hand of Elohim (God) are the souls Enoch tells not to fear, that have died in righteousness (102:4) — grieve not that the body went into Sheol; wait for the day.$n$,$n$Fear ye not, ye souls of the righteous, And be hopeful ye that have died in righteousness.$n$,false),
(25471,'S',102,6,102,6,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach:* The mockers who spoke over the righteous dead — *as we die, so die the righteous* (102:6) — seen now from the other side: the despisers confessing too late.$n$,$n$And yet when ye die the sinners speak over you: ‘As we die, so die the righteous, And what benefit do they reap for their deeds?$n$,false),
(25463,'S',102,7,58,3,$n$Malachi 4:2 — *But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.* The righteous in the light of the sun, the elect in the light of eternal life (58:3), meet the Sun of righteousness who rises for those who fear Yahuah's (the LORD's) name — the other end from the furnace.$n$,$n$And the righteous shall be in the light of the sun, And the elect in the light of eternal life: The days of their life shall be unending, And the days of the holy without number.$n$,false),
(25470,'S',102,7,104,2,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:5 — *How is he numbered among the children of Yahuah (God), and his lot is among the saints!* The righteous shining as the lights of heaven, seen at last with the portals of heaven opened to them (104:2), is this very cry — the despised found among the elect.$n$,$n$Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.$n$,false),
(25472,'S',102,7,108,14,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) own words for the harvest's end render Enoch's close: those born in darkness led into darkness, while the righteous shall be resplendent (108:14).$n$,$n$And they shall see those who were born in darkness led into darkness, while the righteous shall be resplendent.$n$,false),
(25474,'S',102,7,104,2,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* Enoch's righteous who shall shine as the lights of heaven (104:2) are Daniel's resurrection-radiance of the wise.$n$,$n$Be hopeful; for aforetime ye were put to shame through ill and affliction; but now ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen, and the portals of heaven shall be opened to you.$n$,false),
(25491,'S',103,3,103,3,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *And I heard a voice from heaven saying unto me, Write, Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The blessing on the righteous dead — all goodness and joy and glory prepared and written down for the spirits of those who have died in righteousness (103:3).$n$,$n$That all goodness and joy and glory are prepared for them, And written down for the spirits of those who have died in righteousness, And that manifold good shall be given to you in recompense for your labours, And that your lot is abundantly beyond the lot of the living.$n$,false),
(25493,'S',103,3,103,3,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The book of remembrance is the same heavenly register where Enoch sees goodness and glory written down for the spirits of those who died in righteousness (103:3).$n$,$n$That all goodness and joy and glory are prepared for them, And written down for the spirits of those who have died in righteousness, And that manifold good shall be given to you in recompense for your labours, And that your lot is abundantly beyond the lot of the living.$n$,false),
(25496,'S',103,4,103,4,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) confirms what Enoch promises under oath: the spirits of those who died in righteousness shall live and rejoice and their memorial shall not perish (103:4) — the righteous shining in the Father's kingdom.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25497,'S',103,4,103,4,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* The spirits of the righteous dead that shall live and rejoice before the face of the Great One (103:4) are Daniel's wise, shining as the firmament.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25498,'S',103,4,103,4,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The awakening Daniel sees is the very life Enoch swears the righteous spirits shall not lose (103:4).$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25494,'S',103,7,103,4,$n$The Wisdom of Solomon 3:4 — *For though they be punished in the sight of men, yet is their hope full of immortality.* The hope full of immortality is the life Enoch swears the righteous dead shall have — their spirits shall live and rejoice and not perish (103:4).$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25495,'S',103,7,103,4,$n$The Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 — *But the souls of the righteous are in the hand of Yahuah (God), and there shall no torment touch them.* The same safekeeping of the righteous spirits: they shall live and rejoice, and their memorial shall not perish from before the face of the Great One (103:4).$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25487,'S',103,9,108,3,$n$Revelation 20:15 — *And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.* The end of those whose names are blotted out of the book of life (108:3): their seed destroyed, their spirits slain, and the fire — the same end for the unwritten.$n$,$n$And wait ye indeed till sin has passed away, for their names shall be blotted out of the book of life and out of the holy books, and their seed shall be destroyed for ever, and their spirits shall be slain, and they shall cry and make lamentation in a place that is a chaotic wilderness, and in the fire shall they burn; for there is no earth there.$n$,false),
(25492,'S',103,9,104,7,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The sinners say their sins will not be searched out and written down; Enoch answers that they are written down every day (104:7). John's opened books are those records.$n$,$n$And, although ye sinners say: “All our sins shall not be searched out and be written down,” nevertheless they shall write down all your sins every day.$n$,false),
(25488,'S',103,10,103,8,$n$Luke 16:24 — *And he cried and said, Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water, and cool my tongue; for I am tormented in this flame.* The cry from the flame is the cry Enoch hears from the darkness and chains and burning flame where the sinners' spirits enter (103:8).$n$,$n$And into darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgement shall your spirits enter; And the great judgement shall be for all the generations of the world. Woe to you, for ye shall have no peace.$n$,false),
(25489,'S',103,10,103,8,$n$Luke 16:23 — *And in hell he lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Abraham afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom.* The torment-side of Sheol is the darkness and chains and burning flame where Enoch says the sinners' spirits enter, where there is grievous judgment (103:8).$n$,$n$And into darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgement shall your spirits enter; And the great judgement shall be for all the generations of the world. Woe to you, for ye shall have no peace.$n$,false),
(25510,'S',104,3,104,1,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* Deliverance belongs to every one written in the book — Enoch's righteous whose names are written before the glory of the Great One (104:1).$n$,$n$I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.$n$,false),
(25511,'S',104,3,104,1,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The book of remembrance is the same heavenly register where the names of the righteous are written before the glory of the Great One (104:1).$n$,$n$I swear unto you, that in heaven the angels remember you for good before the glory of the Great One: and your names are written before the glory of the Great One.$n$,false),
(25513,'S',104,4,104,4,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) seals Enoch's promise: the righteous shine in the Father's kingdom — great joy as the angels of heaven (104:4).$n$,$n$Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.$n$,false),
(25514,'S',104,4,104,4,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* The great joy as the angels of heaven Enoch promises the righteous (104:4) is Daniel's wise shining as the firmament.$n$,$n$Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.$n$,false),
(25515,'S',104,4,104,4,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The awakening of the dust-sleepers is the very resurrection Enoch promises the righteous in 104:2–5 — hope not cast away, joy as the angels (104:4).$n$,$n$Be hopeful, and cast not away your hope; for ye shall have great joy as the angels of heaven.$n$,false),
(25512,'S',104,5,104,5,$n$the Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* Wisdom's righteous shining at their visitation are Enoch's righteous who will not have to hide on the day of the great judgment and will not be found as sinners (104:5).$n$,$n$What shall ye be obliged to do? Ye shall not have to hide on the day of the great judgement and ye shall not be found as sinners, and the eternal judgement shall be far from you for all the generations of the world.$n$,false),
(25508,'S',104,8,103,4,$n$Revelation 3:5 — *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) promise not to blot the overcomer's name is Enoch's memorial that shall not perish from before the face of the Great One (103:4).$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25509,'S',104,8,103,4,$n$Psalm 69:28 — *Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.* Enoch's righteous memorial shall NOT perish before the Great One (103:4); the wicked are blotted, never the elect written-in.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25506,'S',104,9,98,8,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* John's opened books are the records Enoch names: all your oppression written down every day till the day of your judgment (98:8).$n$,$n$From henceforth ye know that all your oppression wherewith ye oppress is written down every day till the day of your judgement.$n$,false),
(25505,'S',104,12,103,8,$n$Revelation 20:15 — *And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.* The fire that receives the unwritten is the darkness and chains and burning flame Enoch's sinners enter, where there is grievous judgment (103:8).$n$,$n$And into darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgement shall your spirits enter; And the great judgement shall be for all the generations of the world. Woe to you, for ye shall have no peace.$n$,false),
(25529,'S',105,1,103,8,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* The sinner's end — darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgment (103:8) — is the canon's furnace into which the tares of the seed-war are gathered.$n$,$n$And into darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgement shall your spirits enter; And the great judgement shall be for all the generations of the world. Woe to you, for ye shall have no peace.$n$,false),
(25530,'S',105,2,103,4,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The memorial before the face of the Great One (103:4) is deliverance for every name already written in the book — election before the trouble, not after.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(25531,'S',105,2,103,4,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The righteous whose memorial does not perish before the face of the Great One (103:4) are the ones in the book of remembrance kept for those who fear him.$n$,$n$And the spirits of you who have died in righteousness shall live and rejoice, And their spirits shall not perish, nor their memorial from before the face of the Great One Unto all the generations of the world: wherefore no longer fear their contumely.$n$,false),
(16053,'S',8,2,8,4,$n$Exodus 2:23 — *And it came to pass in process of time, that the king of Egypt died: and the children of Yashar'el (Israel) sighed by reason of the bondage, and they cried, and their cry came up unto Elohim (God) by reason of the bondage.* The cry going up to heaven in 1 Enoch 8:4 is the same cry of the oppressed that comes up unto Elohim and moves Him to deliver.$n$,$n$And as men perished, they cried, and their cry went up to heaven...$n$,false),
(16054,'S',8,2,8,4,$n$Genesis 4:10 — *And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother's blood crieth unto me from the ground.* The cry of those perishing that goes up to heaven in 1 Enoch 8:4 is the same cry of innocent blood that the LORD hears from the ground.$n$,$n$And as men perished, they cried, and their cry went up to heaven...$n$,false),
(16060,'S',8,2,8,3,$n$Jubilees 8:3 — *And he found a writing which former (generations) had carved on the rock, and he read what was thereon, and he transcribed it and sinned owing to it; for it contained the teaching of the Watchers in accordance with which they used to observe the omens of the sun and moon and stars in all the signs of heaven.* Jubilees traces the very star-lore of 1 Enoch 8:3 to a surviving Watcher-tablet that re-corrupted men after the Flood.$n$,$n$Semjâzâ taught enchantments, and root-cuttings, Armârôs the resolving of enchantments, Barâqîjâl (taught) astrology, Kôkabêl the constellations, Êzêqêêl the knowledge of the clouds, Araqiêl the signs of the earth, Shamsiêl the signs of the sun, and Sariêl the course of the moon.$n$,false),
(16061,'S',8,2,8,3,$n$Jeremiah 10:2 — *Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), Learn not the way of the heathen, and be not dismayed at the signs of heaven; for the heathen are dismayed at them.* The astrology and the signs of the sun and moon that the Watchers teach in 1 Enoch 8:3 are exactly the signs of heaven the prophet warns Yashar'el not to learn.$n$,$n$Semjâzâ taught enchantments, and root-cuttings, Armârôs the resolving of enchantments, Barâqîjâl (taught) astrology, Kôkabêl the constellations, Êzêqêêl the knowledge of the clouds, Araqiêl the signs of the earth, Shamsiêl the signs of the sun, and Sariêl the course of the moon.$n$,false),
(16686,'S',18,12,18,14,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* Isaiah's prison-pit, holding the host until they are visited, is Enoch's prison for the stars and the host of heaven (18:14), bound till their guilt is consummated (18:14).$n$,$n$The angel said: ‘This place is the end of heaven and earth: this has become a prison for the stars and the host of heaven.$n$,false),
(16687,'S',18,12,18,15,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* The host of the high ones Isaiah sees punished are the stars Enoch saw rolling over the fire — the ones who transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) and did not come forth at their appointed times (18:15).$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$,false),
(16768,'S',25,5,25,5,$n$Isaiah 65:22 — *They shall not build, and another inhabit; they shall not plant, and another eat: for as the days of a tree are the days of my people, and mine elect shall long enjoy the work of their hands.* Isaiah measures the elect's days by a tree, exactly as Enoch's tree gives *fruit shall be for food to the elect* (25:5).$n$,$n$Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.$n$,false),
(16769,'S',25,5,25,5,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The right to Enoch's reserved tree of life (25:5) belongs to those who do Yahuah's commandments — Torah standing, the elect keeping the way into the holy place.$n$,$n$Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.$n$,false),
(16770,'S',25,5,25,5,$n$2 Esdras 8:52 — *For to you is paradise opened, the tree of life is planted, the time to come is prepared, plenteousness is made ready, a city is builded, and rest is allowed, yes, perfect goodness and wisdom.* 2 Esdras pairs the planted tree of life with the builded city exactly as Enoch's tree is transplanted to the holy place, the temple of the Eternal King (25:5).$n$,$n$Its fruit shall be for food to the elect: it shall be transplanted to the holy place, to the temple of Yahuah (Lord), the Eternal King.$n$,false),
(17164,'S',27,2,25,3,$n$Zechariah 14:4 — *And his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives, which is before Jerusalem on the east, and the mount of Olives shall cleave in the midst thereof toward the east and toward the west, and there shall be a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.* Zechariah's day of the King standing on the mountain east of Jerusalem matches the mountain Michael names — the throne where the Holy Great One will sit when he comes down to visit the earth with goodness (25:3).$n$,$n$And he answered saying: ‘This high mountain which thou hast seen, whose summit is like the throne of Elohim (God), is His throne, where the Holy Great One, Yahuah (Lord) of Glory, the Eternal King, will sit, when He shall come down to visit the earth with goodness.$n$,false),
(17165,'S',27,2,26,2,$n$Ezekiel 47:1 — *Afterward he brought me again unto the door of the house; and, behold, waters issued out from under the threshold of the house eastward: for the forefront of the house stood toward the east, and the waters came down from under from the right side of the house, at the south side of the altar.* Ezekiel's eastward and southward sanctuary waters are the very streams Enoch sees flowing east and south from under the holy mountain.$n$,$n$And there I saw a holy mountain, and underneath the mountain to the east there was a stream and it flowed towards the south.$n$,false),
(17234,'S',33,3,72,3,$n$Jubilees 2:9 — *And Elohim (God) appointed the sun to be a great sign on the earth for days and for sabbaths and for months and for feasts and for years and for sabbaths of years and for jubilees and for all seasons of the years.* The same lights that pass through Enoch's portals are the appointed keepers of the feasts and jubilees — the calendar of Torah set in the heavens.$n$,$n$And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.$n$,false),
(17237,'S',33,3,72,3,$n$Psalm 19:5 — *Which is as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, and rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.* The sun that rises from Enoch's eastern portals is the same sun the psalmist sees set on its joyful, fixed course.$n$,$n$And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.$n$,false),
(17238,'S',33,3,72,3,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The sun and moon Enoch watches passing through the portals were appointed at creation for signs and seasons — the moedim.$n$,$n$And I saw six portals in which the sun rises, and six portals in which the sun sets: and the moon rises and sets in these portals, and the leaders of the stars and those whom they lead: six in the east and six in the west, and all following each other in accurately corresponding order: also many windows to the right and left of these portals.$n$,false),
(17951,'S',39,4,39,5,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The water-like righteousness flowing in 1 Enoch 39:5 has its source in the river that proceeds from the throne of the Father and the Lamb.$n$,$n$Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(17952,'S',39,4,39,5,$n$Amos 5:24 — *But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.* Amos's flowing waters of righteousness are the very stream Enoch sees pour before the holy in 1 Enoch 39:5.$n$,$n$Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(17958,'S',39,4,39,5,$n$Revelation 7:15 — *Therefore are they before the throne of Elohim (God), and serve him day and night in his temple: and he that sitteth on the throne shall dwell among them.* John sees the righteous lodged with the holy before the throne, the same resting-places among His angels that Enoch saw in 1 Enoch 39:5.$n$,$n$Here mine eyes saw their dwellings with His righteous angels, And their resting-places with the holy. And they petitioned and interceded and prayed for the children of men, And righteousness flowed before them as water, And mercy like dew upon the earth: Thus it is amongst them for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(18002,'S',51,4,51,4,$n$Psalm 114:4 — *The mountains skipped like rams, and the little hills like lambs.* The Exodus-redemption image of leaping hills is the exact figure Enoch uses in 51:4 for creation rejoicing as the righteous are made victorious.$n$,$n$And in those days shall the mountains leap like rams, And the hills also shall skip like lambs satisfied with milk, And the faces of [all] the angels in heaven shall be lighted up with joy.$n$,false),
(19864,'S',53,6,53,5,$n$Revelation 19:20 — *These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.* The beast and false prophet — chief of the kings and mighty — are cast into the burning lake the instruments of 53:5 foretell.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘They prepare these for the kings and the mighty of this earth, that they may thereby be destroyed.$n$,false),
(19865,'S',53,6,53,5,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 6:6 — *For mercy will soon pardon the meanest: but mighty men shall be mightily tormented.* Wisdom weighs the sentence to the station exactly as 53:5 reserves the instruments for the kings, the mighty, and the exalted.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘They prepare these for the kings and the mighty of this earth, that they may thereby be destroyed.$n$,false),
(19867,'S',53,6,53,5,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* The furnace into which the workers of iniquity are cast is the destruction the instruments of 53:5 are prepared to accomplish.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘They prepare these for the kings and the mighty of this earth, that they may thereby be destroyed.$n$,false),
(19869,'S',53,6,53,5,$n$Isaiah 30:33 — *For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of Yahuah (LORD), like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it.* Isaiah's Tophet, prepared of old for the king, is the very deep furnace whose instruments the angels ready for the kings and mighty in 53:5.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘They prepare these for the kings and the mighty of this earth, that they may thereby be destroyed.$n$,false),
(19993,'S',62,1,62,5,$n$Matthew 25:31 — *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory.* The throne of glory the kings see that Son of Adam sitting on (62:5) is the very throne where Yahusha (Jesus), the Son of Adam, sits to sift the seed gathered out of all nations, the sheep from the goats.$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$,false),
(19994,'S',62,1,62,5,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* Daniel sees one *like* the Son of Adam brought near; Enoch names that same One — *that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory* (62:5). Keep the *like*: he resembles mortal man yet remains the Formed cloud-rider.$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$,false),
(19995,'S',62,1,61,8,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The Head of Days who names and seats the Elect One in Enoch 61:8 is Daniel's Ancient of days who sits before any other throne is given.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits placed the Elect One on the throne of glory. And he shall judge all the works of the holy above in the heaven, And in the balance shall their deeds be weighed.$n$,false),
(21279,'S',63,2,62,2,$n$Psalms 2:9 — *Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter's vessel.* The Anointed Son who breaks the rebellious kings is the Elect One whose mouth-word slays the sinners (62:2).$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$,false),
(21280,'S',63,2,62,2,$n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.* The word of His mouth that slays the sinners (62:2) is the rod-of-the-mouth of the Branch from Jesse's stem.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$,false),
(21282,'S',63,2,62,2,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* The Head of Days seating the Elect One on the throne of glory (62:2) is Daniel's Ancient of days bringing the one LIKE the Son of Adam near — Enoch names the figure Daniel sees by comparison.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.$n$,false),
(19991,'S',62,7,71,14,$n$Matthew 26:64 — *Yahusha (Jesus) saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.* Yahusha (Jesus) owns the very title the angel speaks over him in Enoch's vision: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness* (71:14) — named, not merely likened.$n$,$n$And he (i.e. the angel) came to me and greeted me with His voice, and said unto me: ‘This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness, And righteousness abides over him, And the righteousness of the Head of Days forsakes him not.’$n$,false),
(21348,'S',68,1,6,6,$n$Jubilees 5:1 — *the angels of Elohim (God) saw them on a certain year of this jubilee, that they were beautiful to look upon; and they took themselves wives of all whom they chose, and they bare to them sons and they were giants.* Jubilees tells the same descent, fixing it in its jubilee-reckoning.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$,false),
(21352,'S',68,1,6,6,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* The very descent Enoch's roster commemorates is Moses' own account of the sons of Elohim taking wives.$n$,$n$And they were in all two hundred; who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon, and they called it Mount Hermon, because they had sworn and bound themselves by mutual imprecations upon it.$n$,false),
(23845,'S',85,8,85,9,$n$Hebrews 11:5 — *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because Elohim (God) had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased Elohim (God).* The white bulls proceeding one from another are the righteous line — Enoch among them — that runs from Seth toward the great white bull at the vision's end.$n$,$n$And I saw in my sleep that white bull likewise grow and become a great white bull, and from him proceeded many white bulls, and they resembled him.$n$,false),
(23906,'S',89,21,89,36,$n$Exodus 19:6 — *And ye shall be unto me a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel).* The sheep placed in the great house built for the Lord of the sheep (89:36) is Israel made a kingdom of priests and holy nation at the covenant.$n$,$n$And I saw in this vision till that sheep became a man and built a house for Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, and placed all the sheep in that house.$n$,false),
(23908,'S',89,21,89,36,$n$1 Kings 6:1 — *And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Yashar'el (Israel) were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon's reign over Yashar'el (Israel)... that he began to build the house of Yahuah (LORD).* The great house built for the Lord of the sheep (89:36) is fulfilled in the house of Yahuah, the temple.$n$,$n$And I saw in this vision till that sheep became a man and built a house for Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep, and placed all the sheep in that house.$n$,false),
(25341,'S',94,3,94,8,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James pronounces Enoch's identical woe on the rich whose wealth will fail them (94:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.$n$,false),
(25343,'S',94,3,94,8,$n$Psalm 49:17 — *For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.* The rich man departs from his riches at death, just as Enoch warns 'from your riches shall you depart' (94:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.$n$,false),
(25345,'S',94,3,94,8,$n$Psalm 49:6 — *They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;* the very posture Enoch condemns — trusting in riches instead of remembering the God of Spirits (94:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye rich, for ye have trusted in your riches, And from your riches shall ye depart, Because ye have not remembered the El Elyon (Most High) in the days of your riches.$n$,false),
(25335,'S',94,6,94,7,$n$Isaiah 5:8 — *Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!* Isaiah's woe on those who join house to house is Enoch's woe on those who build their houses with sin (94:7).$n$,$n$Woe to those who build their houses with sin; For from all their foundations shall they be overthrown, And by the sword shall they fall. [And those who acquire gold and silver in judgement suddenly shall perish.]$n$,false),
(25339,'S',94,8,97,9,$n$Ecclesiasticus 11:19 — *Whereas he says, I have found rest, and now will eat continually of my goods; and yet he knoweth not what time shall come upon him, and that he must leave those things to others, and die.* Sirach mocks the hoarder's 'let us do what we purposed' plan with the very ignorance of his end that Enoch exposes (97:9).$n$,$n$And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,$n$,false),
(25369,'S',96,4,96,5,$n$Amos 5:12 — *For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate from their right.* The afflicting of the just stands behind Enoch's repeated charge that they tread upon the poor with their might (96:5).$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25371,'S',96,4,96,5,$n$Isaiah 3:15 — *What mean ye that ye beat my people to pieces, and grind the faces of the poor? saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) of hosts.* Grinding the faces of the poor is Isaiah's image for the trampling Enoch denounces in 96:5.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25372,'S',96,4,96,5,$n$Proverbs 22:23 — *For Yahuah (LORD) will plead their cause, and spoil the soul of those that spoiled them.* Torah's guarantee that Yahuah avenges the oppressed poor is the ground of every woe Enoch pronounces in 96:4-8.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25397,'S',97,6,96,5,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The poor trodden in Enoch 96:5 are James's defrauded reapers, whose cry has already entered the ears of Yahuah.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25402,'S',97,8,97,9,$n$Habakkuk 2:6 — *Shall not all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, Woe to him that increaseth that which is not his! how long? and to him that ladeth himself with thick clay!* Habakkuk's taunting woe against the man who increases what is not his is the same charge Enoch 97:9 lays on those who say 'let us do what we purposed.'$n$,$n$And now let us do what we purposed: For we have gathered silver, And many are the husbandmen in our houses.’ And our granaries are (brim) full as with water,$n$,false),
(25504,'S',97,8,97,8,$n$Isaiah 5:8 — *Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!* Isaiah's woe on the land-engrossers matches Enoch's woe on those who acquire gold and silver in unrighteousness (97:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25484,'S',103,14,103,14,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The cry the rulers would not hear — *cried out against those who devoured us, But they did not attend to our cries* (103:14) — is the cry James says has entered the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.$n$,$n$And we complained to the rulers in our tribulation, And cried out against those who devoured us, But they did not attend to our cries And would not hearken to our voice.$n$,false),
(16759,'S',23,4,23,4,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The sun knowing its going down is the sun Raguel's fire in the west receives — the fire which persecutes all the luminaries of heaven (23:4).$n$,$n$Then Raguel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered me and said unto me: ‘This course of fire which thou hast seen is the fire in the west which persecutes all the luminaries of heaven.’$n$,false),
(16760,'S',23,4,23,4,$n$Psalms 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The fire in the west that pursues the luminaries (23:4) is no rebel flame but a minister of Yahuah (LORD), set to its task like his flaming servants.$n$,$n$Then Raguel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered me and said unto me: ‘This course of fire which thou hast seen is the fire in the west which persecutes all the luminaries of heaven.’$n$,false),
(16763,'S',23,4,23,4,$n$Psalms 19:4 — *Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,* The same sun for which Yahuah (LORD) appointed a tabernacle is the one whose setting Raguel's fire in the west receives (23:4).$n$,$n$Then Raguel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered me and said unto me: ‘This course of fire which thou hast seen is the fire in the west which persecutes all the luminaries of heaven.’$n$,false),
(22553,'S',78,1,78,1,$n$Genesis 1:16 — *And Elohim (God) made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.* Enoch names the sun twice over — Orjârês and Tômâs (78:1) — the greater light of creation week, named out.$n$,$n$And the names of the sun are the following: the first Orjârês, and the second Tômâs.$n$,false),
(25347,'S',94,2,94,2,$n$Matthew 7:13 — *Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:* Yahusha's (Jesus's) broad road to destruction is Enoch's paths of violence and of death — revealed to a generation so that they hold themselves afar from them (94:2).$n$,$n$And to certain men of a generation shall the paths of violence and of death be revealed, And they shall hold themselves afar from them, And shall not follow them.$n$,false),
(16776,'S',25,3,25,3,$n$Jubilees 4:25 — *For Yahuah (God) has four places on the earth, the Garden of Eden, and the Mount of the East, and this mountain on which you are this day, Mount Sinai, and Mount Zion (which) will be sanctified in the new creation for a sanctification of the earth; through it will the earth be sanctified from all (its) guilt and its uncleanness throughout the generations of the world.* Jubilees counts Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3) among Yahuah's holy places on earth, sanctified in the new creation.$n$,$n$And he answered saying: ‘This high mountain which thou hast seen, whose summit is like the throne of Elohim (God), is His throne, where the Holy Great One, Yahuah (Lord) of Glory, the Eternal King, will sit, when He shall come down to visit the earth with goodness.$n$,false),
(16778,'S',25,3,25,3,$n$Ezekiel 28:14 — *Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of Elohim (God); thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.* Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3) is the canon's own holy mountain of Elohim, the Eden-sanctuary from which the covering cherub fell.$n$,$n$And he answered saying: ‘This high mountain which thou hast seen, whose summit is like the throne of Elohim (God), is His throne, where the Holy Great One, Yahuah (Lord) of Glory, the Eternal King, will sit, when He shall come down to visit the earth with goodness.$n$,false),
(16779,'S',25,3,25,3,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* Daniel's fiery seat of the Ancient of days is Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3), where the Eternal King will sit when He comes down to visit the earth.$n$,$n$And he answered saying: ‘This high mountain which thou hast seen, whose summit is like the throne of Elohim (God), is His throne, where the Holy Great One, Yahuah (Lord) of Glory, the Eternal King, will sit, when He shall come down to visit the earth with goodness.$n$,false),
(16767,'S',25,4,25,4,$n$2 Esdras 2:12 — *They shall have the tree of life for an ointment of sweet savour; they shall neither labour, nor be weary.* The tree's sweet-savour healing laid up for the righteous matches Enoch's fragrant tree reserved till the great judgement, whose fragrance shall be in their bones (25:4).$n$,$n$And as for this fragrant tree no mortal is permitted to touch it till the great judgement, when He shall take vengeance on all and bring (everything) to its consummation for ever. It shall then be given to the righteous and holy.$n$,false),
(16764,'S',25,6,25,6,$n$Revelation 22:3 — *And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him.* The lifted curse and the throne in the holy place answer Enoch's long restful life entered into the holy place by the tree (25:6).$n$,$n$Then shall they rejoice with joy and be glad, And into the holy place shall they enter; And its fragrance shall be in their bones, And they shall live a long life on earth, Such as thy fathers lived: And in their days shall no sorrow or plague Or torment or calamity touch them.’$n$,false),
(16765,'S',25,6,25,6,$n$Revelation 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.* John's restored creation where no sorrow or pain remains is Enoch's promise that *no sorrow or plague or torment or calamity* shall touch the elect (25:6).$n$,$n$Then shall they rejoice with joy and be glad, And into the holy place shall they enter; And its fragrance shall be in their bones, And they shall live a long life on earth, Such as thy fathers lived: And in their days shall no sorrow or plague Or torment or calamity touch them.’$n$,false),
(16766,'S',25,6,25,6,$n$Isaiah 25:8 — *He will swallow up death in victory; and Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) will wipe away tears from off all faces; and the rebuke of his people shall he take away from off all the earth: for Yahuah (LORD) hath spoken it.* The end of all sorrow and torment Enoch promises the elect (25:6) is Isaiah's swallowing-up of death and wiping of every tear.$n$,$n$Then shall they rejoice with joy and be glad, And into the holy place shall they enter; And its fragrance shall be in their bones, And they shall live a long life on earth, Such as thy fathers lived: And in their days shall no sorrow or plague Or torment or calamity touch them.’$n$,false),
(17192,'S',25,6,25,6,$n$Ezekiel 47:12 — *And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.* Ezekiel's healing trees flowing from the sanctuary match the temple-tree of Enoch 25:6 whose fragrance brings life and ends all plague.$n$,$n$Then shall they rejoice with joy and be glad, And into the holy place shall they enter; And its fragrance shall be in their bones, And they shall live a long life on earth, Such as thy fathers lived: And in their days shall no sorrow or plague Or torment or calamity touch them.’$n$,false),
(16682,'S',21,10,21,10,$n$Revelation 20:3 — *And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season.* The shut-up, sealed pit of John is the prison of the angels Enoch reaches at 21:10 — a holding, kept till the appointed time.$n$,$n$And he said unto me: ‘This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be imprisoned for ever.’$n$,false),
(25331,'S',96,5,96,5,$n$James 5:5 — *Ye have lived in pleasure on the earth, and been wanton; ye have nourished your hearts, as in a day of slaughter.* James condemns the same self-indulgent feasting on the backs of others that Enoch pronounces woe upon (96:5).$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25334,'S',96,5,96,5,$n$Isaiah 5:22 — *Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:* the mighty wine-drinkers Isaiah condemns are Enoch's who 'drink the finest wine, And tread upon the poor with your might' (96:5).$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(25467,'S',96,5,96,5,$n$Amos 6:6 — *That drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments: but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph.* Enoch's drinkers of wine in large bowls (96:5) are Amos's feasters indifferent to the suffering of the people.$n$,$n$Woe to you who devour the finest of the wheat, And drink wine in large bowls, And tread under foot the lowly with your might.$n$,false),
(18043,'S',41,7,41,7,$n$Jubilees 2:9 — *And Elohim (God) appointed the sun to be a great sign on the earth for days and for sabbaths and for months and for feasts and for years and for sabbaths of years and for jubilees and for all seasons of the years* — the monthly revolution of 41:7 is the very clockwork by which the moedim are appointed.$n$,$n$And after that I saw the hidden and the visible path of the moon, and she accomplishes the course of her path in that place by day and by night—the one holding a position opposite to the other before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. And they give thanks and praise and rest not; For unto them is their thanksgiving rest.$n$,false),
(18044,'S',41,7,41,7,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork* — the lights that praise and rest not before Yahuah of Spirits in 41:7 are the same unceasing witness the Psalm hears in the firmament.$n$,$n$And after that I saw the hidden and the visible path of the moon, and she accomplishes the course of her path in that place by day and by night—the one holding a position opposite to the other before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. And they give thanks and praise and rest not; For unto them is their thanksgiving rest.$n$,false),
(17926,'S',69,28,69,28,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* Daniel's two-fold awaking, to life or to shame, is Enoch's parting of the righteous made victorious from the sinners bound and cast into the furnace (69:28).$n$,$n$With chains shall they be bound, And in their assemblage-place of destruction shall they be imprisoned, And all their works vanish from the face of the earth.$n$,false),
(23899,'S',89,15,89,15,$n$Exodus 3:7 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, I have surely seen the affliction of my people which are in Egypt, and have heard their cry by reason of their taskmasters; for I know their sorrows;* The Lord of the sheep who hears the sheep's cry (89:16) is Yahuah hearing Israel's cry in Egypt.$n$,$n$And the wolves began to fear them, and they oppressed them until they destroyed their little ones, and they cast their young into a river of much water: but those sheep began to cry aloud on account of their little ones, and to complain unto their Lord.$n$,false),
(16278,'S',11,1,10,9,$n$Genesis 6:3 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.* Yahuah's (the LORD's) sentence that man's days be a hundred and twenty is of a piece with his word to Gabriel over the Watchers' children: *for length of days shall they not have* (10:9).$n$,$n$And to Gabriel said Yahuah (Lord): ‘Proceed against the bastards and the reprobates, and against the children of fornication: and destroy [the children of fornication and] the children of the Watchers from amongst men [and cause them to go forth]: send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle: for length of days shall they not have.$n$,false),
(25553,'S',108,10,100,6,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) gives the righteous shining in their Father's kingdom; Enoch gives the children of the earth seeing the wise in security at last (100:6).$n$,$n$And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.$n$,false),
(19848,'S',52,6,56,4,$n$Zechariah 4:7 — *Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.* The valley filled with the elect and beloved when the days of leading astray are ended (56:4) is Zechariah's great mountain flattened to a plain before the chosen one.$n$,$n$And then that valley shall be filled with their elect and beloved, And the days of their lives shall be at an end, And the days of their leading astray shall not thenceforward be reckoned.$n$,false),
(19863,'S',53,3,53,2,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* The sinners destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits and banished from his earth (53:2) are these kings and mighty men, undone before the face from which they cannot be hidden.$n$,$n$And their hands commit lawless deeds, And the sinners devour all whom they lawlessly oppress: Yet the sinners shall be destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And they shall be banished from off the face of His earth, And they shall perish for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(25363,'S',95,7,95,7,$n$Amos 6:7 — *Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the banquet of them that stretched themselves shall be removed.* — the banquet removed and the feasters led captive is the cutting-off of the rich oppressor's might in Enoch 95:7.$n$,$n$Woe to you, sinners, for ye persecute the righteous; For ye shall be delivered up and persecuted because of injustice, And heavy shall its yoke be upon you.$n$,false),
(25485,'S',103,15,97,8,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James opens the very woe Enoch pronounces on those who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say they have everything they desired (97:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(23897,'S',89,14,89,13,$n$Exodus 1:13 — *And the Egyptians made the children of Yashar'el (Israel) to serve with rigour:* The sheep given over to the wolves (89:13) is Israel made to serve Egypt with rigour.$n$,$n$And when those twelve sheep had grown, they gave up one of them to the asses, and those asses again gave up that sheep to the wolves, and that sheep grew up among the wolves.$n$,false),
(21285,'S',63,3,62,9,$n$Matthew 25:11 — *Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Adonai (Lord), Adonai (Lord), open to us.* The late cry of the foolish virgins matches the kings' too-late worship of that Son of Adam (62:9).$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$,false),
(21286,'S',63,4,62,10,$n$Luke 13:25 — *When once the master of the house is risen up, and hath shut to the door, and ye begin to stand without, and to knock at the door, saying, Adonai (Lord), Adonai (Lord), open unto us; and he shall answer and say unto you, I know you not whence ye are:* Yahusha's (Jesus's) shut door is Enoch's pressed-out departure (62:10) — the petition is heard but the hour of mercy has passed.$n$,$n$Nevertheless that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits will so press them That they shall hastily go forth from His presence, And their faces shall be filled with shame, And the darkness grow deeper on their faces.$n$,false),
(19988,'S',62,9,46,4,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* The Son of Adam who casts down kings and kingdoms in Enoch 46:4-6 holds the everlasting dominion Daniel saw given to him by the Ancient of days.$n$,$n$And this Son of Adam whom thou hast seen Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats, [And the strong from their thrones] And shall loosen the reins of the strong, And break the teeth of the sinners.$n$,false),
(23923,'S',89,49,90,37,$n$John 10:16 — *And other sheep I have, which are not of this fold: them also I must bring, and they shall hear my voice; and there shall be one fold, and one shepherd.* The white bull before whom all are transformed into white bulls (90:37-38) is the one Shepherd gathering the scattered into one fold.$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$,false),
(16043,'S',7,4,7,5,$n$Jubilees 7:24 — *And after this they sinned against the beasts and birds, and all that moves and walks on the earth: and much blood was shed on the earth, and every imagination and desire of men imagined vanity and evil continually.* Jubilees records the same sinning against beasts and birds and the much blood shed that 1 Enoch 7:4-5 describes.$n$,$n$And they began to sin against birds, and beasts, and reptiles, and fish, and to devour one another's flesh, and drink the blood.$n$,false),
(21408,'S',71,1,71,1,$n$Psalms 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire.* Names what the flame-treaders of 71:1 are: ministering servants of fire, not gods — an ordered court under the Creator.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(16013,'S',5,8,1,9,$n$Deuteronomy 33:2 — *And he said, Yahuah (LORD) came from Sinai, and rose up from Seir unto them; he shined forth from mount Paran, and he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand went a fiery law for them.* The Judge who comes with ten thousands is the same who came to Sinai with the fiery law — Torah and judgement issue from one hand.$n$,$n$And behold! He cometh with ten thousands of His holy ones To execute judgement upon all, And to destroy all the ungodly: And to convict all flesh Of all the works of their ungodliness which they have ungodly committed, And of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against Him.$n$,false),
(16016,'S',5,7,1,8,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:6 — *Therefore have we erred from the way of truth, and the light of righteousness has not shined to us, and the sun of righteousness rose not upon us.* The light that appears unto the elect is the very light the godless confess, too late, never shined on them.$n$,$n$But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.$n$,false),
(16018,'S',5,7,1,8,$n$Malachi 4:2 — *But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.* The peace and light granted to the elect rise as the Sun of righteousness on those who fear His name.$n$,$n$But with the righteous He will make peace. And will protect the elect, And mercy shall be upon them. And they shall all belong to Elohim (God), And they shall be prospered, And they shall all be blessed. And He will help them all, And light shall appear unto them, And He will make peace with them.$n$,false),
(16040,'S',7,5,7,6,$n$Jubilees 7:25 — *And Yahuah (God) destroyed everything from off the face of the earth; because of the wickedness of their deeds, and because of the blood which they had shed in the midst of the earth He destroyed everything.* Jubilees names the shed blood as the very ground of the judgment the earth's accusation in 1 Enoch 7:6 calls for.$n$,$n$Then the earth laid accusation against the lawless ones.$n$,false),
(16042,'S',7,5,7,6,$n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* The Torah's verdict on the same generation whose lawlessness makes the earth itself lay accusation in 1 Enoch 7:6.$n$,$n$Then the earth laid accusation against the lawless ones.$n$,false),
(16044,'S',7,4,7,5,$n$Leviticus 17:14 — *For it is the life of all flesh; the blood of it is for the life thereof: therefore I said unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), Ye shall eat the blood of no manner of flesh: for the life of all flesh is the blood thereof: whosoever eateth it shall be cut off.* The Torah's standing blood statute marks the very line the giants of 1 Enoch 7:5 crossed when they devoured flesh and drank blood.$n$,$n$And they began to sin against birds, and beasts, and reptiles, and fish, and to devour one another's flesh, and drink the blood.$n$,false),
(16045,'S',7,4,7,5,$n$Genesis 9:4 — *But flesh with the life thereof, which is the blood thereof, shall ye not eat.* The blood-drinking of 1 Enoch 7:5 is the exact corruption the Creator forbids to the renewed post-flood earth.$n$,$n$And they began to sin against birds, and beasts, and reptiles, and fish, and to devour one another's flesh, and drink the blood.$n$,false),
(16274,'S',11,2,10,12,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* Isaiah lifts the binding of the Watchers in Enoch 10:12 to the day of judgement, when the host of the high ones is finally visited.$n$,$n$And when their sons have slain one another, and they have seen the destruction of their beloved ones, bind them fast for seventy generations in the valleys of the earth, till the day of their judgement and of their consummation, till the judgement that is for ever and ever is consummated.$n$,false),
(16275,'S',11,2,10,12,$n$Jubilees 5:6 — *And against the angels whom He had sent upon the earth, He was exceedingly wroth, and He gave commandment to root them out of all their dominion, and He bade us to bind them in the depths of the earth, and behold they are bound in the midst of them, and are (kept) separate.* Jubilees tells the same binding Michael is commanded to perform in Enoch 10:12, in the depths of the earth.$n$,$n$And when their sons have slain one another, and they have seen the destruction of their beloved ones, bind them fast for seventy generations in the valleys of the earth, till the day of their judgement and of their consummation, till the judgement that is for ever and ever is consummated.$n$,false),
(16276,'S',11,2,10,12,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment.* Peter and Enoch 10:12 give the same verdict: the sinning angels are bound fast and reserved unto judgement.$n$,$n$And when their sons have slain one another, and they have seen the destruction of their beloved ones, bind them fast for seventy generations in the valleys of the earth, till the day of their judgement and of their consummation, till the judgement that is for ever and ever is consummated.$n$,false),
(16279,'S',11,1,10,11,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* This is the very defilement Michael is sent to punish in Enoch 10:11 — the Watchers who united themselves with women.$n$,$n$And Yahuah (Lord) said unto Michael: ‘Go, bind Semjâzâ and his associates who have united themselves with women so as to have defiled themselves with them in all their uncleanness.$n$,false),
(16314,'S',14,20,18,15,$n$Genesis 1:16 — *And Elohim (God) made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.* The stars the Creator made to rule their courses are the very stars that transgressed His commandment in the beginning of their rising in 18:15.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$,false),
(16318,'S',14,21,18,16,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude names the prisoners as the rebel angels reserved in chains until the judgment — the same binding 'till the time when their guilt should be consummated' Enoch records in 18:16.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$,false),
(16320,'S',14,21,18,16,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* The shutting-up in prison until a later visitation is exactly Enoch's binding of the stars 'till the time when their guilt should be consummated' in 18:16.$n$,$n$And He was wroth with them, and bound them till the time when their guilt should be consummated (even) for ten thousand years.’$n$,false),
(16322,'S',14,18,18,12,$n$Jeremiah 4:25 — *I beheld, and, lo, there was no man, and all the birds of the heavens were fled.* The fled birds match Enoch's place where 'there was no water upon it, and no birds' (18:12) — the desolation that mirrors the place of imprisonment.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$,false),
(16323,'S',14,18,18,12,$n$Jeremiah 4:23 — *I beheld the earth, and, lo, it was without form, and void; and the heavens, and they had no light.* Jeremiah sees creation rolled back to formlessness under judgement — the same waste place with no firmament above that Enoch is shown in 18:12.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$,false),
(16324,'S',14,18,18,12,$n$Genesis 1:2 — *And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of Elohim (God) moved upon the face of the waters.* The 'waste and horrible place' with no firmament and no founded earth is the tohu-and-bohu of creation's first verse — the un-ordered ground that lies outside the Creator's order in 18:12.$n$,$n$And beyond that abyss I saw a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it: there was no water upon it, and no birds, but it was a waste and horrible place.$n$,false),
(16325,'S',14,15,18,8,$n$Revelation 4:2 — *And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.* John is carried up in the spirit to the same enthroned glory Enoch is carried up to see in 18:8, the one throne that stands from his vision to John's.$n$,$n$But the middle one reached to heaven like the throne of Elohim (God), of alabaster, and the summit of the throne was of sapphire.$n$,false),
(16330,'S',15,11,16,1,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude's 'judgment of the great day' is Enoch 16:1's 'great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless.'$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$,false),
(16331,'S',15,11,16,1,$n$Genesis 6:3 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.* The mortality decreed on flesh in Genesis 6:3 is the very death Enoch 15:4-11 traces — the giants 'die and perish,' and their spirits are loosed until the great judgement.$n$,$n$From the days of the slaughter and destruction and death of the giants, from the souls of whose flesh the spirits, having gone forth, shall destroy without incurring judgement—thus shall they destroy until the day of the consummation, the great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless, yea, shall be wholly consummated."$n$,false),
(16332,'S',15,6,15,8,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 14:6 — *For in the old time also, when the proud giants perished, the hope of the world governed by your hand escaped in a weak vessel, and left to all ages a seed of generation.* Wisdom remembers the proud giants of Enoch 15:8 perishing in the Flood while righteous seed was preserved in the ark.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$,false),
(16333,'S',15,7,15,9,$n$Jubilees 10:1 — *And in the third week of this jubilee the unclean demons began to lead astray the children of the sons of Noah; and to make to err and destroy them.* Jubilees shows the spirits of Enoch 15:9 already at work after the Flood — the surviving giant-spirits leading astray and destroying mankind.$n$,$n$Evil spirits have proceeded from their bodies; because they are born from men and from the holy Watchers is their beginning and primal origin; they shall be evil spirits on earth, and evil spirits shall they be called.$n$,false),
(16334,'S',15,6,15,8,$n$Matthew 12:43 — *When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and findeth none.* The restless, earth-bound spirit Yahusha (Jesus) describes is exactly Enoch 15:8's giant-spirit whose dwelling is on the earth, seeking a body and finding no true home.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$,false),
(16676,'S',17,6,17,7,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,* The treasuries of winter's darkness and the waters of the deep that Enoch sees (1 Enoch 17:7) are the hidden treasures Yahuah keeps from Job.$n$,$n$I saw the mountains of the darkness of winter and the place whence all the waters of the deep flow.$n$,false),
(16677,'S',17,5,17,6,$n$Job 38:16 — *Hast thou entered into the springs of the sea? or hast thou walked in the search of the depth?* The place where no flesh walks and the waters of the deep (1 Enoch 17:6-6) are the springs of the sea Yahuah challenges Job to enter.$n$,$n$I saw the great rivers and came to the great river and to the great darkness, and went to the place where no flesh walks.$n$,false),
(16679,'S',17,4,17,5,$n$Deuteronomy 32:22 — *For a fire is kindled in mine anger, and shall burn unto the lowest hell, and shall consume the earth with her increase, and set on fire the foundations of the mountains.* The river of fire that flows like water (1 Enoch 17:5) is the same kindled fire Moses says burns to the lowest depths.$n$,$n$And I came to a river of fire in which the fire flows like water and discharges itself into the great sea towards the west.$n$,false),
(16689,'S',18,13,18,15,$n$Job 38:33 — *Knowest thou the ordinances of heaven? canst thou set the dominion thereof in the earth?* The ordinances of heaven the stars broke by not coming forth at their appointed times (Enoch 18:15).$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$,false),
(16690,'S',18,13,18,15,$n$Job 38:31 — *Canst thou bind the sweet influences of Pleiades, or loose the bands of Orion?* The fixed star-order Job cannot command is the very order the seven stars transgressed in Enoch 18:15.$n$,$n$And the stars which roll over the fire are they which have transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) in the beginning of their rising, because they did not come forth at their appointed times.$n$,false),
(16745,'S',22,14,22,7,$n$Genesis 4:10 — *And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother's blood crieth unto me from the ground.* Enoch 22:7 names the very spirit whose crying blood Genesis records — Abel's suit against Cain, still going up to heaven.$n$,$n$And he answered me saying: ‘This is the spirit which went forth from Abel, whom his brother Cain slew, and he makes his suit against him till his seed is destroyed from the face of the earth, and his seed is annihilated from amongst the seed of men.’$n$,false),
(16746,'S',22,9,22,2,$n$Luke 16:26 — *And beside all this, between us and you there is a great gulf fixed: so that they which would pass from hence to you cannot; neither can they pass to us, that would come from thence.* The fixed gulf in Sheol is Enoch's separated hollow places, the righteous parted from the sinners (Enoch 22:2).$n$,$n$And there was in it four hollow places, deep and wide and very smooth. How smooth are the hollow places and deep and dark to look at.$n$,false),
(16747,'S',22,10,22,3,$n$Luke 16:22 — *And it came to pass, that the beggar died, and was carried by the angels into Abraham's bosom: the rich man also died, and was buried;* the two dead men gathered into one waiting-place match Enoch's hollow places where all the souls of the children of men assemble.$n$,$n$Then Raphael answered, one of the holy angels who was with me, and said unto me: ‘These hollow places have been created for this very purpose, that the spirits of the souls of the dead should assemble therein, yea that all the souls of the children of men should assemble here.$n$,false),
(16748,'S',22,4,21,3,$n$Jude 1:13 — *Raging waves of the sea, foaming out their own shame; wandering stars, to whom is reserved the blackness of darkness for ever.* Jude keeps Enoch's very image of the bound seven stars as fallen luminaries reserved in darkness (Enoch 21:3).$n$,$n$And there I saw seven stars of the heaven bound together in it, like great mountains and burning with fire.$n$,false),
(17135,'S',25,6,15,8,$n$Jubilees 10:1 — *And in the third week of this jubilee the unclean demons began to lead astray the children of the sons of Noah; and to make to err and destroy them.* Jubilees shows Enoch's evil spirits at work after the Flood, the giants' offspring leading the living astray.$n$,$n$And now, the giants, who are produced from the spirits and flesh, shall be called evil spirits upon the earth, and on the earth shall be their dwelling.$n$,false),
(17138,'S',25,4,15,4,$n$Genesis 6:3 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.* The Creator's limit on flesh answers the Watchers who, though spiritual and living the eternal life, lusted after flesh and blood.$n$,$n$And though ye were holy, spiritual, living the eternal life, you have defiled yourselves with the blood of women, and have begotten (children) with the blood of flesh, and, as the children of men, have lusted after flesh and blood as those also do who die and perish.$n$,false),
(17923,'S',37,5,1,3,$n$Matthew 11:25 — *At that time Yahusha (Jesus) answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Yahuah (Lord) of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.* The Father's selective unveiling to the chosen is Enoch's parable spoken 'concerning the elect' (1 Enoch 1:3).$n$,$n$Concerning the elect I said, and took up my parable concerning them: The Holy Great One will come forth from His dwelling,$n$,false),
(17988,'S',41,7,41,8,$n$Jubilees 2:8 — *And on the fourth day He created the sun and the moon and the stars, and set them in the firmament of the heaven, to give light upon all the earth, and to rule over the day and the night, and divide the light from the darkness.* Jubilees sets the same dividing of light from darkness on the fourth day, the lights that govern Enoch's faithful orbit and the appointed feasts.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(17990,'S',41,6,41,7,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The moon that accomplishes her monthly revolution and sets by oath in Enoch is the moon Yahuah appointed for the seasons.$n$,$n$And after that I saw the hidden and the visible path of the moon, and she accomplishes the course of her path in that place by day and by night—the one holding a position opposite to the other before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits. And they give thanks and praise and rest not; For unto them is their thanksgiving rest.$n$,false),
(17991,'S',41,7,41,8,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* Enoch's division of light from darkness and his ordered sun and moon are the fourth-day lights set for signs and seasons — the moedim.$n$,$n$For the sun changes oft for a blessing or a curse, And the course of the path of the moon is light to the righteous And darkness to the sinners in the name of Yahuah (Lord), Who made a separation between the light and the darkness, And divided the spirits of men, And strengthened the spirits of the righteous, In the name of His righteousness.$n$,false),
(18049,'S',44,1,41,3,$n$Job 38:35 — *Canst thou send lightnings, that they may go, and say unto thee, Here we are?* Yahuah's challenge to Job names the same secret of lightning and thunder Enoch is shown in the storehouses of 41:3.$n$,$n$And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.$n$,false),
(19860,'S',53,3,53,2,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* The pit-prison for the gathered transgressors mirrors the perishing for ever and ever of the sinners in 53:2.$n$,$n$And their hands commit lawless deeds, And the sinners devour all whom they lawlessly oppress: Yet the sinners shall be destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And they shall be banished from off the face of His earth, And they shall perish for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(19861,'S',53,3,53,2,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* Isaiah joins the host above and the kings below under one judgement, as 53:2 banishes the oppressors from off the face of His earth.$n$,$n$And their hands commit lawless deeds, And the sinners devour all whom they lawlessly oppress: Yet the sinners shall be destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And they shall be banished from off the face of His earth, And they shall perish for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(19862,'S',53,3,53,2,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:* The sinners destroyed *before the face of Yahuah of Spirits* (53:2) are those who beg to be hidden from that very face.$n$,$n$And their hands commit lawless deeds, And the sinners devour all whom they lawlessly oppress: Yet the sinners shall be destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And they shall be banished from off the face of His earth, And they shall perish for ever and ever.$n$,false),
(19868,'S',53,5,53,4,$n$Matthew 13:41 — *The Son of Adam shall send forth his angels, and they shall gather out of his kingdom all things that offend, and them which do iniquity;* The Son of Adam dispatches the same angels of punishment Enoch sees making ready the instruments at 53:4-5.$n$,$n$And I asked the angel of peace who went with me: ‘For whom are they preparing these instruments?’$n$,false),
(19942,'S',59,2,41,3,$n$Jubilees 2:2 — *For on the first day He created the heavens which are above and the earth and the waters and all the spirits which serve before Him–the angels of the presence, and the angels of sanctification, and the angels of the spirit of fire and the angels of the spirit of the winds, and the angels of the spirit of the clouds, and of darkness, and of snow and of hail and of hoar frost, and the angels of the voices and of the thunder and of the lightning, and the angels of the spirits of cold and of heat, and of winter and of spring and of autumn and of summer, and of all the spirits of His creatures which are in the heavens and on the earth, (He created) the abysses and the darkness, eventide (and night), and the light, dawn and day, which He has prepared in the knowledge of His heart.* Jubilees stations angels over the very winds, clouds, hail, thunder, and lightning whose divided chambers Enoch is shown.$n$,$n$And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.$n$,false),
(19943,'S',59,2,41,3,$n$Psalm 29:3 — *The voice of Yahuah (LORD) is upon the waters: the Elohim (God) of glory thundereth: Yahuah (LORD) is upon many waters.* David hears the thunder as the voice of Yahuah, the secret Enoch is shown behind the storm.$n$,$n$And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.$n$,false),
(19948,'S',60,14,41,4,$n$Jeremiah 10:13 — *When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens, and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.* The prophet confesses the same wind-out-of-the-treasuries order that the angel shows Enoch in the closed chambers of 41:4.$n$,$n$And there I saw closed chambers out of which the winds are divided, the chamber of the hail and winds, the chamber of the mist, and of the clouds, and the cloud thereof hovers over the earth from the beginning of the world.$n$,false),
(19950,'S',60,13,41,3,$n$Job 38:25 — *Who hath divided a watercourse for the overflowing of waters, or a way for the lightning of thunder;* the dividing of the lightning-and-thunder paths in 41:3 is Yahuah's own ordering of the storm in His answer to Job.$n$,$n$And there mine eyes saw the secrets of the lightning and of the thunder, and the secrets of the winds, how they are divided to blow over the earth, and the secrets of the clouds and dew, and there I saw from whence they proceed in that place and from whence they saturate the dusty earth.$n$,false),
(19980,'S',62,12,46,6,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach.* The shame-covered strong of Enoch 46:6 echo the mockers who, too late, recognize the righteous One they had despised.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(19982,'S',62,10,46,5,$n$Revelation 1:7 — *Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.* The kings who refused to acknowledge Him in Enoch 46:5 are those who at His coming see Him too late and wail before the throne of glory.$n$,$n$[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.$n$,false),
(19983,'S',62,12,46,6,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.* The mighty whose countenance is covered with shame in Enoch 46:6 beg the rocks to hide them from the face of the enthroned Son of Adam — the wrath of the Lamb.$n$,$n$And he shall put down the countenance of the strong, And shall fill them with shame. And darkness shall be their dwelling, And worms shall be their bed, And they shall have no hope of rising from their beds, Because they do not extol the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(19987,'S',62,10,46,5,$n$Psalm 2:9 — *Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter's vessel.* The Son of Adam who 'put down the kings from their thrones' in Enoch 46:5 is the Psalm's enthroned Son who breaks the raging rulers with the iron rod.$n$,$n$[And he shall put down the kings from their thrones and kingdoms] Because they do not extol and praise Him, Nor humbly acknowledge whence the kingdom was bestowed upon them.$n$,false),
(19992,'S',62,2,61,9,$n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.* The judging 'by the way of the righteous judgement' in Enoch 61:9 is Isaiah's Branch who judges in righteousness, not by the sight of the eyes.$n$,$n$And when he shall lift up his countenance To judge their secret ways according to the word of the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, And their path according to the way of the righteous judgement of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits, Then shall they all with one voice speak and bless, And glorify and extol and sanctify the name of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(21274,'S',63,8,62,5,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach:* The wicked's late, useless remorse on beholding the righteous One mirrors the kings' fallen countenance before the Son of Adam (62:5).$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$,false),
(21276,'S',63,8,62,5,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:* The dread before Him that sitteth on the throne is Enoch's terror at seeing that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory (62:5).$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$,false),
(21277,'S',63,8,62,5,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* John's roll of the terrified is Enoch's kings and mighty whose countenance falls when they see the Son of Adam (62:5).$n$,$n$And one portion of them shall look on the other, And they shall be terrified, And they shall be downcast of countenance, And pain shall seize them, When they see that Son of Adam Sitting on the throne of his glory.$n$,false),
(21283,'S',63,4,62,10,$n$Isaiah 26:10 — *Let favour be shewed to the wicked, yet will he not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness will he deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of Yahuah (LORD).* The wicked who would not learn now confess only under pressure, then go forth in shame (62:10).$n$,$n$Nevertheless that Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits will so press them That they shall hastily go forth from His presence, And their faces shall be filled with shame, And the darkness grow deeper on their faces.$n$,false),
(21284,'S',63,3,62,9,$n$Matthew 25:12 — *But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.* The refusal that meets the late virgins is the shame and darkness that meets the kings who supplicate too late (62:9-4).$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$,false),
(21287,'S',63,3,62,9,$n$Proverbs 1:28 — *Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:* The kings' late supplication at the Son of Adam's hands (62:9) is the cry that Wisdom long ago foretold would go unanswered.$n$,$n$And all the kings and the mighty and the exalted and those who rule the earth Shall fall down before him on their faces, And worship and set their hope upon that Son of Adam, And petition him and supplicate for mercy at his hands.$n$,false),
(21329,'S',67,5,47,4,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* The martyrs' cry for their blood to be avenged is Enoch's blood of the righteous "required before Yahuah (God) of Spirits" at 47:4.$n$,$n$And the hearts of the holy were filled with joy; Because the number of the righteous had been offered, And the prayer of the righteous had been heard, And the blood of the righteous been required before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(21354,'S',69,5,8,1,$n$Genesis 6:4 — *There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of Elohim (God) came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown.* The giants of Genesis are the offspring of the very leaders Enoch names teaching swords, sorcery, and the metals of war.$n$,$n$And Azâzêl taught men to make swords, and knives, and shields, and breastplates, and made known to them the metals of the earth and the art of working them, and bracelets, and ornaments, and the use of antimony, and the beautifying of the eyelids, and all kinds of costly stones, and all colouring tinctures.$n$,false),
(21355,'S',69,6,8,2,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude carries Enoch's fallen Watchers straight into the New Testament — it ain't new.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$,false),
(21356,'S',69,6,8,2,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment.* Peter holds the same reserved-in-chains sentence over the named angels who corrupted all their ways.$n$,$n$And there arose much godlessness, and they committed fornication, and they were led astray, and became corrupt in all their ways.$n$,false),
(21357,'S',69,7,8,3,$n$Jubilees 7:21 — *For owing to these three things came the flood upon the earth, namely, owing to the fornication wherein the Watchers against the law of their ordinances went a whoring after the daughters of men, and took themselves wives of all which they chose: and they made the beginning of uncleanness. And they begat sons the Nâphîdîm, and they were all unlike, and they devoured one another: and the Giants slew the Nâphîl, and the Nâphîl slew the Eljô, and the Eljô mankind, and one man another.* Jubilees keeps the same Watcher-account — rebellion against the law of their ordinances — that Enoch lays out by name.$n$,$n$Semjâzâ taught enchantments, and root-cuttings, Armârôs the resolving of enchantments, Barâqîjâl (taught) astrology, Kôkabêl the constellations, Êzêqêêl the knowledge of the clouds, Araqiêl the signs of the earth, Shamsiêl the signs of the sun, and Sariêl the course of the moon.$n$,false),
(21358,'S',69,10,69,6,$n$Genesis 6:1 — *And it came to pass, when men began to multiply on the face of the earth, and daughters were born unto them.* The multiplying generations into which Gâdreêl loosed the weapons of death are the very days Genesis opens before the Watchers' descent.$n$,$n$And the third was named Gâdreêl: he it is who showed the children of men all the blows of death, and he led astray Eve, and showed [the weapons of death to the sons of men] the shield and the coat of mail, and the sword for battle, and all the weapons of death to the children of men.$n$,false),
(21359,'S',69,15,69,11,$n$Genesis 6:4 — *There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of Elohim (God) came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown.* Men made pure and like the angels were corrupted into the world of giants and bloodshed that Genesis names.$n$,$n$For men were created exactly like the angels, to the intent that they should continue pure and righteous, and death, which destroys everything, could not have taken hold of them, but through this their knowledge they are perishing, and through this power it is consuming me.$n$,false),
(21360,'S',69,20,69,16,$n$Psalm 33:6 — *By the word of Yahuah (LORD) were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.* The oath by which heaven was suspended before the world is the spoken Word by which the Psalm says the heavens were made.$n$,$n$And these are the secrets of this oath... And they are strong through his oath: And the heaven was suspended before the world was created, And for ever.$n$,false),
(21361,'S',69,21,69,17,$n$Psalm 33:9 — *For he spake, and it was done; he commanded, and it stood fast.* The oath that founded the earth upon the water is the creative command of which the Psalm says he spake and it stood fast.$n$,$n$And through it the earth was founded upon the water, And from the secret recesses of the mountains come beautiful waters, From the creation of the world and unto eternity.$n$,false),
(21362,'S',69,22,69,18,$n$Job 38:11 — *And said, Hitherto shalt thou come, but no further: and here shall thy proud waves be stayed?* The sand set against the sea's anger so it dare not pass its bound is the very boundary Job hears the Creator decree over the proud waves.$n$,$n$And through that oath the sea was created, And as its foundation He set for it the sand against the time of (its) anger, And it dare not pass beyond it from the creation of the world unto eternity.$n$,false),
(21363,'S',69,22,69,18,$n$Jeremiah 5:22 — *Fear ye not me? saith Yahuah (LORD): will ye not tremble at my presence, which have placed the sand for the bound of the sea by a perpetual decree, that it cannot pass it: and though the waves thereof toss themselves, yet can they not prevail; though they roar, yet can they not pass over it?* Jeremiah names the same sand, the same perpetual decree binding the sea, that Enoch ascribes to the hidden oath.$n$,$n$And through that oath the sea was created, And as its foundation He set for it the sand against the time of (its) anger, And it dare not pass beyond it from the creation of the world unto eternity.$n$,false),
(21364,'S',69,23,69,19,$n$Proverbs 8:29 — *When he gave to the sea his decree, that the waters should not pass his commandment: when he appointed the foundations of the earth.* Wisdom stands at the founding of the deep and the bounding of the sea that Enoch's oath makes fast from eternity to eternity.$n$,$n$And through that oath are the depths made fast, And abide and stir not from their place from eternity to eternity.$n$,false),
(21365,'S',69,20,69,16,$n$John 1:1 — *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God).* The hidden oath suspended before the world was created is the Word who was in the beginning, the Formed Son with the Head of Days.$n$,$n$And these are the secrets of this oath... And they are strong through his oath: And the heaven was suspended before the world was created, And for ever.$n$,false),
(21366,'S',69,21,69,17,$n$John 1:3 — *All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.* The oath by which earth, sea, and depths were founded is the Word by whom John says all things were made.$n$,$n$And through it the earth was founded upon the water, And from the secret recesses of the mountains come beautiful waters, From the creation of the world and unto eternity.$n$,false),
(21367,'S',69,24,69,20,$n$Colossians 1:16 — *For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him.* The oath that orders sun, moon, and stars in their courses is the Son by whom Paul says all things in heaven were created.$n$,$n$And through that oath the sun and moon complete their course, And deviate not from their ordinance from eternity to eternity.$n$,false),
(21368,'S',69,25,69,21,$n$Hebrews 1:3 — *Who being the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high.* The oath that keeps the stars in their paths and calls them by name is the Son still upholding all things by the word of his power.$n$,$n$And through that oath the stars complete their course, And He calls them by their names, And they answer Him from eternity to eternity.$n$,false),
(21383,'S',70,4,71,4,$n$Daniel 10:6 — *His body also was like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.* Daniel's fiery angelic revealer parallels the heavenly guide who shows Enoch the ends of heaven and the chambers of the stars in 1 Enoch 71:4.$n$,$n$And he showed me all the secrets of the ends of the heaven, And all the chambers of all the stars, and all the luminaries, Whence they proceed before the face of the holy ones.$n$,false),
(21384,'S',70,3,71,3,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The same archangel Michael who guards the covenant people in Daniel takes Enoch by the right hand to show him the secrets of righteousness in 1 Enoch 71:3.$n$,$n$And the angel Michael [one of the archangels] seized me by my right hand, And lifted me up and led me forth into all the secrets, And he showed me all the secrets of righteousness.$n$,false),
(21385,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Revelation 1:14 — *His head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;* John's glorified vision keeps the white-as-snow and flame-of-fire of the throne, the same imagery in which Enoch sees the holy ones with faces shining like snow in 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21386,'S',70,2,71,2,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The fiery stream from the throne matches the two streams of fire Enoch sees in 1 Enoch 71:2 before the Yahuah of Spirits.$n$,$n$And I saw two streams of fire, And the light of that fire shone like hyacinth, And I fell on my face before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(21388,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Jubilees 4:23 — *And he was taken from amongst the children of men, and we conducted him into the Garden of Eden in majesty and honour, and behold there he writes down the condemnation and judgment of the world, and all the wickedness of the children of men.* Jubilees confirms Enoch was conducted away to a heavenly dwelling, the same removal 1 Enoch 71:1 describes as his spirit ascending into the heavens.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21389,'S',70,2,71,2,$n$2 Kings 2:11 — *And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, there appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.* Elijah's bodily ascent into heaven is the only canonical parallel to Enoch's translation, and both are surrounded by fire as in 1 Enoch 71:2's two streams of fire.$n$,$n$And I saw two streams of fire, And the light of that fire shone like hyacinth, And I fell on my face before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.$n$,false),
(21390,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Ecclesiasticus 49:14 — *But upon the earth was no man created like Enoch; for he was taken from the earth.* Sirach marks Enoch's removal as without equal among the earth-born, matching the singular lifting-out narrated in 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21391,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Ecclesiasticus 44:16 — *Enoch pleased Yahuah (God), and was translated, being an example of repentance to all generations.* Sirach keeps the same verb "translated" for Enoch's removal that 1 Enoch 71:1 unfolds as an ascent into the heavens.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21392,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Hebrews 11:5 — *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because Elohim (God) had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased Elohim (God).* The New Testament names the manner — translation, not death — which is exactly the "my spirit was translated And it ascended" of 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21393,'S',70,1,71,1,$n$Genesis 5:24 — *And Enoch walked with Elohim (God): and he was not; for Elohim (God) took him.* The canon's single line of Enoch's removal is the event 1 Enoch 71:1 narrates from the inside as his spirit is translated and ascends into the heavens.$n$,$n$And it came to pass after this that my spirit was translated And it ascended into the heavens: And I saw the holy sons of Elohim (God). They were stepping on flames of fire: Their garments were white [and their raiment], And their faces shone like snow.$n$,false),
(21398,'S',71,7,70,4,$n$Hebrews 12:23 — *To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to Elohim (God) the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect.* The spirits of just men made perfect are the very first fathers and righteous Enoch sees dwelling in that place in 70:4.$n$,$n$And there I saw the first fathers and the righteous who from the beginning dwell in that place.$n$,false),
(22568,'S',80,4,80,3,$n$Isaiah 24:4 — *The earth mourneth and fadeth away, the world languisheth and fadeth away, the haughty people of the earth do languish.* The earth's fruits held back in Enoch 80:3 are Isaiah's mourning, fading world languishing under inhabitants who broke the everlasting covenant.$n$,$n$And in those times the fruits of the earth shall be backward, And shall not grow in their time, And the fruits of the trees shall be withheld in their time.$n$,false),
(23822,'S',84,3,9,5,$n$Daniel 4:35 — *And all the inhabitants of the earth are reputed as nothing: and he doeth according to his will in the army of heaven, and among the inhabitants of the earth: and none can stay his hand, or say unto him, What doest thou?* Enoch's 'Thou hast power over all things' is Daniel's 'none can stay his hand.'$n$,$n$Thou hast made all things, and power over all things hast Thou: and all things are naked and open in Thy sight, and Thou seest all things, and nothing can hide itself from Thee.$n$,false),
(23846,'S',85,7,85,8,$n$Jubilees 4:7 — *And Adam and his wife mourned for Abel four weeks of years, and in the fourth year of the fifth week they became joyful, and Adam knew his wife again, and she bare him a son, and he called his name Seth; for he said “Elohim (God) has raised up a second seed to us on the earth instead of Abel; for Cain slew him.”* Jubilees tells the comfort after the lament that Enoch shows as the cow quieted and bearing the second white bull.$n$,$n$And after that she bore another white bull, and after him she bore many bulls and black cows.$n$,false),
(23847,'S',85,7,85,8,$n$Genesis 4:26 — *And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of Yahuah (LORD).* The many white bulls proceeding from the second white bull are the righteous Sethite line that called on the name of Yahuah.$n$,$n$And after that she bore another white bull, and after him she bore many bulls and black cows.$n$,false),
(23848,'S',85,7,85,8,$n$Genesis 4:25 — *And Adam knew his wife again; and she bare a son, and called his name Seth: For Elohim (God), said she, hath appointed me another seed instead of Abel, whom Cain slew.* The second white bull the cow bears is Seth, the seed appointed in Abel's place.$n$,$n$And after that she bore another white bull, and after him she bore many bulls and black cows.$n$,false),
(23849,'S',85,5,85,6,$n$Hebrews 12:24 — *And to Yahusha (Jesus) the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.* The great lamentation over the red bull is answered at last by a better blood than Abel's.$n$,$n$And that cow, that first one, went from the presence of that first bull in order to seek that red one, but found him not, and lamented with a great lamentation over him and sought him.$n$,false),
(23850,'S',85,5,85,6,$n$Matthew 23:35 — *That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar.* Abel's blood, the herd's first lament, heads the whole tally of righteous blood spilled in the seed-war.$n$,$n$And that cow, that first one, went from the presence of that first bull in order to seek that red one, but found him not, and lamented with a great lamentation over him and sought him.$n$,false),
(23851,'S',85,5,85,6,$n$Hebrews 11:4 — *By faith Abel offered unto Elohim (God) a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, Elohim (God) testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.* The red bull lamented and sought is the righteous Abel who, being dead, yet speaks.$n$,$n$And that cow, that first one, went from the presence of that first bull in order to seek that red one, but found him not, and lamented with a great lamentation over him and sought him.$n$,false),
(23852,'S',85,5,85,6,$n$Genesis 4:10 — *And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother’s blood crieth unto me from the ground.* The cow seeking the red bull and finding him not is Abel gone, his blood crying from the ground.$n$,$n$And that cow, that first one, went from the presence of that first bull in order to seek that red one, but found him not, and lamented with a great lamentation over him and sought him.$n$,false),
(23922,'S',89,49,90,37,$n$Ezekiel 34:23 — *And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.* The white bull born with great horns whom all the beasts fear (90:37) is the one Shepherd, the Messiah, set over the regathered flock.$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$,false),
(23945,'S',90,20,90,37,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* The great white bull born at the end is the same dominion-bearer Daniel sees as one like the Son of Adam, the Formed One who took on flesh (note the kaph-comparative, like).$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$,false),
(23946,'S',90,20,90,37,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* All the beasts and birds fearing the white bull and petitioning him is the dominion given to the Son of Adam that all nations should serve.$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$,false),
(23947,'S',90,21,90,38,$n$Isaiah 11:6 — *The wolf also shall dwell with the lamb, and the leopard shall lie down with the kid; and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together; and a little child shall lead them.* The transformation of all generations into white bulls is the restored peace where wolf and lamb dwell together.$n$,$n$And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.$n$,false),
(23948,'S',90,21,90,38,$n$Isaiah 65:25 — *The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock: and dust shall be the serpent’s meat. They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain, saith Yahuah (LORD).* The whole flock made white bulls is the new-creation peace where lion and lamb feed together and none hurt in the holy mountain.$n$,$n$And I saw till all their generations were transformed, and they all became white bulls; and the first among them became a lamb, and that lamb became a great animal and had great black horns on its head; and Yahuah (Lord) of the sheep rejoiced over it and over all the oxen.$n$,false),
(23949,'S',90,20,90,37,$n$Genesis 1:26 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.* The great white bull crowning the seed-line restores the dominion first given to Adam in God's image.$n$,$n$And I saw that a white bull was born, with large horns, and all the beasts of the field and all the birds of the air feared him and made petition to him all the time.$n$,false),
(25361,'S',95,7,97,8,$n$Jeremiah 17:11 — *As the partridge sitteth on eggs, and hatcheth them not; so he that getteth riches, and not by right, shall leave them in the midst of his days, and at his end shall be a fool.* — riches acquired in unrighteousness (Enoch 97:8) end in folly and loss.$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25379,'S',96,5,97,8,$n$Luke 12:19 — *And I will say to my soul, Soul, thou hast much goods laid up for many years; take thine ease, eat, drink, and be merry.* The fool's self-talk matches the boast Enoch puts in the rich man's mouth — we have acquired everything we desired (97:8).$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25381,'S',96,5,97,8,$n$Amos 8:5 — *Saying, When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn? and the sabbath, that we may set forth wheat, making the ephah small, and the shekel great, and falsifying the balances by deceit?* Amos shows the rigged scales by which the gold of 97:8 was acquired in unrighteousness.$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25403,'S',97,7,97,8,$n$James 5:3 — *Your gold and silver is cankered; and the rust of them shall be a witness against you, and shall eat your flesh as it were fire. Ye have heaped treasure together for the last days.* The hoarded silver and gold of Enoch 97:8-8 becomes the very witness that eats the flesh of those who gathered it in unrighteousness.$n$,$n$Woe to you who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say: ‘We have become rich with riches and have possessions; And have acquired everything we have desired.$n$,false),
(25545,'S',108,10,100,6,$n$Isaiah 5:8 — *Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!* Isaiah's woe on the land-grabbing rich is the system Enoch judges, whose riches cannot save in the overthrow of their sins.$n$,$n$And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.$n$,false),
(25550,'S',108,13,100,9,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* The furnace for the tares answers Enoch's sinners burning *worse than fire* — the dark half of the parable whose light half shines the righteous.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye sinners, on account of the words of your mouth, And on account of the deeds of your hands which your godlessness has wrought, In blazing flames burning worse than fire shall ye burn.$n$,false),
(25551,'S',108,13,100,9,$n$Isaiah 66:24 — *And they shall go forth, and look upon the carcases of the men that have transgressed against me: for their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched; and they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh.* The unquenchable fire that closes Isaiah is the *blazing flames burning worse than fire* that close Enoch.$n$,$n$Woe to you, ye sinners, on account of the words of your mouth, And on account of the deeds of your hands which your godlessness has wrought, In blazing flames burning worse than fire shall ye burn.$n$,false),
(25552,'S',108,9,100,5,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* The parallel extra-canon resurrection hope matches Enoch's wise shining in security after the long sleep.$n$,$n$And over all the righteous and holy He will appoint guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye, Until He makes an end of all wickedness and all sin, And though the righteous sleep a long sleep, they have nought to fear.$n$,false),
(25554,'S',108,10,100,6,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* Enoch's *wise* seen *in security* are Daniel's wise who shine as the firmament.$n$,$n$And (then) the children of the earth shall see the wise in security, And shall understand all the words of this book, And recognize that their riches shall not be able to save them In the overthrow of their sins.$n$,false),
(25555,'S',108,9,100,5,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* Enoch's *long sleep* with *nought to fear* is Daniel's dust-sleep ending in everlasting life for the kept righteous.$n$,$n$And over all the righteous and holy He will appoint guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye, Until He makes an end of all wickedness and all sin, And though the righteous sleep a long sleep, they have nought to fear.$n$,false),
(25556,'S',108,9,100,5,$n$Psalm 17:8 — *Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,* the believer's prayer for exactly the guarding Enoch promises the holy ones.$n$,$n$And over all the righteous and holy He will appoint guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye, Until He makes an end of all wickedness and all sin, And though the righteous sleep a long sleep, they have nought to fear.$n$,false);
INSERT INTO _s463m VALUES
(27,4255,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The name given at Matthew 1:21 was named before the Head of Days.$n$),
(27,4257,$n$1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* The Formed one, hidden before creation, revealed as Emmanuel.$n$),
(71,4390,$n$1 Enoch 46:1 — *with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man.* The Head of Days and the one beside him; the Son of Adam of Matthew 8:20 is that one.$n$),
(71,4392,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness … whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The title by which Yahusha (Jesus) names himself at Matthew 8:20, given to Enoch by the angel.$n$),
(96,4409,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The one named before creation is the one with power on earth to forgive sins (Matthew 9:6).$n$),
(115,4455,$n$1 Enoch 99:5 — *they shall abandon their children.* The household comes apart in the day of destruction; Matthew 10:35 says the King's voice divides it too.$n$),
(115,4456,$n$1 Enoch 100:1 — *the fathers together with their sons shall be smitten And brothers one with another shall fall in death.* The seed war inside one house; *a man's foes shall be they of his own household* (Matthew 10:36).$n$),
(125,4481,$n$1 Enoch 46:1 — *One who had a head of days … And with Him was another being.* Father and Son seen together before the incarnation; Matthew 11:27 names their knowing of each other.$n$),
(125,4482,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *who revealeth all the treasures of that which is hidden.* The Son reveals the hidden Father, to whom he will (Matthew 11:27).$n$),
(125,4483,$n$1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* Known to the Father before anyone else existed; *no man knoweth the Son, but the Father* (Matthew 11:27).$n$),
(125,4484,$n$1 Enoch 48:7 — *the wisdom of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits hath revealed him to the holy and righteous.* The babes of Matthew 11:25 are the holy and righteous whose lot he preserved.$n$),
(186,4502,$n$1 Enoch 49:1 — *wisdom is poured out like water, And glory faileth not before him.* The Spirit put upon the servant (Matthew 12:18; Isaiah 42:1), seen from heaven's side.$n$),
(186,4503,$n$1 Enoch 49:3 — *in him dwells the spirit of wisdom, And the spirit which gives insight, And the spirit of understanding and of might.* Isaiah 11:2's spirits on the Elect One, with the righteous dead added.$n$),
(188,4508,$n$1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The strong man bound (Matthew 12:29) — done in Jared's days, done in Galilee, done again at Revelation 20:2.$n$),
(188,4509,$n$1 Enoch 54:5 — *These are being prepared for the hosts of Azâzêl.* The chains were forged before the King spoke of binding.$n$),
(188,7917,$n$1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The stronger one who overcomes and divides the spoils (Luke 11:22) is doing what Raphael was sent to do.$n$),
(191,4518,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *Sheol also shall give back that which it has received.* The heart of the earth returns the Son of Adam after three days (Matthew 12:40) because the earth returns what it holds.$n$),
(197,4535,$n$1 Enoch 6:2 — *let us choose us wives from among the children of men and beget us children.* The enemy's sowing (Matthew 13:25), told as history.$n$),
(197,4537,$n$1 Enoch 15:8 — *the giants … shall be called evil spirits upon the earth.* The tares' origin; another seed, not bad wheat (Matthew 13:38).$n$),
(199,4542,$n$1 Enoch 104:2 — *ye shall shine as the lights of heaven, ye shall shine and ye shall be seen.* The righteous shining as the sun (Matthew 13:43; Daniel 12:3).$n$),
(200,4544,$n$1 Enoch 48:6 — *chosen and hidden before Him, Before the creation of the world.* The secret kept from the foundation (Matthew 13:35) is the one speaking the parables.$n$),
(202,4554,$n$1 Enoch 100:5 — *guardians from amongst the holy angels To guard them as the apple of an eye.* The angels who guard the just are the angels who sever the wicked from them (Matthew 13:49).$n$),
(224,4599,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* Kefa's (Peter's) confession (Matthew 16:16) recognizes a name given before the world.$n$),
(224,4600,$n$1 Enoch 48:3 — *before the sun and the signs were created … His name was named.* What the Father revealed to Kefa (Peter) (Matthew 16:17) is older than the stars.$n$),
(227,4613,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* Why the gates of hell cannot prevail (Matthew 16:18).$n$),
(371,4678,$n$1 Enoch 10:8 — *the whole earth has been corrupted through the works that were taught by Azâzêl.* Why offences must come (Matthew 18:7) — and why the man they come by still answers.$n$),
(371,4679,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray.* Leading astray is the offence; the woe is for the leaders, the led are victims (Matthew 18:7).$n$),
(371,4681,$n$1 Enoch 27:2 — *This accursed valley is for those who are accursed for ever.* The valley Enoch saw is the Gehenna of Matthew 18:9 — a real place of judgment.$n$),
(372,4684,$n$1 Enoch 90:6 — *lambs were borne by those white sheep, and they began to open their eyes and to see.* The Father's will that none of the little ones perish (Matthew 18:14): the lambs that can open their eyes do.$n$),
(379,4714,$n$1 Enoch 98:10 — *ye know no ransom.* Riches cannot save; the disciples' *who then can be saved?* (Matthew 19:25) already answered.$n$),
(382,4727,$n$1 Enoch 48:1 — *all the thirsty drank of them … And their dwellings were with the righteous and holy and elect.* Many drink; the few are those already dwelling with the elect (Matthew 20:16).$n$),
(384,4734,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness … whose lot hath the pre-eminence.* The pre-eminent one came to serve and give his life (Matthew 20:28).$n$),
(384,4735,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — *that Son of Adam was named In the presence of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The ransom (Matthew 20:28) was settled before the world; *the Lamb slain from the foundation* (Revelation 13:8).$n$),
(395,4780,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The half of the answer the Pharisees did not have at Matthew 22:42.$n$),
(395,4781,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — *his name before the Head of Days.* Why David calls his descendant *my Lord* (Matthew 22:43): the descendant is older than David.$n$),
(397,4791,$n$1 Enoch 99:2 — *Woe to them who pervert the words of uprightness, And transgress the eternal law, And transform themselves into what they were not.* The proselyte made twofold a child of hell (Matthew 23:15).$n$),
(401,4806,$n$1 Enoch 10:2 — *Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!”* The days of Noah (Matthew 24:37): a corrupted earth, a warning to the few, a day the many do not see.$n$),
(402,4811,$n$1 Enoch 57:1 — *coming on the winds from the east, and from the west to the south.* The coming of the Son of Adam fills the sky (Matthew 24:27); nothing secret about it.$n$),
(402,4812,$n$1 Enoch 57:2 — *the sound thereof was heard from the one end of heaven to the other.* Matthew 24:31's phrase, and the gathering it describes.$n$),
(402,4813,$n$1 Enoch 61:5 — *those who have been devoured by the fish of the sea, That they may return … For none shall be destroyed before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The four winds give back the seed they took (Matthew 24:31).$n$),
(411,4851,$n$1 Enoch 46:4 — *Shall raise up the kings and the mighty from their seats.* The council that sentenced him (Matthew 26:64) will be raised from its seats by him.$n$),
(411,4852,$n$1 Enoch 48:3 — *His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* The Father named the Son before the world; the Sanhedrin's verdict (Matthew 26:64–66) does not.$n$),
(423,4898,$n$1 Enoch 51:1 — *the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it.* The firstfruits walked out (Matthew 28:6); all power follows (Matthew 28:18).$n$),
(423,4899,$n$1 Enoch 51:2 — *he shall choose the righteous and holy from among them.* The sifting after the gathering, done by the one given all power (Matthew 28:18). The tares were never wheat; the wheat is sifted.$n$),
(629,7878,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *whose lot hath the pre-eminence before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits in uprightness for ever.* The right hand of power (Mark 14:62) is that pre-eminence.$n$),
(649,7944,$n$1 Enoch 10:2 — *reveal to him the end that is approaching: that the whole earth will be destroyed.* The days of Noah (Luke 17:26): a warning carried to one man over a corrupted earth.$n$),
(649,7943,$n$1 Enoch 10:3 — *that he may escape and his seed may be preserved for all the generations of the world.* Two outcomes at the flood, two in the days of the Son of Adam (Luke 17:27).$n$),
(665,7993,$n$1 Enoch 48:3 — *before the sun and the signs were created, Before the stars of the heaven were made, His name was named.* Before Avraham (Abraham), before the stars — *I am* (John 8:58).$n$),
(2063,15033,$n$1 Enoch 18:12 — *a place which had no firmament of the heaven above, and no firmly founded earth beneath it.* The bottomless pit the fallen star is given the key to (Revelation 9:1).$n$),
(5164,25558,$n$1 Enoch 48:3 — *His name was named before Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits.* Names were written before the world; chapter 108 blots them out; nothing adds one.$n$),
(5188,25629,$n$1 Enoch 13:8 — *I saw visions of chastisement, and a voice came bidding (me) I to tell it to the sons of heaven.* The scribe-of-judgment commission of Jubilees 4:23, from the inside.$n$),
(5189,25627,$n$1 Enoch 6:6 — *who descended in the days of Jared on the summit of Mount Hermon.* The same generation Jubilees 4:15 names, with the place and the number.$n$),
(5190,25648,$n$1 Enoch 7:4 — *the giants turned against them and devoured mankind.* The devouring of Jubilees 5:2, with its cause.$n$),
(5191,25653,$n$1 Enoch 10:3 — *that he may escape and his seed may be preserved.* What the grace Noah found (Jubilees 5:5) looked like as an order.$n$),
(5192,25656,$n$1 Enoch 10:9 — *send them one against the other that they may destroy each other in battle.* The sword of Jubilees 5:9 is Gabriel's commission.$n$),
(5263,25900,$n$1 Enoch 10:6 — *on the day of the great judgement he shall be cast into the fire.* The day of Jubilees 9:15's oath; the same fire.$n$),
(5264,25928,$n$1 Enoch 15:8 — *the giants … shall be called evil spirits upon the earth.* The unclean demons of Jubilees 10:1 are the dead giants' spirits.$n$),
(5276,25953,$n$1 Enoch 19:1 — *their spirits assuming many different forms are defiling mankind and shall lead them astray.* The spirits Abram prays to be kept from after turning from the stars (Jubilees 12:17–20).$n$),
(5292,26002,$n$1 Enoch 99:7 — *those who worship impure spirits and demons … shall get no manner of help from them.* The spirits set over the nations (Jubilees 15:31) are the tenants of the idols.$n$),
(5294,26034,$n$1 Enoch 10:13 — *led off to the abyss of fire: and to the torment and the prison.* A sentence written before the day, as Sodom's was engraven (Jubilees 16:9).$n$),
(6192,29171,$n$1 Enoch 10:2 — *Go to Noah and tell him in my name “Hide thyself!”* The warning Jasher 5:25 reports, with the messenger named.$n$),
(14877,60445,$n$1 Enoch 10:4 — *Bind Azâzêl hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness.* The chains of darkness of 2 Peter 2:4, written out in full.$n$),
(30425,4392,$n$1 Enoch 46:3 — *This is the Son of Adam who hath righteousness.* The library's own naming of the Son of Adam beside the Head of Days — the figure of Daniel 7, named.$n$),
(30915,4599,$n$1 Enoch 48:2 — the Son of Adam named before the Head of Days; the Father reveals on earth what he named in heaven.$n$),
(35119,141653,$n$1 Enoch 15:3 — *Wherefore have ye left the high, holy, and eternal heaven.* The folly the angels were charged with (Job 4:18), spoken to their faces.$n$),
(2682,16045,$n$Genesis 9:4 — *But flesh with the life thereof, which is the blood thereof, shall ye not eat.* The blood-drinking of 1 Enoch 7:5 is the exact corruption the Creator forbids to the renewed post-flood earth.$n$),
(2682,16044,$n$Leviticus 17:14 — *For it is the life of all flesh; the blood of it is for the life thereof: therefore I said unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), Ye shall eat the blood of no manner of flesh: for the life of all flesh is the blood thereof: whosoever eateth it shall be cut off.* The Torah's standing blood statute marks the very line the giants of 1 Enoch 7:5 crossed when they devoured flesh and drank blood.$n$),
(2682,16043,$n$Jubilees 7:24 — *And after this they sinned against the beasts and birds, and all that moves and walks on the earth: and much blood was shed on the earth, and every imagination and desire of men imagined vanity and evil continually.* Jubilees records the same sinning against beasts and birds and the much blood shed that 1 Enoch 7:4-5 describes.$n$),
(2683,16042,$n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* The Torah's verdict on the same generation whose lawlessness makes the earth itself lay accusation in 1 Enoch 7:6.$n$),
(2683,16040,$n$Jubilees 7:25 — *And Yahuah (God) destroyed everything from off the face of the earth; because of the wickedness of their deeds, and because of the blood which they had shed in the midst of the earth He destroyed everything.* Jubilees names the shed blood as the very ground of the judgment the earth's accusation in 1 Enoch 7:6 calls for.$n$),
(2685,16061,$n$Jeremiah 10:2 — *Thus saith Yahuah (LORD), Learn not the way of the heathen, and be not dismayed at the signs of heaven; for the heathen are dismayed at them.* The astrology and the signs of the sun and moon that the Watchers teach in 1 Enoch 8:3 are exactly the signs of heaven the prophet warns Yashar'el not to learn.$n$),
(2685,16060,$n$Jubilees 8:3 — *And he found a writing which former (generations) had carved on the rock, and he read what was thereon, and he transcribed it and sinned owing to it; for it contained the teaching of the Watchers in accordance with which they used to observe the omens of the sun and moon and stars in all the signs of heaven.* Jubilees traces the very star-lore of 1 Enoch 8:3 to a surviving Watcher-tablet that re-corrupted men after the Flood.$n$),
(2687,16054,$n$Genesis 4:10 — *And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother's blood crieth unto me from the ground.* The cry of those perishing that goes up to heaven in 1 Enoch 8:4 is the same cry of innocent blood that the LORD hears from the ground.$n$),
(2687,16053,$n$Exodus 2:23 — *And it came to pass in process of time, that the king of Egypt died: and the children of Yashar'el (Israel) sighed by reason of the bondage, and they cried, and their cry came up unto Elohim (God) by reason of the bondage.* The cry going up to heaven in 1 Enoch 8:4 is the same cry of the oppressed that comes up unto Elohim and moves Him to deliver.$n$),
(2738,16279,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* This is the very defilement Michael is sent to punish in Enoch 10:11 — the Watchers who united themselves with women.$n$),
(2738,16278,$n$Genesis 6:3 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.* Yahuah's (the LORD's) sentence that man's days be a hundred and twenty is of a piece with his word to Gabriel over the Watchers' children: *for length of days shall they not have* (10:9).$n$),
(2738,16276,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment.* Peter and Enoch 10:12 give the same verdict: the sinning angels are bound fast and reserved unto judgement.$n$),
(2738,16275,$n$Jubilees 5:6 — *And against the angels whom He had sent upon the earth, He was exceedingly wroth, and He gave commandment to root them out of all their dominion, and He bade us to bind them in the depths of the earth, and behold they are bound in the midst of them, and are (kept) separate.* Jubilees tells the same binding Michael is commanded to perform in Enoch 10:12, in the depths of the earth.$n$),
(2738,16274,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* Isaiah lifts the binding of the Watchers in Enoch 10:12 to the day of judgement, when the host of the high ones is finally visited.$n$),
(2750,16297,$n$Jubilees 5:10 — *And their fathers were witnesses (of their destruction), and after this they were bound in the depths of the earth for ever, until the day of the great condemnation when judgment is executed on all those who have corrupted their ways and their works before Yahuah (God).* Why the petition Enoch read at the waters of Dan till he fell asleep (13:7) fails — the Watcher-fathers are bound, not forgiven.$n$),
(2751,16327,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The throne like the fiery flame with wheels as burning fire is the lofty throne Enoch saw — its appearance as crystal, its wheels as the shining sun, and the cherubim about it (14:18).$n$),
(2751,16326,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The fiery stream that issued from before the Ancient of days is the stream Enoch saw: from underneath the throne came streams of flaming fire, so that he could not look on it (14:19).$n$),
(2751,16325,$n$Revelation 4:2 — *And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.* John is carried up in the spirit to the same enthroned glory Enoch is carried up to see in 18:8, the one throne that stands from his vision to John's.$n$),
(2752,16324,$n$Genesis 1:2 — *And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of Elohim (God) moved upon the face of the waters.* The 'waste and horrible place' with no firmament and no founded earth is the tohu-and-bohu of creation's first verse — the un-ordered ground that lies outside the Creator's order in 18:12.$n$),
(2752,16323,$n$Jeremiah 4:23 — *I beheld the earth, and, lo, it was without form, and void; and the heavens, and they had no light.* Jeremiah sees creation rolled back to formlessness under judgement — the same waste place with no firmament above that Enoch is shown in 18:12.$n$),
(2752,16322,$n$Jeremiah 4:25 — *I beheld, and, lo, there was no man, and all the birds of the heavens were fled.* The fled birds match Enoch's place where 'there was no water upon it, and no birds' (18:12) — the desolation that mirrors the place of imprisonment.$n$),
(2753,16320,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* The shutting-up in prison until a later visitation is exactly Enoch's binding of the stars 'till the time when their guilt should be consummated' in 18:16.$n$),
(2753,16318,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude names the prisoners as the rebel angels reserved in chains until the judgment — the same binding 'till the time when their guilt should be consummated' Enoch records in 18:16.$n$),
(2754,16314,$n$Genesis 1:16 — *And Elohim (God) made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.* The stars the Creator made to rule their courses are the very stars that transgressed His commandment in the beginning of their rising in 18:15.$n$),
(2757,16334,$n$Matthew 12:43 — *When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and findeth none.* The restless, earth-bound spirit Yahusha (Jesus) describes is exactly Enoch 15:8's giant-spirit whose dwelling is on the earth, seeking a body and finding no true home.$n$),
(2757,16333,$n$Jubilees 10:1 — *And in the third week of this jubilee the unclean demons began to lead astray the children of the sons of Noah; and to make to err and destroy them.* Jubilees shows the spirits of Enoch 15:9 already at work after the Flood — the surviving giant-spirits leading astray and destroying mankind.$n$),
(2757,16332,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 14:6 — *For in the old time also, when the proud giants perished, the hope of the world governed by your hand escaped in a weak vessel, and left to all ages a seed of generation.* Wisdom remembers the proud giants of Enoch 15:8 perishing in the Flood while righteous seed was preserved in the ark.$n$),
(2758,16330,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude's 'judgment of the great day' is Enoch 16:1's 'great judgement in which the age shall be consummated, over the Watchers and the godless.'$n$),
(2759,16354,$n$Genesis 6:2 — *That the sons of Elohim (God) saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.* The Watchers' "union" with women in Enoch 15:4 is Moses' sons-of-Elohim taking wives of the daughters of men.$n$),
(2759,16353,$n$Genesis 6:4 — *There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of Elohim (God) came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown.* The defilement Enoch names in 15:4 is the very union that produced the giants of Genesis 6.$n$),
(2759,16352,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* Jude reads the Watchers' crossing of the heaven-flesh boundary in Enoch 15:4 as angels abandoning their first estate, reserved for judgment.$n$),
(2843,16679,$n$Deuteronomy 32:22 — *For a fire is kindled in mine anger, and shall burn unto the lowest hell, and shall consume the earth with her increase, and set on fire the foundations of the mountains.* The river of fire that flows like water (1 Enoch 17:5) is the same kindled fire Moses says burns to the lowest depths.$n$),
(2844,16677,$n$Job 38:16 — *Hast thou entered into the springs of the sea? or hast thou walked in the search of the depth?* The place where no flesh walks and the waters of the deep (1 Enoch 17:6-6) are the springs of the sea Yahuah challenges Job to enter.$n$),
(2844,16676,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,* The treasuries of winter's darkness and the waters of the deep that Enoch sees (1 Enoch 17:7) are the hidden treasures Yahuah keeps from Job.$n$),
(2844,16675,$n$Psalms 104:2 — *Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:* The wisdom by which He ordered all creation and founded the world (1 Enoch 18:1) is the psalm's God who stretches out the heavens.$n$),
(2850,16690,$n$Job 38:31 — *Canst thou bind the sweet influences of Pleiades, or loose the bands of Orion?* The fixed star-order Job cannot command is the very order the seven stars transgressed in Enoch 18:15.$n$),
(2850,16689,$n$Job 38:33 — *Knowest thou the ordinances of heaven? canst thou set the dominion thereof in the earth?* The ordinances of heaven the stars broke by not coming forth at their appointed times (Enoch 18:15).$n$),
(2851,16687,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* The host of the high ones Isaiah sees punished are the stars Enoch saw rolling over the fire — the ones who transgressed the commandment of Yahuah (Lord) and did not come forth at their appointed times (18:15).$n$),
(2851,16686,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* Isaiah's prison-pit, holding the host until they are visited, is Enoch's prison for the stars and the host of heaven (18:14), bound till their guilt is consummated (18:14).$n$),
(2852,16682,$n$Revelation 20:3 — *And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season.* The shut-up, sealed pit of John is the prison of the angels Enoch reaches at 21:10 — a holding, kept till the appointed time.$n$),
(2863,16748,$n$Jude 1:13 — *Raging waves of the sea, foaming out their own shame; wandering stars, to whom is reserved the blackness of darkness for ever.* Jude keeps Enoch's very image of the bound seven stars as fallen luminaries reserved in darkness (Enoch 21:3).$n$),
(2864,16746,$n$Luke 16:26 — *And beside all this, between us and you there is a great gulf fixed: so that they which would pass from hence to you cannot; neither can they pass to us, that would come from thence.* The fixed gulf in Sheol is Enoch's separated hollow places, the righteous parted from the sinners (Enoch 22:2).$n$),
(2865,16745,$n$Genesis 4:10 — *And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother's blood crieth unto me from the ground.* Enoch 22:7 names the very spirit whose crying blood Genesis records — Abel's suit against Cain, still going up to heaven.$n$),
(2865,16744,$n$Hebrews 12:24 — *And to Yahusha (Jesus) the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.* Hebrews knows Abel's blood still speaks. Enoch heard it: the spirit that went forth from Abel, making his suit against his brother's seed (22:7). The blood of sprinkling answers that suit with a better word.$n$),
(2865,16743,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* The martyrs' cry for vengeance is Enoch's suit of the dead going forth to heaven (Enoch 22:5), still awaiting the appointed reckoning.$n$),
(2867,16763,$n$Psalms 19:4 — *Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,* The same sun for which Yahuah (LORD) appointed a tabernacle is the one whose setting Raguel's fire in the west receives (23:4).$n$),
(2867,16760,$n$Psalms 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:* The fire in the west that pursues the luminaries (23:4) is no rebel flame but a minister of Yahuah (LORD), set to its task like his flaming servants.$n$),
(2867,16759,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The sun knowing its going down is the sun Raguel's fire in the west receives — the fire which persecutes all the luminaries of heaven (23:4).$n$),
(2870,16779,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* Daniel's fiery seat of the Ancient of days is Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3), where the Eternal King will sit when He comes down to visit the earth.$n$),
(2870,16778,$n$Ezekiel 28:14 — *Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of Elohim (God); thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.* Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3) is the canon's own holy mountain of Elohim, the Eden-sanctuary from which the covering cherub fell.$n$),
(2870,16776,$n$Jubilees 4:25 — *For Yahuah (God) has four places on the earth, the Garden of Eden, and the Mount of the East, and this mountain on which you are this day, Mount Sinai, and Mount Zion (which) will be sanctified in the new creation for a sanctification of the earth; through it will the earth be sanctified from all (its) guilt and its uncleanness throughout the generations of the world.* Jubilees counts Enoch's throne-mountain (25:3) among Yahuah's holy places on earth, sanctified in the new creation.$n$),
(2871,16770,$n$2 Esdras 8:52 — *For to you is paradise opened, the tree of life is planted, the time to come is prepared, plenteousness is made ready, a city is builded, and rest is allowed, yes, perfect goodness and wisdom.* 2 Esdras pairs the planted tree of life with the builded city exactly as Enoch's tree is transplanted to the holy place, the temple of the Eternal King (25:5).$n$),
(2872,16769,$n$Revelation 22:14 — *Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.* The right to Enoch's reserved tree of life (25:5) belongs to those who do Yahuah's commandments — Torah standing, the elect keeping the way into the holy place.$n$),
(2872,16768,$n$Isaiah 65:22 — *They shall not build, and another inhabit; they shall not plant, and another eat: for as the days of a tree are the days of my people, and mine elect shall long enjoy the work of their hands.* Isaiah measures the elect's days by a tree, exactly as Enoch's tree gives *fruit shall be for food to the elect* (25:5).$n$),
(2872,16767,$n$2 Esdras 2:12 — *They shall have the tree of life for an ointment of sweet savour; they shall neither labour, nor be weary.* The tree's sweet-savour healing laid up for the righteous matches Enoch's fragrant tree reserved till the great judgement, whose fragrance shall be in their bones (25:4).$n$),
(2873,16766,$n$Isaiah 25:8 — *He will swallow up death in victory; and Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) will wipe away tears from off all faces; and the rebuke of his people shall he take away from off all the earth: for Yahuah (LORD) hath spoken it.* The end of all sorrow and torment Enoch promises the elect (25:6) is Isaiah's swallowing-up of death and wiping of every tear.$n$),
(2873,16765,$n$Revelation 21:4 — *And Elohim (God) shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.* John's restored creation where no sorrow or pain remains is Enoch's promise that *no sorrow or plague or torment or calamity* shall touch the elect (25:6).$n$),
(2873,16764,$n$Revelation 22:3 — *And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him.* The lifted curse and the throne in the holy place answer Enoch's long restful life entered into the holy place by the tree (25:6).$n$),
(2972,17149,$n$Ezekiel 47:12 — *And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.* Ezekiel sees trees lining both sides of the sanctuary-stream — Enoch saw fragrant cinnamon on the sides of the valleys of the holy mountain (30:3).$n$),
(2974,17164,$n$Zechariah 14:4 — *And his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives, which is before Jerusalem on the east, and the mount of Olives shall cleave in the midst thereof toward the east and toward the west, and there shall be a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.* Zechariah's day of the King standing on the mountain east of Jerusalem matches the mountain Michael names — the throne where the Holy Great One will sit when he comes down to visit the earth with goodness (25:3).$n$),
(2983,17201,$n$Song of Solomon 4:14 — *Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:* The bride's garden has aloes among its chief spices; Enoch found a whole mountain of aloe-trees at the east of the ends of the earth, their trees full of stacte (31:2).$n$),
(2983,17200,$n$Exodus 30:23 — *Take thou also unto thee principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred shekels, and of sweet cinnamon half so much, even two hundred and fifty shekels, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty shekels,* Enoch found cinnamon on the sides of the valleys (30:3) — one of the principal spices Yahuah (LORD) set apart for the holy anointing oil.$n$),
(2985,17192,$n$Ezekiel 47:12 — *And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.* Ezekiel's healing trees flowing from the sanctuary match the temple-tree of Enoch 25:6 whose fragrance brings life and ends all plague.$n$),
(2986,17209,$n$Exodus 30:34 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:* The galbanum that flows as nectar from the groves Enoch saw (31:1) is one of the sweet spices Yahuah (LORD) named for the holy incense.$n$),
(2986,17208,$n$Song of Solomon 3:6 — *Who is this that cometh out of the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all powders of the merchant?* The myrrh and frankincense that herald the Bridegroom are what Enoch's aromatic trees exhale (29:2).$n$),
(2999,17259,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail,* The frost and snow that come through Enoch's north portals (34:2) are drawn from these treasuries no man has entered.$n$),
(3002,17272,$n$Revelation 7:1 — *And after these things I saw four angels standing on the four corners of the earth, holding the four winds of the earth, that the wind should not blow on the earth, nor on the sea, nor on any tree.* John sees four angels holding the four winds at the four corners of the earth; Enoch was shown the twelve portals at the ends of the earth, open to all the quarters, from which the winds go forth (76:1).$n$),
(3168,17925,$n$Matthew 13:35 — *That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world.* Yahusha's parable-speech unveils what was kept secret, exactly as Enoch's vision of wisdom is reserved 'not for this generation' (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$),
(3168,17924,$n$Deuteronomy 29:29 — *The secret things belong unto Yahuah Eloheinu (the LORD our God): but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.* The Torah's sealed-versus-revealed line is the very frame of Enoch's wisdom withheld from former generations and granted to the elect (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$),
(3168,17923,$n$Matthew 11:25 — *At that time Yahusha (Jesus) answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Yahuah (Lord) of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.* The Father's selective unveiling to the chosen is Enoch's parable spoken 'concerning the elect' (1 Enoch 1:3).$n$),
(3168,17922,$n$1 Corinthians 2:7 — *But we speak the wisdom of Elohim (God) in a mystery, even the hidden wisdom, which Elohim (God) ordained before the world unto our glory.* Paul's hidden wisdom ordained before the world matches Enoch's vision of wisdom held back for the generation 'which is for to come' (1 Enoch 1:2).$n$),
(3172,17940,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* Wisdom's persecuted elect shining at their visitation is Enoch's congregation of the righteous appearing while the sinners are judged and driven from the face of the earth (38:1).$n$),
(3174,17935,$n$Isaiah 53:11 — *He shall see of the travail of his soul, and shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.* Isaiah's righteous servant who justifies many is the Righteous One who appears before the eyes of the righteous in Enoch's first parable (38:2).$n$),
(3174,17934,$n$Isaiah 26:2 — *Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.* Isaiah's righteous nation that keeps the truth is the congregation of the righteous and elect who are victorious in the name of Yahuah of Spirits (50:2).$n$),
(3175,17932,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* John's kings and mighty men hiding in terror are Enoch's kings of the earth downcast in countenance on the day of their anguish, unable to save themselves (48:8).$n$),
(3175,17931,$n$Revelation 6:17 — *For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?* The great day before which no power can stand is Enoch's day when the kings and the mighty go out from his presence with their faces filled with shame (62:10).$n$),
(3175,17930,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) furnace of fire for the children of the wicked one is the burning furnace the four archangels cast the hosts of Azazel into on the great day (54:6).$n$),
(3176,17928,$n$Revelation 20:11 — *And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.* The throne from whose face earth and heaven flee is the presence Enoch sees the godless driven from — away from the righteous and the elect (38:3).$n$),
(3176,17927,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The books opened and the dead judged by their works is the hour Enoch names: the secrets of the righteous revealed and the sinners judged (38:3).$n$),
(3176,17926,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* Daniel's two-fold awaking, to life or to shame, is Enoch's parting of the righteous made victorious from the sinners bound and cast into the furnace (69:28).$n$),
(3177,17959,$n$John 14:2 — *In my Father's house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.* Yahusha (Jesus) names the dwelling-places Enoch's spirit longed for — *there I wished to dwell, and my spirit longed for that dwelling-place* (39:8) — and says he goes ahead to prepare them.$n$),
(3177,17958,$n$Revelation 7:15 — *Therefore are they before the throne of Elohim (God), and serve him day and night in his temple: and he that sitteth on the throne shall dwell among them.* John sees the righteous lodged with the holy before the throne, the same resting-places among His angels that Enoch saw in 1 Enoch 39:5.$n$),
(3177,17957,$n$Revelation 21:3 — *And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of Elohim (God) is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God).* John hears the tabernacle of Elohim (God) with men; Enoch saw the Elect One of righteousness with the righteous and the elect without number before him for ever and ever (39:6).$n$),
(3178,17956,$n$Isaiah 42:1 — *Behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, in whom my soul delighteth; I have put my spirit upon him: he shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles.* Isaiah's *mine elect* is Enoch's *Mine Elect One* (45:3) — the chosen servant in whom the Father delights, set on the throne of glory.$n$),
(3179,17952,$n$Amos 5:24 — *But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.* Amos's flowing waters of righteousness are the very stream Enoch sees pour before the holy in 1 Enoch 39:5.$n$),
(3179,17951,$n$Revelation 22:1 — *And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of Elohim (God) and of the Lamb.* The water-like righteousness flowing in 1 Enoch 39:5 has its source in the river that proceeds from the throne of the Father and the Lamb.$n$),
(3181,17946,$n$Revelation 4:8 — *And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Yahuah Elohim (Lord God) Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.* John's four living creatures praising ceaselessly about the throne are Enoch's four presences who surround the throne of glory and praise in 1 Enoch 40:2.$n$),
(3187,17981,$n$Matthew 10:26 — *Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and hid, that shall not be known.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) promise that every hidden thing shall be uncovered is Enoch's hour when the secrets of the righteous are revealed and the sinners judged (38:3).$n$),
(3191,17987,$n$1 Timothy 2:5 — *For there is one Elohim (God), and one mediator between Elohim (God) and men, the man HaMashiach Yahusha (Christ Jesus);* No angel hinders, no power hinders; he judges them all before him (41:9). The one mediator between that judge and men is not an angel but the Formed Son come in flesh.$n$),
(3191,17986,$n$Hebrews 7:25 — *Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto Elohim (God) by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.* Enoch is told no angel hinders and no power can — he himself appoints the judge and judges all (41:9). The intercession that reaches that throne is the Son's, who ever lives to make it for those who come to the Father by him.$n$),
(3191,17985,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* He who judges them all before him in Enoch (41:9) is the One whose opened books judge the dead by their works.$n$),
(3195,18004,$n$Sirach 24:8 — *So the Creator of all things gave me a commandment, and he that made me caused my tabernacle to rest, and said, Let your dwelling be in Jacob, and your inheritance in Yashar'el (Israel).* Wisdom, denied a dwelling among men, is given her resting-place in Jacob — the elect over whom Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits abides and with whom the Son of Adam eats for ever (62:14).$n$),
(3195,18003,$n$Revelation 21:3 — *And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of Elohim (God) is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and Elohim (God) himself shall be with them, and be their Elohim (God).* Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits abiding over his elect, who eat and lie down and rise up with the Son of Adam for ever (62:14), is the tabernacle of Elohim (God) finally set among his people.$n$),
(3196,18002,$n$Psalm 114:4 — *The mountains skipped like rams, and the little hills like lambs.* The Exodus-redemption image of leaping hills is the exact figure Enoch uses in 51:4 for creation rejoicing as the righteous are made victorious.$n$),
(3203,18049,$n$Job 38:35 — *Canst thou send lightnings, that they may go, and say unto thee, Here we are?* Yahuah's challenge to Job names the same secret of lightning and thunder Enoch is shown in the storehouses of 41:3.$n$),
(3204,18044,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork* — the lights that praise and rest not before Yahuah of Spirits in 41:7 are the same unceasing witness the Psalm hears in the firmament.$n$),
(3204,18043,$n$Jubilees 2:9 — *And Elohim (God) appointed the sun to be a great sign on the earth for days and for sabbaths and for months and for feasts and for years and for sabbaths of years and for jubilees and for all seasons of the years* — the monthly revolution of 41:7 is the very clockwork by which the moedim are appointed.$n$),
(3205,18042,$n$Genesis 1:4 — *And Elohim (God) saw the light, that it was good: and Elohim (God) divided the light from the darkness* The first division of creation is the pattern Enoch extends in 41:8 to the dividing of the spirits of men — the same one who separated light from darkness.$n$),
(3205,18041,$n$Genesis 1:18 — *And to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness: and Elohim (God) saw that it was good* The luminaries themselves are the agents of the division Enoch names in 41:8 — light to the righteous and darkness to the sinners, in the name of him who divided the spirits of men.$n$),
(3433,18933,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) furnace of fire for the wicked is the furnace of fire into which Enoch's sinners' spirits are cast, in shame and slaughter (98:3).$n$),
(3433,18934,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* The righteous shining in the kingdom of their Father are the righteous ones the Father has satisfied with peace and caused to dwell before him, while judgment waits for the sinners (45:6).$n$),
(3433,18935,$n$Malachi 4:1 — *For, behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that cometh shall burn them up, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts), that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.* The wicked as stubble in the burning day is Enoch 48:9's sinners who burn as straw in the fire before the face of the holy, and leave no trace.$n$),
(3433,18936,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* The righteous flaming over the stubble is the bright reverse of Enoch 48:9, where the sinners themselves become the straw that burns.$n$),
(3674,19848,$n$Zechariah 4:7 — *Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.* The valley filled with the elect and beloved when the days of leading astray are ended (56:4) is Zechariah's great mountain flattened to a plain before the chosen one.$n$),
(3675,19870,$n$Isaiah 66:24 — *And they shall go forth, and look upon the carcases of the men that have transgressed against me: for their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched; and they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh.* Isaiah names the never-quenched judgment on the transgressors; Enoch saw the deep valley with open mouths that receives the homage of all the earth and never becomes full (53:1).$n$),
(3676,19869,$n$Isaiah 30:33 — *For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of Yahuah (LORD), like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it.* Isaiah's Tophet, prepared of old for the king, is the very deep furnace whose instruments the angels ready for the kings and mighty in 53:5.$n$),
(3676,19867,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* The furnace into which the workers of iniquity are cast is the destruction the instruments of 53:5 are prepared to accomplish.$n$),
(3676,19865,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 6:6 — *For mercy will soon pardon the meanest: but mighty men shall be mightily tormented.* Wisdom weighs the sentence to the station exactly as 53:5 reserves the instruments for the kings, the mighty, and the exalted.$n$),
(3676,19864,$n$Revelation 19:20 — *These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.* The beast and false prophet — chief of the kings and mighty — are cast into the burning lake the instruments of 53:5 foretell.$n$),
(3677,19863,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* The sinners destroyed before the face of Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits and banished from his earth (53:2) are these kings and mighty men, undone before the face from which they cannot be hidden.$n$),
(3677,19862,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:* The sinners destroyed *before the face of Yahuah of Spirits* (53:2) are those who beg to be hidden from that very face.$n$),
(3677,19861,$n$Isaiah 24:21 — *And it shall come to pass in that day, that Yahuah (LORD) shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.* Isaiah joins the host above and the kings below under one judgement, as 53:2 banishes the oppressors from off the face of His earth.$n$),
(3677,19860,$n$Isaiah 24:22 — *And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.* The pit-prison for the gathered transgressors mirrors the perishing for ever and ever of the sinners in 53:2.$n$),
(3703,19950,$n$Job 38:25 — *Who hath divided a watercourse for the overflowing of waters, or a way for the lightning of thunder;* the dividing of the lightning-and-thunder paths in 41:3 is Yahuah's own ordering of the storm in His answer to Job.$n$),
(3703,19948,$n$Jeremiah 10:13 — *When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens, and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.* The prophet confesses the same wind-out-of-the-treasuries order that the angel shows Enoch in the closed chambers of 41:4.$n$),
(3709,19995,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The Head of Days who names and seats the Elect One in Enoch 61:8 is Daniel's Ancient of days who sits before any other throne is given.$n$),
(3709,19994,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* Daniel sees one *like* the Son of Adam brought near; Enoch names that same One — *that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory* (62:5). Keep the *like*: he resembles mortal man yet remains the Formed cloud-rider.$n$),
(3709,19993,$n$Matthew 25:31 — *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory.* The throne of glory the kings see that Son of Adam sitting on (62:5) is the very throne where Yahusha (Jesus), the Son of Adam, sits to sift the seed gathered out of all nations, the sheep from the goats.$n$),
(3709,19992,$n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.* The judging 'by the way of the righteous judgement' in Enoch 61:9 is Isaiah's Branch who judges in righteousness, not by the sight of the eyes.$n$),
(3710,19991,$n$Matthew 26:64 — *Yahusha (Jesus) saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of Adam sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.* Yahusha (Jesus) owns the very title the angel speaks over him in Enoch's vision: *This is the Son of Adam who is born unto righteousness* (71:14) — named, not merely likened.$n$),
(3711,19988,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* The Son of Adam who casts down kings and kingdoms in Enoch 46:4-6 holds the everlasting dominion Daniel saw given to him by the Ancient of days.$n$),
(3711,19987,$n$Psalm 2:9 — *Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter's vessel.* The Son of Adam who 'put down the kings from their thrones' in Enoch 46:5 is the Psalm's enthroned Son who breaks the raging rulers with the iron rod.$n$),
(3711,19986,$n$Isaiah 45:23 — *I have sworn by myself, the word is gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and shall not return, That unto me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear.* The pride of the mighty abased in Enoch 46:6 ends where every knee bows before the throne of glory.$n$),
(3711,19985,$n$Philippians 2:10 — *That at the name of Yahusha (Jesus) every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth.* Paul names the One before whom the proud of Enoch 46:6 are abased: Yahusha, the Son of Adam exalted by the Father.$n$),
(3712,19983,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.* The mighty whose countenance is covered with shame in Enoch 46:6 beg the rocks to hide them from the face of the enthroned Son of Adam — the wrath of the Lamb.$n$),
(3712,19982,$n$Revelation 1:7 — *Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.* The kings who refused to acknowledge Him in Enoch 46:5 are those who at His coming see Him too late and wail before the throne of glory.$n$),
(3712,19981,$n$Isaiah 52:15 — *So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for that which had not been told them shall they see; and that which they had not heard shall they consider.* The strong abased and silenced in Enoch 46:6 are the kings who shut their mouths before the vindicated Servant.$n$),
(3712,19980,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach.* The shame-covered strong of Enoch 46:6 echo the mockers who, too late, recognize the righteous One they had despised.$n$),
(4030,21287,$n$Proverbs 1:28 — *Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:* The kings' late supplication at the Son of Adam's hands (62:9) is the cry that Wisdom long ago foretold would go unanswered.$n$),
(4030,21286,$n$Luke 13:25 — *When once the master of the house is risen up, and hath shut to the door, and ye begin to stand without, and to knock at the door, saying, Adonai (Lord), Adonai (Lord), open unto us; and he shall answer and say unto you, I know you not whence ye are:* Yahusha's (Jesus's) shut door is Enoch's pressed-out departure (62:10) — the petition is heard but the hour of mercy has passed.$n$),
(4030,21285,$n$Matthew 25:11 — *Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Adonai (Lord), Adonai (Lord), open to us.* The late cry of the foolish virgins matches the kings' too-late worship of that Son of Adam (62:9).$n$),
(4030,21284,$n$Matthew 25:12 — *But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.* The refusal that meets the late virgins is the shame and darkness that meets the kings who supplicate too late (62:9-4).$n$),
(4030,21283,$n$Isaiah 26:10 — *Let favour be shewed to the wicked, yet will he not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness will he deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of Yahuah (LORD).* The wicked who would not learn now confess only under pressure, then go forth in shame (62:10).$n$),
(4031,21282,$n$Daniel 7:13 — *I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* The Head of Days seating the Elect One on the throne of glory (62:2) is Daniel's Ancient of days bringing the one LIKE the Son of Adam near — Enoch names the figure Daniel sees by comparison.$n$),
(4031,21281,$n$Daniel 7:14 — *And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* The Son of Adam driving the sinners from the earth (69:27) exercises the everlasting dominion given Him before the Ancient of days.$n$),
(4031,21280,$n$Isaiah 11:4 — *But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.* The word of His mouth that slays the sinners (62:2) is the rod-of-the-mouth of the Branch from Jesse's stem.$n$),
(4031,21279,$n$Psalms 2:9 — *Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter's vessel.* The Anointed Son who breaks the rebellious kings is the Elect One whose mouth-word slays the sinners (62:2).$n$),
(4031,21278,$n$Matthew 25:31 — *When the Son of Adam shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:* Yahusha (Jesus) names himself the Son of Adam seated on the throne of glory to judge — the seat Yahuah (Lord) of Spirits set him on, where the word of his mouth slays all the sinners (62:2).$n$),
(4032,21277,$n$Revelation 6:15 — *And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;* John's roll of the terrified is Enoch's kings and mighty whose countenance falls when they see the Son of Adam (62:5).$n$),
(4032,21276,$n$Revelation 6:16 — *And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:* The dread before Him that sitteth on the throne is Enoch's terror at seeing that Son of Adam sitting on the throne of his glory (62:5).$n$),
(4032,21275,$n$Revelation 6:17 — *For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?* The day of wrath that none can stand against is Enoch's day when pain comes upon the kings and the mighty as on a woman in travail (62:4).$n$),
(4032,21274,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach:* The wicked's late, useless remorse on beholding the righteous One mirrors the kings' fallen countenance before the Son of Adam (62:5).$n$),
(4032,21273,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:8 — *What has pride profited us? or what good has riches with our vaunting brought us?* The hollow boast of pride and riches is exactly the confession of Enoch's kings: *our hope was in the sceptre of our kingdom, and in our glory* (63:7).$n$),
(4033,21270,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:6 — *Therefore have we erred from the way of truth, and the light of righteousness has not shined to us, and the sun of righteousness rose not upon us.* Those who led the world astray (69:27) confess at last that they themselves erred from the way of truth.$n$),
(4033,21269,$n$Psalms 2:12 — *Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish from the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him.* Passing away from before his face on account of their works (63:9) is the perishing-from-the-way the kings courted by refusing to kiss the Son while there was time.$n$),
(4038,21311,$n$2 Peter 2:3 — *And through covetousness shall they with feigned words make merchandise of you: whose judgment now of a long time lingereth not, and their damnation slumbereth not.* The command that has gone forth from the presence of Yahuah (Lord) — their ruin accomplished because of the secrets they learned (65:6) — is the sentence Peter says lingers not and does not slumber.$n$),
(4039,21308,$n$Genesis 6:12 — *And Elohim (God) looked upon the earth, and, behold, it was corrupt; for all flesh had corrupted his way upon the earth.* The angels who 'corrupted the earth' in Enoch 64:2 are why Moses says all flesh had corrupted its way.$n$),
(4039,21307,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* The descended angels of Enoch 64:2 are the angels Jude says left their habitation and are reserved in chains for judgement.$n$),
(4039,21306,$n$2 Peter 2:4 — *For if Elohim (God) spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment.* Those who showed what was hidden have no place of repentance for ever — *they are the damned* (65:11). Peter's angels that sinned, cast down and reserved unto judgment, are these.$n$),
(4039,21305,$n$Jubilees 5:1 — *And it came to pass when the children of men began to multiply on the face of the earth and daughters were born to them, that the angels of Elohim (God) saw them on a certain year of this jubilee, that they were beautiful to look upon; and they took themselves wives of all whom they chose, and they bare to them sons and they were giants.* The spirits of the giants in Enoch 15:12 are the offspring of the angels Jubilees says took wives and bore giants.$n$),
(4040,21302,$n$Jubilees 5:11 — *And He destroyed all from their places, and there was not left one of them whom He judged not according to all their wickedness. And He made for all His works a new and righteous nature, so that they should not sin in their whole nature for ever, but should be all righteous each in his kind alway.* The earth cleansed and made righteous in Enoch 10:20 is Jubilees' new and righteous nature after the Flood.$n$),
(4040,21301,$n$Genesis 8:21 — *And Yahuah (LORD) smelled a sweet savour; and Yahuah (LORD) said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake; for the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth; neither will I again smite any more every thing living, as I have done.* The cleansed earth of Enoch 10:20 is the ground Yahuah vows not again to curse once the Flood has passed.$n$),
(4044,21318,$n$2 Peter 2:9 — *Yahuah (Lord) knoweth how to deliver the godly out of temptations, and to reserve the unjust unto the day of judgment to be punished.* The same Lord who drowns the ungodly delivers his own, just as Enoch's righteous and elect are saved on that day and never again see the face of the sinners (62:13).$n$),
(4045,21340,$n$Jude 1:6 — *And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.* The reserving of the fallen angels for the judgment of the great day is Enoch's *in those days they shall be led off to the abyss of fire* (10:13) — the prison kept for them till then.$n$),
(4047,21329,$n$Revelation 6:10 — *And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Yahuah (Lord), holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?* The martyrs' cry for their blood to be avenged is Enoch's blood of the righteous "required before Yahuah (God) of Spirits" at 47:4.$n$),
(4048,21327,$n$Isaiah 65:17 — *For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth: and the former shall not be remembered, nor come into mind.* Isaiah's new creation is Enoch's earth cleansed from all unrighteousness and uncleanness (10:20) — the defiled former order wiped away and remembered no more.$n$),
(4048,21326,$n$2 Peter 3:13 — *Nevertheless we, according to his promise, look for new heavens and a new earth, wherein dwelleth righteousness.* Peter's hope of an earth *wherein dwelleth righteousness* is Enoch's earth cleansed from all oppression, all unrighteousness, all sin and all godlessness (10:20).$n$),
(4048,21325,$n$Revelation 21:1 — *And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.* John sees the cleansed creation Enoch foresaw — the corrupted first earth passed away once all sin and iniquity are purged at 10:20.$n$),
(4057,21393,$n$Genesis 5:24 — *And Enoch walked with Elohim (God): and he was not; for Elohim (God) took him.* The canon's single line of Enoch's removal is the event 1 Enoch 71:1 narrates from the inside as his spirit is translated and ascends into the heavens.$n$),
(4057,21392,$n$Hebrews 11:5 — *By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because Elohim (God) had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased Elohim (God).* The New Testament names the manner — translation, not death — which is exactly the "my spirit was translated And it ascended" of 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$),
(4057,21391,$n$Ecclesiasticus 44:16 — *Enoch pleased Yahuah (God), and was translated, being an example of repentance to all generations.* Sirach keeps the same verb "translated" for Enoch's removal that 1 Enoch 71:1 unfolds as an ascent into the heavens.$n$),
(4057,21390,$n$Ecclesiasticus 49:14 — *But upon the earth was no man created like Enoch; for he was taken from the earth.* Sirach marks Enoch's removal as without equal among the earth-born, matching the singular lifting-out narrated in 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$),
(4057,21389,$n$2 Kings 2:11 — *And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, there appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.* Elijah's bodily ascent into heaven is the only canonical parallel to Enoch's translation, and both are surrounded by fire as in 1 Enoch 71:2's two streams of fire.$n$),
(4057,21388,$n$Jubilees 4:23 — *And he was taken from amongst the children of men, and we conducted him into the Garden of Eden in majesty and honour, and behold there he writes down the condemnation and judgment of the world, and all the wickedness of the children of men.* Jubilees confirms Enoch was conducted away to a heavenly dwelling, the same removal 1 Enoch 71:1 describes as his spirit ascending into the heavens.$n$),
(4058,21386,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The fiery stream from the throne matches the two streams of fire Enoch sees in 1 Enoch 71:2 before the Yahuah of Spirits.$n$),
(4058,21385,$n$Revelation 1:14 — *His head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;* John's glorified vision keeps the white-as-snow and flame-of-fire of the throne, the same imagery in which Enoch sees the holy ones with faces shining like snow in 1 Enoch 71:1.$n$),
(4059,21384,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The same archangel Michael who guards the covenant people in Daniel takes Enoch by the right hand to show him the secrets of righteousness in 1 Enoch 71:3.$n$),
(4059,21383,$n$Daniel 10:6 — *His body also was like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.* Daniel's fiery angelic revealer parallels the heavenly guide who shows Enoch the ends of heaven and the chambers of the stars in 1 Enoch 71:4.$n$),
(4061,21408,$n$Psalms 104:4 — *Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire.* Names what the flame-treaders of 71:1 are: ministering servants of fire, not gods — an ordered court under the Creator.$n$),
(4064,21398,$n$Hebrews 12:23 — *To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to Elohim (God) the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect.* The spirits of just men made perfect are the very first fathers and righteous Enoch sees dwelling in that place in 70:4.$n$),
(4065,21396,$n$Job 38:22 — *Hast thou entered into the treasures of the snow? or hast thou seen the treasures of the hail.* The storehouses of the heavens Enoch is shown in 60:12 are the same treasure-chambers Yahuah challenges Job to enter — the Creator's hidden ordering of the elements.$n$),
(4065,21395,$n$Jeremiah 10:13 — *When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens, and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.* The winds brought out of Yahuah's treasures are the storehouses of the winds Enoch sees divided and weighed in 60:12.$n$),
(4065,21394,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The same ordering hand that weighs the winds in 60:12 appoints the lights of the moon — the Creator's measured order, looking ahead to Enoch's Luminaries.$n$),
(4353,22497,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* As fifteen parts of light are transferred to the moon till her light is accomplished according to the sign of the year (78:7), she keeps the seasons she was appointed to mark.$n$),
(4354,22496,$n$Psalm 89:37 — *It shall be established for ever as the moon, and as a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.* The moon Enoch watches wax to fifteen parts and wane part by part (78:7–8) is the heaven's faithful witness — her steady count pledges the steadiness of the covenant.$n$),
(4354,22495,$n$Ecclesiasticus 43:6 — *He made the moon also to serve in her season for a declaration of times, and a sign of the world.* The waning Enoch numbers part by part (78:8) is the moon serving in her season as the declared sign of the times.$n$),
(4356,22510,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The moon accomplishing all her light in the east and all her darkness in the west, by sevenths (74:3), is the Creator's own appointment of the seasons, not a man-made scheme.$n$),
(4356,22509,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork.* The positions and months of the luminaries Uriel showed Enoch and he wrote down (74:2) are the firmament preaching the Maker's handiwork.$n$),
(4357,22507,$n$Jubilees 6:36 — *For there will be those who will assuredly make observations of the moon–now (it) disturbs the seasons and comes in from year to year ten days too soon.* Jubilees names the same shortfall Enoch records — the moon falling behind the sun and the stars, six days every year, thirty in five (74:11). Enoch counts her against the sun; Jubilees counts her ten days short of the 364; both say the moon cannot keep the year.$n$),
(4358,22504,$n$Jubilees 6:35 — *...for the book (lies) written before me, and on the heavenly tables the division of days is ordained, lest they forget the feasts of the covenant and walk according to the feasts of the nations after their error and after their ignorance.* The heavenly tables ordain the division of days so the covenant feasts are kept — the same righteousness Enoch 74:12 demands of the year.$n$),
(4359,22502,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* To change the order of the lights is the enemy's work — the horn who thinks to change the very times and laws Enoch 74:12 says must not be changed.$n$),
(4360,22521,$n$Psalms 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The leaders set over the stars and the four days that divide the year (75:1) keep the very appointment the Psalmist celebrates — the moon for the seasons, the sun for its setting.$n$),
(4360,22520,$n$1 Chronicles 27:1 — *Now the children of Yashar'el (Israel) after their number, to wit, the chief fathers and captains of thousands and hundreds, and their officers that served the king in any matter of the courses, which came in and went out month by month throughout all the months of the year, of every course were twenty and four thousand.* The leaders of the heads of thousands set over the whole creation and the stars, who serve on the four days outside the count of the year (75:1), are mirrored on earth by Israel's courses of captains of thousands — the heavenly ranks ordering time as the priestly ranks order service.$n$),
(4364,22525,$n$Job 37:9 — *Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.* Job sorts the winds by quarter just as Enoch's portals do — the east wind of the first portal bringing desolation, drought, heat, and destruction (76:5), the north portals cold and frost.$n$),
(4367,22539,$n$Genesis 2:9 — *And out of the ground made Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.* Enoch's tree of wisdom in the Garden of Righteousness (32:3) is the Torah's tree set in the midst of the garden.$n$),
(4369,22553,$n$Genesis 1:16 — *And Elohim (God) made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.* Enoch names the sun twice over — Orjârês and Tômâs (78:1) — the greater light of creation week, named out.$n$),
(4369,22551,$n$Psalm 148:5 — *Let them praise the name of Yahuah (LORD): for he commanded, and they were created.* Enoch names the sun by name — Orjârês and Tômâs (78:1); Psalm 148 grounds the naming in the Creator's command that made them.$n$),
(4370,22548,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts.* The sun and the stars completing the years with perfect justice in 364 days (74:12) is the very reckoning Jubilees commands Israel keep so the feasts are not disturbed.$n$),
(4372,22545,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years.* The new moon named on its first day (78:12) is one of the signs and seasons the fourth-day mandate set the lights for.$n$),
(4372,22544,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The first day is called the new moon, for on that day the light rises upon her (78:12) — the moon appointed for the seasons, the Creator's order of the appointed times.$n$),
(4372,22543,$n$Psalm 19:1 — *The heavens declare the glory of Elohim (God); and the firmament sheweth his handywork.* The luminaries that complete their courses in righteousness (Enoch 69:20) are the firmament preaching its Maker's order without a word.$n$),
(4372,22542,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* Where Enoch's sun and moon deviate not from their ordinance from eternity to eternity (69:20), the enemy thinks to change the times — the perversion of the reckoning the luminary book warns against.$n$),
(4374,22563,$n$Psalm 148:3 — *Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.* The sun and the stars that complete the years with perfect justice (74:12) are the chorus the Psalm calls to praise.$n$),
(4375,22558,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts.* The 364 days Enoch counts when the years are full (74:10) is the same reckoning Jubilees commands Israel to keep so the feasts are not disturbed.$n$),
(4375,22557,$n$Jubilees 6:36 — *For there will be those who will assuredly make observations of the moon–now (it) disturbs the seasons and comes in from year to year ten days too soon.* Enoch records the moon falling behind the sun and the order of the stars (79:5) — the disturbance Jubilees warns of when men reckon by the moon alone.$n$),
(4377,22577,$n$Deuteronomy 4:19 — *And lest thou lift up thine eyes unto heaven, and when thou seest the sun, and the moon, and the stars, even all the host of heaven, shouldest be driven to worship them, and serve them, which Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath divided unto all nations under the whole heaven.* When the chiefs of the stars transgress their order and alter their orbits (80:6), men err and worship the host of heaven — the very driving-away Moses forbade.$n$),
(4377,22576,$n$Jeremiah 8:2 — *And they shall spread them before the sun, and the moon, and all the host of heaven, whom they have loved, and whom they have served, and after whom they have walked, and whom they have sought, and whom they have worshipped: they shall not be gathered, nor be buried; they shall be for dung upon the face of the earth.* Jeremiah's idolaters loved and served the same sun, moon, and host that Enoch says men come to take for gods (80:7).$n$),
(4377,22575,$n$Romans 1:25 — *Who changed the truth of Elohim (God) into a lie, and worshipped and served the creature more than the Creator, who is blessed for ever. Amen.* Paul names the root of the error Enoch foretells — the order of the stars concealed from the sinners, who err and take them to be gods (80:7): the created luminary served in place of the Creator who appointed it.$n$),
(4380,22568,$n$Isaiah 24:4 — *The earth mourneth and fadeth away, the world languisheth and fadeth away, the haughty people of the earth do languish.* The earth's fruits held back in Enoch 80:3 are Isaiah's mourning, fading world languishing under inhabitants who broke the everlasting covenant.$n$),
(4382,22588,$n$Deuteronomy 6:7 — *And thou shalt teach them diligently unto thy children, and shalt talk of them when thou sittest in thine house, and when thou walkest by the way, and when thou liest down, and when thou risest up.* Enoch's charge to teach his children and record it for them and testify to all his children (81:6) is the Shema's command to teach the next generation diligently.$n$),
(4382,22587,$n$Deuteronomy 6:6 — *And these words, which I command thee this day, shall be in thine heart:* The words of truth Enoch writes for Methuselah to preserve (82:1) are the commanded words kept in the heart so they are not lost.$n$),
(4382,22586,$n$Proverbs 3:3 — *Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:* Enoch writes the wisdom down lest it be lost (82:1); the canon writes the same on the tablet of the heart.$n$),
(4383,22585,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The times and seasons were written into creation by the lights; in the days of the sinners all things on the earth alter and do not appear in their time (80:2) — the order violated, not rewritten by men.$n$),
(4383,22584,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* To alter the orbits and seasons prescribed (80:6) is the work of the horn who thinks to change times and laws.$n$),
(4383,22583,$n$Jubilees 6:34 — *And all the children of Yashar'el (Israel) will forget, and will not find the path of the years, and will forget the new moons, and seasons, and sabbaths, and they will go wrong as to all the order of the years.* Jubilees describes the identical drift Enoch foretells — men at fault, not reckoning the days accurately in the whole reckoning of the year (82:5) — forgetting the new moons, seasons and sabbaths of the 364-day order.$n$),
(4383,22582,$n$Jubilees 6:37 — *For this reason the years will come upon them when they will disturb (the order), and make an abominable (day) the day of testimony, and an unclean day a feast day, and they will confound all the days, the holy with the unclean, and the unclean day with the holy; for they will go wrong as to the months and sabbaths and feasts and jubilees. For this reason I command and testify to you that you may testify to them; for after your death your children will disturb (them), so that they will not make the year three hundred and sixty-four days only, and for this reason they will go wrong as to the new moons and seasons and sabbaths and festivals, and they will eat all kinds of blood with all kinds of flesh.* Jubilees names what Enoch foresaw — the chiefs of the stars transgressing their order and not appearing at the seasons prescribed (80:6) — and adds the result among men: going wrong as to new moons, seasons, sabbaths and festivals, and eating blood with all kinds of flesh.$n$),
(4384,22581,$n$Leviticus 23:2 — *Speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), and say unto them, Concerning the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my feasts.* Blessed are those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners in the reckoning of all their days (82:4) — to keep the count is to keep the feasts that are Yahuah's (the LORD's) own appointed times, fixed by the lights.$n$),
(4384,22578,$n$Psalm 1:1 — *Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.* Enoch's righteous who die on account of the deeds of men and are taken away because of the doings of the godless (81:9) are the blessed man of the two ways — the one who would not walk in the counsel of the ungodly, and paid for it.$n$),
(4385,22606,$n$Daniel 7:25 — *And he shall speak great words against the El Elyon (most High), and shall wear out the saints of the El Elyon (most High), and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.* Enoch's sinners from whom the order of the stars is concealed, who err about the times (80:7), are Daniel's horn that thinks to change times and laws.$n$),
(4385,22605,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The year completed in three hundred and sixty-four days, truly recorded for ever (82:6), is the Genesis decree of lights for days and years worked out in full.$n$),
(4385,22604,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The new moons and seasons men fail to reckon accurately (82:5) are appointed by the luminaries themselves.$n$),
(4385,22603,$n$Deuteronomy 4:19 — *And lest thou lift up thine eyes unto heaven, and when thou seest the sun, and the moon, and the stars, even all the host of heaven, shouldest be driven to worship them, and serve them, which Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath divided unto all nations under the whole heaven.* When the order of the lights is concealed from the sinners they err and take them to be gods (80:7) — the host-of-heaven idolatry Torah forbade.$n$),
(4386,22601,$n$Psalm 1:1 — *Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.* Enoch's *blessed are all those who walk in the way of righteousness and sin not as the sinners* (82:4) is the blessing of the man who does not walk in the way of sinners.$n$),
(4386,22600,$n$Psalm 1:2 — *But his delight is in the law of Yahuah (LORD); and in his law doth he meditate day and night.* The blessed walk in the way of righteousness and keep the reckoning of their days (82:4) because their delight is in his law.$n$),
(4386,22599,$n$Leviticus 23:4 — *These are the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), even holy convocations, which ye shall proclaim in their seasons.* Blessed are those who sin not as the sinners in the reckoning of all their days (82:4) — to keep the count right is to keep the appointed feasts in their seasons, as the lights ordain them.$n$),
(4387,22598,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The luminaries do not alter their courses because their Maker fixed them for signs and seasons from creation — the exact account Uriel showed Enoch (82:7).$n$),
(4387,22597,$n$Psalm 104:19 — *He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.* The seasons do not shift because the reckoning of the luminaries is exact and recorded (82:7); the moon and sun keep the courses they were appointed.$n$),
(4387,22596,$n$Jubilees 6:32 — *And command you the children of Yashar'el (Israel) that they observe the years according to this reckoning-three hundred and sixty-four days, and (these) will constitute a complete year, and they will not disturb its time from its days and from its feasts; for everything will fall out in them according to their testimony, and they will not leave out any day nor disturb any feasts...* The reckoning Enoch records as true for ever — the year completed in three hundred and sixty-four days (82:6) — is the same count Jubilees commands Israel to keep.$n$),
(4388,22595,$n$Leviticus 23:2 — *Speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel), and say unto them, Concerning the feasts of Yahuah (LORD), which ye shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my feasts.* The leaders who divide the four parts of the year and the months (82:11) mark the appointed feasts of Yahuah (LORD), proclaimed by the lights.$n$),
(4388,22594,$n$Genesis 1:14 — *And Elohim (God) said, Let there be lights in the firmament of the heaven to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs, and for seasons, and for days, and years:* The leaders who divide the parts of the year, the months and the days (82:11) keep the very signs and seasons set at creation.$n$),
(4388,22593,$n$Jubilees 6:17 — *For this reason it is ordained and written on the heavenly tables, that they should celebrate the feast of weeks in this month once a year, to renew the covenant every year...* The feasts governed by Enoch's leaders of the four parts of the year and the twelve orders of the months (82:11) are the heavenly-tablet appointments by which the covenant is renewed.$n$),
(4712,23820,$n$Genesis 6:11 — *The earth also was corrupt before Elohim (God), and the earth was filled with violence.* The violence that fills the earth is the corruption Enoch sees punished when the earth is swallowed in the abyss at 83:4.$n$),
(4712,23819,$n$Genesis 6:13 — *And Elohim (God) said unto Noah, The end of all flesh is come before me; for the earth is filled with violence through them; and, behold, I will destroy them with the earth.* The sin of the earth that sinks it into the abyss (83:7) is this very decree against all flesh.$n$),
(4712,23818,$n$Genesis 7:11 — *In the six hundredth year of Noah's life, in the second month, the seventeenth day of the month, the same day were all the fountains of the great deep broken up, and the windows of heaven were opened.* The broken-up deep is the great abyss that swallows the earth in Enoch's vision (83:4).$n$),
(4712,23817,$n$Genesis 7:23 — *And every living substance was destroyed which was upon the face of the ground, both man, and cattle, and the creeping things, and the fowl of the heaven; and they were destroyed from the earth: and Noah only remained alive, and they that were with him in the ark.* The earth destroyed with a great destruction for the sin of the earth (83:7) is the deluge that left only Noah's house alive.$n$),
(4713,23815,$n$Isaiah 34:4 — *And all the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a scroll: and all their host shall fall down, as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling fig from the fig tree.* Isaiah's unmaking on the Day of Yahuah (the LORD) — the host falling as leaves from the vine — is the unmaking Enoch dreamed: the earth swallowed in the abyss and the mountains hurled down (83:4).$n$),
(4713,23814,$n$Revelation 6:14 — *And the heaven departed as a scroll when it is rolled together; and every mountain and island were moved out of their places.* The sixth seal's mountains and islands moved out of their places is Enoch's dream — mountains suspended on mountains, hills sinking on hills, as the earth is swallowed in the abyss (83:4).$n$),
(4714,23808,$n$Amos 7:5 — *Then said I, O Yahuah (Lord) GOD, cease, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he is small.* The prophet's intercession for the small remnant echoes Enoch praying that the whole earth not be destroyed (83:8).$n$),
(4714,23807,$n$Amos 7:6 — *Yahuah (LORD) repented for this: This also shall not be, saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD).* Yahuah relents at the prophet's plea, the very answer Enoch's intercession seeks when he prays the earth be spared (83:8).$n$),
(4715,23806,$n$Matthew 24:37 — *But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be.* Yahusha (Jesus) makes the flood Mahalalel reads in Enoch's dream — the earth sinking into the abyss for the sin of the earth (83:7) — the type of the coming of the Son of Adam.$n$),
(4715,23805,$n$Matthew 24:39 — *And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of Adam be.* The flood that takes all away is the great destruction Mahalalel names over Enoch's dream — the earth sinking into the abyss (83:7) — made the figure of the last day.$n$),
(4715,23804,$n$Genesis 8:1 — *And Elohim (God) remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the cattle that was with him in the ark: and Elohim (God) made a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged.* The remembering of Noah is the answer to Enoch's prayer that the whole earth not be destroyed (83:8) — a seed preserved through the waters.$n$),
(4715,23803,$n$2 Peter 3:11 — *Seeing then that all these things shall be dissolved, what manner of persons ought ye to be in all holy conversation and godliness.* Peter turns the earth Enoch saw sink into the abyss and be destroyed with a great destruction (83:7) toward holy living, not toward law-as-curse.$n$),
(4732,23897,$n$Exodus 1:13 — *And the Egyptians made the children of Yashar'el (Israel) to serve with rigour:* The sheep given over to the wolves (89:13) is Israel made to serve Egypt with rigour.$n$),
(4732,23899,$n$Exodus 3:7 — *And Yahuah (LORD) said, I have surely seen the affliction of my people which are in Egypt, and have heard their cry by reason of their taskmasters; for I know their sorrows;* The Lord of the sheep who hears the sheep's cry (89:16) is Yahuah hearing Israel's cry in Egypt.$n$),
(4732,23900,$n$Exodus 3:8 — *And I am come down to deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians, and to bring them up out of that land unto a good land and a large, unto a land flowing with milk and honey...* The Lord of the sheep descending at the voice of the sheep from a lofty abode and pasturing them (89:16) is Yahuah (LORD) come down to deliver Israel.$n$),
(4733,23901,$n$Exodus 14:21 — *And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and Yahuah (LORD) caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided.* The wolves pursuing the sheep till they reached a sea of water (89:23) is Pharaoh's pursuit broken at the divided sea.$n$),
(4733,23902,$n$Exodus 14:28 — *And the waters returned, and covered the chariots, and the horsemen, and all the host of Pharaoh that came into the sea after them; there remained not so much as one of them.* The sea gathering itself together and rising till it covered the wolves (89:26) is the host of Pharaoh drowned in the returning sea.$n$),
(4733,23903,$n$Exodus 14:30 — *Thus Yahuah (LORD) saved Yashar'el (Israel) that day out of the hand of the Egyptians; and Yashar'el (Israel) saw the Egyptians dead upon the sea shore.* All the wolves who pursued the sheep perished and were drowned (89:27) — Yahuah (LORD) himself saved Israel out of Egypt's hand.$n$),
(4733,23904,$n$Exodus 19:4 — *Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles' wings, and brought you unto myself.* The Lord of the sheep coming down to the sheep that cried to him (89:16) is Yahuah (LORD) bearing Israel on eagles' wings to himself.$n$),
(4734,23905,$n$Exodus 19:18 — *And mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke, because Yahuah (LORD) descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.* The Lord of the sheep standing before them, great and terrible and majestic, so that all the sheep were afraid before his face (89:30), is Sinai, where Yahuah (LORD) descended in fire.$n$),
(4734,23906,$n$Exodus 19:6 — *And ye shall be unto me a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unto the children of Yashar'el (Israel).* The sheep placed in the great house built for the Lord of the sheep (89:36) is Israel made a kingdom of priests and holy nation at the covenant.$n$),
(4734,23907,$n$Exodus 24:8 — *And Moses took the blood, and sprinkled it on the people, and said, Behold the blood of the covenant, which Yahuah (LORD) hath made with you concerning all these words.* The sheep whose eyes began to open in the wilderness, pastured by the Lord of the sheep himself (89:28), are the people brought to the covenant he would seal with blood.$n$),
(4734,23908,$n$1 Kings 6:1 — *And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Yashar'el (Israel) were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon's reign over Yashar'el (Israel)... that he began to build the house of Yahuah (LORD).* The great house built for the Lord of the sheep (89:36) is fulfilled in the house of Yahuah, the temple.$n$),
(4735,23909,$n$2 Kings 17:6 — *In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria, and carried Yashar'el (Israel) away into Assyria, and placed them in Halah and in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.* The house and tower forsaken and the sheep given into the hand of the lions (89:56) is the northern house carried away into Assyria.$n$),
(4735,23910,$n$2 Kings 17:23 — *Until Yahuah (LORD) removed Yashar'el (Israel) out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Yashar'el (Israel) carried away out of their own land to Assyria unto this day.* The Lord of the sheep unmoved while the sheep are devoured and robbed (89:58) is Yahuah (LORD) removing Israel out of his sight for breaking the covenant.$n$),
(4735,23911,$n$Ezekiel 34:5 — *And they were scattered, because there is no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.* The wild beasts tearing the sheep in pieces (89:55) is Ezekiel's flock made meat to the beasts of the field.$n$),
(4735,23912,$n$Psalm 80:1 — *Give ear, O Shepherd of Yashar'el (Israel), thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest between the cherubims, shine forth.* Enoch crying to the Lord of the sheep that they were devoured by all the wild beasts (89:57) is the cry to the Shepherd of Israel to shine forth on Joseph's scattered flock.$n$),
(4736,23913,$n$Ezekiel 34:2 — *Son of Adam, prophesy against the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel)... Woe be to the shepherds of Yashar'el (Israel) that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?* The seventy shepherds judged and found guilty and cast into the fiery abyss (90:25) are Ezekiel's self-feeding shepherds of Israel.$n$),
(4736,23914,$n$Ezekiel 34:10 — *Behold, I am against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock... for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.* The judgment of the shepherds and their casting into the abyss (90:25) is Yahuah requiring His flock at the false shepherds' hand.$n$),
(4736,23915,$n$Jeremiah 23:1 — *Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds judged for not feeding the sheep (90:25) are Jeremiah's pastors who destroy and scatter the flock.$n$),
(4736,23916,$n$Zechariah 11:17 — *Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword shall be upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.* The shepherds cast into the fiery abyss (90:25) are Zechariah's worthless idol shepherd who abandons the flock of slaughter.$n$),
(4737,23917,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The throne erected and the sealed books opened before the Lord of the sheep (90:20) is Daniel's judgment set and the books opened.$n$),
(4737,23918,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The sealed books opened before the Lord of the sheep on his throne (90:20) is the white-throne judgment with the books opened.$n$),
(4737,23919,$n$Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar'el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all:* The new house gathering all the sheep (90:29) is the two houses made one nation under one king, the regathering.$n$),
(4737,23920,$n$Isaiah 11:12 — *And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Yashar'el (Israel), and gather together the dispersed of Yahudah (Judah) from the four corners of the earth.* The Lord bringing all the sheep into the new house (90:29) is the assembling of the outcasts of Israel and dispersed of Judah.$n$),
(4737,23921,$n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.* The new house greater and loftier than the first (90:29) is the New Jerusalem coming down from heaven.$n$),
(4737,23922,$n$Ezekiel 34:23 — *And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.* The white bull born with great horns whom all the beasts fear (90:37) is the one Shepherd, the Messiah, set over the regathered flock.$n$),
(4737,23923,$n$John 10:16 — *And other sheep I have, which are not of this fold: them also I must bring, and they shall hear my voice; and there shall be one fold, and one shepherd.* The white bull before whom all are transformed into white bulls (90:37-38) is the one Shepherd gathering the scattered into one fold.$n$),
(4738,23924,$n$1 Maccabees 2:1 — *In those days arose Mattathias the son of John, the son of Simeon, a priest of the sons of Joarib, from Jerusalem, and dwelt in Modin.* The great horn that cried to the sheep so that the rams ran to it (90:10) is read first against the Maccabean priest-line raised up to rally a scattered Israel.$n$),
(4738,23925,$n$1 Maccabees 2:66 — *As for Judas Maccabeus, he has been mighty and strong, even from his youth up: let him be your captain, and fight the battle of the people.* The great horn that sprouted on one of the sheep, whose eyes were opened (90:9), matches the mighty captain raised to fight the people's battle.$n$),
(4738,23926,$n$Jeremiah 23:5 — *Behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth.* The Lord of the sheep rejoicing over the great one with the black horns and over all the oxen (90:38) points beyond the Maccabees to the righteous Branch raised to David.$n$),
(4739,23927,$n$Ezekiel 34:23 — *And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.* The great horn raised on one of the sheep (90:9), with help sent to it from heaven (90:14), is the Lord's setting up of the one Davidic shepherd over the flock.$n$),
(4739,23929,$n$John 10:11 — *I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.* The Lord of the sheep rejoicing over the great one and over all the oxen (90:38) is the good shepherd who laid down his life for his own, now rejoicing over them.$n$),
(4740,23930,$n$Daniel 7:9 — *I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.* The throne erected in the pleasant land, the Lord of the sheep seated on it, and the sealed books opened before him (90:20) is the Ancient of days seated for judgment.$n$),
(4740,23931,$n$Daniel 7:10 — *A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.* The judgment held first over the stars, judged and found guilty and cast into the abyss of fire (90:24), is Daniel's set judgment with the books opened — the books of 90:20 opened and the sentence read.$n$),
(4740,23932,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The blinded sheep judged and found guilty and cast into the fiery abyss (90:26) is the white-throne judgment where the dead are judged by what is written in the books.$n$),
(4741,23933,$n$Jeremiah 23:1 — *Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds to whom the sheep were delivered for destruction, who trampled and devoured them (89:74), are the pastors woed for destroying and scattering the flock.$n$),
(4741,23934,$n$Jeremiah 23:2 — *Therefore thus saith Yahuah Elohim (the LORD God) of Yashar'el (Israel) against the pastors that feed my people; Ye have scattered my flock, and driven them away, and have not visited them: behold, I will visit upon you the evil of your doings, saith Yahuah (LORD).* The shepherds who trampled the sheep with their feet and devoured them (89:74) are visited for scattering and not visiting the flock.$n$),
(4741,23935,$n$Zechariah 11:17 — *Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword shall be upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.* The blinded shepherds who destroyed the sheep delivered to them (89:74) answer the woe on the idol shepherd who leaves the flock.$n$),
(4741,23936,$n$Revelation 20:10 — *And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.* The stars judged and found guilty and cast into an abyss full of fire and pillars of fire (90:24) are the deceiving powers consigned to the lake of fire.$n$),
(4742,23937,$n$Revelation 21:2 — *And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from Elohim (God) out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.* The new house, large and broad and very full (90:36), is the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from heaven.$n$),
(4743,23943,$n$Ezekiel 37:21 — *And say unto them, Thus saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD); Behold, I will take the children of Yashar'el (Israel) from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land:* All that had been destroyed and dispersed assembled in that house (90:33) is the regathering of scattered Israel from the heathen into their land.$n$),
(5110,25347,$n$Matthew 7:13 — *Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:* Yahusha's (Jesus's) broad road to destruction is Enoch's paths of violence and of death — revealed to a generation so that they hold themselves afar from them (94:2).$n$),
(5111,25345,$n$Psalm 49:6 — *They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;* the very posture Enoch condemns — trusting in riches instead of remembering the God of Spirits (94:8).$n$),
(5111,25344,$n$Psalm 49:7 — *None of them can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to Elohim (God) a ransom for him:* Riches cannot ransom a man — exactly what Enoch says the children of the earth will come to recognize: *their riches shall not be able to save them in the overthrow of their sins* (100:6).$n$),
(5111,25343,$n$Psalm 49:17 — *For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.* The rich man departs from his riches at death, just as Enoch warns 'from your riches shall you depart' (94:8).$n$),
(5111,25342,$n$Luke 12:20 — *But Elohim (God) said unto him, Thou fool, this night thy soul shall be required of thee: then whose shall those things be, which thou hast provided?* Yahusha's (Jesus's) rich fool meets the same reckoning Enoch announces on those who say *we have become rich with riches and have possessions* (97:8).$n$),
(5111,25341,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James pronounces Enoch's identical woe on the rich whose wealth will fail them (94:8).$n$),
(5112,25339,$n$Ecclesiasticus 11:19 — *Whereas he says, I have found rest, and now will eat continually of my goods; and yet he knoweth not what time shall come upon him, and that he must leave those things to others, and die.* Sirach mocks the hoarder's 'let us do what we purposed' plan with the very ignorance of his end that Enoch exposes (97:9).$n$),
(5113,25335,$n$Isaiah 5:8 — *Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!* Isaiah's woe on those who join house to house is Enoch's woe on those who build their houses with sin (94:7).$n$),
(5113,25334,$n$Isaiah 5:22 — *Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:* the mighty wine-drinkers Isaiah condemns are Enoch's who 'drink the finest wine, And tread upon the poor with your might' (96:5).$n$),
(5113,25331,$n$James 5:5 — *Ye have lived in pleasure on the earth, and been wanton; ye have nourished your hearts, as in a day of slaughter.* James condemns the same self-indulgent feasting on the backs of others that Enoch pronounces woe upon (96:5).$n$),
(5114,25367,$n$Isaiah 5:20 — *Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!* Isaiah's woe against inverting the moral order is Enoch's woe on those who pervert the words of uprightness and transgress the eternal law (99:2).$n$),
(5114,25366,$n$Isaiah 5:21 — *Woe unto them that are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!* — the self-wise who glory in their own lying are the godless of Enoch 99:1 who shall find no good.$n$),
(5115,25363,$n$Amos 6:7 — *Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the banquet of them that stretched themselves shall be removed.* — the banquet removed and the feasters led captive is the cutting-off of the rich oppressor's might in Enoch 95:7.$n$),
(5115,25361,$n$Jeremiah 17:11 — *As the partridge sitteth on eggs, and hatcheth them not; so he that getteth riches, and not by right, shall leave them in the midst of his days, and at his end shall be a fool.* — riches acquired in unrighteousness (Enoch 97:8) end in folly and loss.$n$),
(5118,25368,$n$Amos 5:11 — *Forasmuch therefore as your treading is upon the poor, and ye take from him burdens of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink wine of them.* The prophet's word for the very treading-and-feasting Enoch condemns in 96:5, and the houses the oppressors shall not keep.$n$),
(5118,25369,$n$Amos 5:12 — *For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate from their right.* The afflicting of the just stands behind Enoch's repeated charge that they tread upon the poor with their might (96:5).$n$),
(5118,25370,$n$Isaiah 3:14 — *Yahuah (LORD) will enter into judgment with the ancients of his people, and the princes thereof: for ye have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor is in your houses.* Those who devour the might of others and eat the best food (96:5) are the very princes who have eaten up the vineyard.$n$),
(5118,25371,$n$Isaiah 3:15 — *What mean ye that ye beat my people to pieces, and grind the faces of the poor? saith Adonai Yahuah (the Lord GOD) of hosts.* Grinding the faces of the poor is Isaiah's image for the trampling Enoch denounces in 96:5.$n$),
(5118,25372,$n$Proverbs 22:23 — *For Yahuah (LORD) will plead their cause, and spoil the soul of those that spoiled them.* Torah's guarantee that Yahuah avenges the oppressed poor is the ground of every woe Enoch pronounces in 96:4-8.$n$),
(5119,25373,$n$Luke 6:24 — *But woe unto you that are rich! for ye have received your consolation.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) woe on the rich is the sentence Enoch pronounces on the mighty who oppress the righteous with their might: *the day of your destruction is coming* (96:8).$n$),
(5119,25374,$n$Luke 6:25 — *Woe unto you that are full! for ye shall hunger. Woe unto you that laugh now! for ye shall mourn and weep.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) woe on the full is Enoch's woe on those who devour the finest of the wheat and drink wine in large bowls while treading the lowly under foot (96:5).$n$),
(5119,25375,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James opens his woe on the rich where Enoch does — the mighty who oppress the righteous, whose day of destruction is coming (96:8).$n$),
(5119,25376,$n$James 5:3 — *Your gold and silver is cankered; and the rust of them shall be a witness against you, and shall eat your flesh as it were fire. Ye have heaped treasure together for the last days.* The cankering of hoarded wealth is how James shows the day of destruction Enoch warns the mighty of (96:8).$n$),
(5119,25377,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:8 — *What has pride profited us? or what good has riches with our vaunting brought us?* Wisdom voices the doomed rich confessing the emptiness of their feasting — the finest of the wheat and the wine in large bowls Enoch's woe names (96:5).$n$),
(5120,25378,$n$Luke 12:18 — *And he said, This will I do: I will pull down my barns, and build greater; and there will I bestow all my fruits and my goods.* The rich fool's brimming barns are the very granaries Enoch's hoarders boast of in 97:9.$n$),
(5120,25379,$n$Luke 12:19 — *And I will say to my soul, Soul, thou hast much goods laid up for many years; take thine ease, eat, drink, and be merry.* The fool's self-talk matches the boast Enoch puts in the rich man's mouth — we have acquired everything we desired (97:8).$n$),
(5120,25381,$n$Amos 8:5 — *Saying, When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn? and the sabbath, that we may set forth wheat, making the ephah small, and the shekel great, and falsifying the balances by deceit?* Amos shows the rigged scales by which the gold of 97:8 was acquired in unrighteousness.$n$),
(5120,25382,$n$Amos 8:6 — *That we may buy the poor for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes; yea, and sell the refuse of the wheat?* The wheat hoarded in Enoch's full granaries (97:9) is the same refuse Amos says was sold by defrauding the needy.$n$),
(5121,25383,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The mighty who oppress the righteous with their might (96:8) are James's rich men whose withheld wages cry to Yahuah (Lord) of hosts.$n$),
(5121,25385,$n$Ecclesiasticus 34:22 — *He that takes away his neighbour's living slayeth him; and he that defraudeth the labourer of his hire is a bloodshedder.* Ben Sira makes defrauding the labourer a deed of blood — the oppression of the righteous by might that Enoch's woe names (96:8).$n$),
(5123,25403,$n$James 5:3 — *Your gold and silver is cankered; and the rust of them shall be a witness against you, and shall eat your flesh as it were fire. Ye have heaped treasure together for the last days.* The hoarded silver and gold of Enoch 97:8-8 becomes the very witness that eats the flesh of those who gathered it in unrighteousness.$n$),
(5123,25402,$n$Habakkuk 2:6 — *Shall not all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, Woe to him that increaseth that which is not his! how long? and to him that ladeth himself with thick clay!* Habakkuk's taunting woe against the man who increases what is not his is the same charge Enoch 97:9 lays on those who say 'let us do what we purposed.'$n$),
(5124,25397,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The poor trodden in Enoch 96:5 are James's defrauded reapers, whose cry has already entered the ears of Yahuah.$n$),
(5142,25478,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 — *But the souls of the righteous are in the hand of Yahuah (God), and there shall no torment touch them.* Wisdom's souls of the righteous in the hand of Elohim (God) are the souls Enoch tells not to fear, that have died in righteousness (102:4) — grieve not that the body went into Sheol; wait for the day.$n$),
(5142,25477,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:2 — *In the sight of the unwise they seemed to die: and their departure is taken for misery,* Wisdom's unwise who take the righteous death for misery are Enoch's sinners speaking over the righteous dead — *as we die, so die the righteous, and what benefit do they reap for their deeds?* (102:6). The world reads that death as defeat and cannot see the path that runs through it.$n$),
(5142,25476,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 3:4 — *For though they be punished in the sight of men, yet is their hope full of immortality.* The hope full of immortality is Enoch's word to the righteous dead: fear not, and be hopeful, ye that have died in righteousness (102:4) — punished in the world's eyes, kept whole before him.$n$),
(5142,25475,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *...and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* When he brings a grievous fire and there is nowhere to flee (102:1), Daniel's deliverance belongs to every one found written in the book — the deciding line is the name already written, election before any confession.$n$),
(5143,25474,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* Enoch's righteous who shall shine as the lights of heaven (104:2) are Daniel's resurrection-radiance of the wise.$n$),
(5143,25473,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The division made in Sheol between the spirits of the righteous and the rest (22:9) is Daniel's two-fold awakening — life for the one, shame for the other.$n$),
(5143,25472,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) own words for the harvest's end render Enoch's close: those born in darkness led into darkness, while the righteous shall be resplendent (108:14).$n$),
(5143,25471,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:3 — *And they repenting and groaning for anguish of spirit shall say within themselves, This was he, whom we had sometimes in derision, and a proverb of reproach:* The mockers who spoke over the righteous dead — *as we die, so die the righteous* (102:6) — seen now from the other side: the despisers confessing too late.$n$),
(5143,25470,$n$Wisdom of Solomon 5:5 — *How is he numbered among the children of Yahuah (God), and his lot is among the saints!* The righteous shining as the lights of heaven, seen at last with the portals of heaven opened to them (104:2), is this very cry — the despised found among the elect.$n$),
(5144,25467,$n$Amos 6:6 — *That drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments: but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph.* Enoch's drinkers of wine in large bowls (96:5) are Amos's feasters indifferent to the suffering of the people.$n$),
(5145,25463,$n$Malachi 4:2 — *But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.* The righteous in the light of the sun, the elect in the light of eternal life (58:3), meet the Sun of righteousness who rises for those who fear Yahuah's (the LORD's) name — the other end from the furnace.$n$),
(5146,25498,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The awakening Daniel sees is the very life Enoch swears the righteous spirits shall not lose (103:4).$n$),
(5146,25497,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* The spirits of the righteous dead that shall live and rejoice before the face of the Great One (103:4) are Daniel's wise, shining as the firmament.$n$),
(5146,25496,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) confirms what Enoch promises under oath: the spirits of those who died in righteousness shall live and rejoice and their memorial shall not perish (103:4) — the righteous shining in the Father's kingdom.$n$),
(5146,25495,$n$The Wisdom of Solomon 3:1 — *But the souls of the righteous are in the hand of Yahuah (God), and there shall no torment touch them.* The same safekeeping of the righteous spirits: they shall live and rejoice, and their memorial shall not perish from before the face of the Great One (103:4).$n$),
(5146,25494,$n$The Wisdom of Solomon 3:4 — *For though they be punished in the sight of men, yet is their hope full of immortality.* The hope full of immortality is the life Enoch swears the righteous dead shall have — their spirits shall live and rejoice and not perish (103:4).$n$),
(5147,25493,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The book of remembrance is the same heavenly register where Enoch sees goodness and glory written down for the spirits of those who died in righteousness (103:3).$n$),
(5147,25492,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* The sinners say their sins will not be searched out and written down; Enoch answers that they are written down every day (104:7). John's opened books are those records.$n$),
(5147,25491,$n$Revelation 14:13 — *And I heard a voice from heaven saying unto me, Write, Blessed are the dead which die in Yahusha (Lord) from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.* The blessing on the righteous dead — all goodness and joy and glory prepared and written down for the spirits of those who have died in righteousness (103:3).$n$),
(5148,25489,$n$Luke 16:23 — *And in hell he lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Abraham afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom.* The torment-side of Sheol is the darkness and chains and burning flame where Enoch says the sinners' spirits enter, where there is grievous judgment (103:8).$n$),
(5148,25488,$n$Luke 16:24 — *And he cried and said, Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water, and cool my tongue; for I am tormented in this flame.* The cry from the flame is the cry Enoch hears from the darkness and chains and burning flame where the sinners' spirits enter (103:8).$n$),
(5148,25487,$n$Revelation 20:15 — *And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.* The end of those whose names are blotted out of the book of life (108:3): their seed destroyed, their spirits slain, and the fire — the same end for the unwritten.$n$),
(5149,25485,$n$James 5:1 — *Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.* James opens the very woe Enoch pronounces on those who acquire silver and gold in unrighteousness and say they have everything they desired (97:8).$n$),
(5149,25484,$n$James 5:4 — *Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.* The cry the rulers would not hear — *cried out against those who devoured us, But they did not attend to our cries* (103:14) — is the cry James says has entered the ears of Yahuah (Lord) of sabaoth.$n$),
(5151,25515,$n$Daniel 12:2 — *And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.* The awakening of the dust-sleepers is the very resurrection Enoch promises the righteous in 104:2–5 — hope not cast away, joy as the angels (104:4).$n$),
(5151,25514,$n$Daniel 12:3 — *And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.* The great joy as the angels of heaven Enoch promises the righteous (104:4) is Daniel's wise shining as the firmament.$n$),
(5151,25513,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) seals Enoch's promise: the righteous shine in the Father's kingdom — great joy as the angels of heaven (104:4).$n$),
(5151,25512,$n$the Wisdom of Solomon 3:7 — *And in the time of their visitation they shall shine, and run to and fro like sparks among the stubble.* Wisdom's righteous shining at their visitation are Enoch's righteous who will not have to hide on the day of the great judgment and will not be found as sinners (104:5).$n$),
(5152,25511,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The book of remembrance is the same heavenly register where the names of the righteous are written before the glory of the Great One (104:1).$n$),
(5152,25510,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* Deliverance belongs to every one written in the book — Enoch's righteous whose names are written before the glory of the Great One (104:1).$n$),
(5152,25509,$n$Psalm 69:28 — *Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.* Enoch's righteous memorial shall NOT perish before the Great One (103:4); the wicked are blotted, never the elect written-in.$n$),
(5152,25508,$n$Revelation 3:5 — *He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.* Yahusha's (Jesus's) promise not to blot the overcomer's name is Enoch's memorial that shall not perish from before the face of the Great One (103:4).$n$),
(5153,25506,$n$Revelation 20:12 — *And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before Elohim (God); and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.* John's opened books are the records Enoch names: all your oppression written down every day till the day of your judgment (98:8).$n$),
(5153,25505,$n$Revelation 20:15 — *And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.* The fire that receives the unwritten is the darkness and chains and burning flame Enoch's sinners enter, where there is grievous judgment (103:8).$n$),
(5154,25504,$n$Isaiah 5:8 — *Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!* Isaiah's woe on the land-engrossers matches Enoch's woe on those who acquire gold and silver in unrighteousness (97:8).$n$),
(5156,25531,$n$Malachi 3:16 — *Then they that feared Yahuah (LORD) spake often one to another: and Yahuah (LORD) hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared Yahuah (LORD), and that thought upon his name.* The righteous whose memorial does not perish before the face of the Great One (103:4) are the ones in the book of remembrance kept for those who fear him.$n$),
(5156,25530,$n$Daniel 12:1 — *And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.* The memorial before the face of the Great One (103:4) is deliverance for every name already written in the book — election before the trouble, not after.$n$),
(5156,25529,$n$Matthew 13:42 — *And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.* The sinner's end — darkness and chains and a burning flame where there is grievous judgment (103:8) — is the canon's furnace into which the tares of the seed-war are gathered.$n$),
(5165,25553,$n$Matthew 13:43 — *Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.* Yahusha (Jesus) gives the righteous shining in their Father's kingdom; Enoch gives the children of the earth seeing the wise in security at last (100:6).$n$);
